// ts_print: the PROVISIONAL printer of the to-silica transpiler: one form of a session to Silica source text. It
// stands in for the passes of app design 6.2 (resolve, hints, lower, mechanics, print) until they exist.
//
// THE RULE IT FOLLOWS (contract 8.6, decided 2026-11-13): THE SENDER DECIDES EVERY TYPE. This printer infers no
// type and converts no value. A type is what the sender stated: a hint on the node (contract T8.5), a literal, a
// variable's binding, what an operator fixes, or what the node's place states (contract T8.9, the whole list).
// Where the contract requires a type (T8.10) and none is stated, or the stated types disagree (T8.11), the form
// is not printed and the answer carries a T31xx code (T8.13) with the construct, the node and its place.
// It sees one form at a time. What it is given from outside the form is `decls`: the session's declared types
// ((:type) forms, contract T8.14) and the session's context (the hello's lowering choices and the name of the unit
// being printed), which the transpile actor keeps and passes in. What needs the whole unit (the types of a unit's
// messages and process phases, which functions can run as a process) is left as marks in a form's text and
// spelled out by unit_rest when the unit is complete (see "processes" below).
//
// Source file: ts_print.silica.in; the $NAME$ placeholders are spelled out by silica-sink/tools/expand.py.
//
// EXPORTS
//   form_source(body, decls) -> { ok, stub, exports, text, sig, code, why, at: { file, line, column }, decl }
//     ok true               text is the function's Silica source; exports is its export line ("" when not exported).
//                           For a (:type) form text is a comment line and decl is its entry for decls.
//     ok false, stub true   text is a FAILING STUB with the function's name and signature, so its callers compile
//                           (contract T9.10); exports is its export line. The stub calls to_silica_gap (below).
//     ok false, stub false  nothing could be written; text and exports are "".
//     sig    "name/arity" for every function form and for an entry form (the entry function); "" otherwise.
//     code   "" when ok; "T4001" when the cause is the sender's own gap ((:gap, FormGap) or a (:gap_node));
//            "T4002" when the printer cannot print the construct; "T3101" a required type is not stated;
//            "T3102" operands of different types with no conversion; "T3103" inconsistent typing; "T3104" a
//            declared type that no earlier (:type) form declares (contract T8.13).
//     why    names the construct and its node ("... at node 7 ..."), and for T4001 carries the sender's construct
//            and note.
//     at     the form's head.file and the line and column of the node that stopped the printer (code.locations
//            through the node's `at`); of the function's first clause when ok or when no node is the cause; a type
//            form's at_line; a gap form's place. line 0: no place.
//     decl   for a (:type) form (also one that could not be written out), its entry for decls; "" otherwise.
//     code "T4004" with ok true: the form is written, and why is a warning about what was written (a process
//            function in which a message may be dropped where the source language keeps it; contract T9.13).
//   options_text(choices) -> string   the hello's lowering choices as the session's context holds them.
//   unit_rest(silica_unit, decls, exports, text, sigs, entry) -> string
//                                     everything of a unit's file after its `module` line: the exports, the helper
//                                     functions the text calls (to_silica_gap for a stub or a failing catch-all,
//                                     to_silica_i2f, to_silica_f2i, to_silica_round, to_silica_append_<type>), the
//                                     forms' texts and, for a unit with processes, the process runtime (the file
//                                     process_runtime.silica.tmpl). `main` is written when entry is a function of
//                                     the unit with no parameters that was written (sigs): for a unit with
//                                     processes from process_main.silica.tmpl (a failure reporter, the unit's
//                                     supervisor, the entry function as the first process); otherwise
//                                     `fn main() -> int64 { _: T <- entry(); 0 }`.
//   unit_notes(text, kind) -> string  what unit_rest found that concerns the whole unit, from its text: kind
//                                     "NOTE" (something that fails when it is reached: T4002, one gap), kind
//                                     "CHOICE" (lowering choices the process runtime does not follow: T2001).
//
// WHAT IS PRINTED
//   Functions whose signature carries a type hint (contract T8.10 a, node -1) that is a t_fun of printable types,
//   with at most eight parameters (Silica's limit). The hint is used as written, whatever its strength and policy:
//   there is no untyped representation, so no representation conversion (app design 6.3) is emitted. The session's
//   profile and lowering choices are not consulted.
//   Types: t_int, t_float; t_basic boolean, text (string) and symbol (atom); t_symbols (atom; its atoms `:a | :b`
//   when it is an alternative of a union); t_tuple; t_tagged `(:tag, A, B)`; t_record `{ a: A, b: B }`; t_union
//   `A | B` when every alternative is a t_symbols, a t_tagged, a t_record or a union of those (Silica refuses
//   other alternatives, see LIMITATIONS OBSERVED); t_fun `fn(A, B) -> R`; t_list `List[T, mem(normal)]`; t_actor
//   `actor_ref` (Silica's reference carries no message type); t_named, written out from decls with its arguments
//   in place of the declaration's parameters (Silica has no type names); t_var inside a declaration only.
//   Expressions: int (the int64 extremes included), float (digits.digits with an optional exponent), text (every
//   character: \n \t \r \\ \" and \xNN for other control bytes), symbol, boolean, variables, tuples, records built
//   inline and updated (every field is written out: the fields come from the record's type), field access, the
//   operators of contract Appendix B except the bitwise ones and `++` (`<>` is Silica's concat; to_float, trunc
//   and round are calls of helper functions), local calls, a call through a parameter of a function type, a local
//   function as a value (fun_ref), `case` on any printable expression, `cond`, blocks and matches (local
//   variables, tuple patterns), lists ([], [H | T], [A, B, C]), `++` for lists of int64, float64, boolean, string,
//   atom and process references, loop_hint (its body), and fail (PROVISIONAL: the failing expression of a
//   catch-all; the actor ends, the reason is not carried; in tail position of a process function with a symbol
//   reason the actor ends with that reason).
//   L1 (contract T9.16): (:sl_call) of a Silica print builtin, written as a call of the helper to_silica_b_<name>.
//   Process nodes (contract 9.4a; "processes" below): self, spawn of a function of the unit, send, receive in
//   tail position of its function, with guards and a timeout, and exit_signal with a symbol reason under a5_5
//   supervisor_request. A STATIC CHILD (contract T9.14b): (:register) of a (:spawn) with literal arguments is a
//   row of the child list the unit's supervisor has from its start, with the A4.4 override of the spawn as its
//   restart policy (the only override that is read); (:send_named) is a cast to a registered name (T9.14c).
//   Patterns, in clause heads, `case` and matches: variables, `_`, int, float, text, symbol and boolean literals
//   (negative numbers also as the operator neg on a literal), tuples of these, nested; [] and [H | T] with a
//   variable or `_` as H and T; a record pattern whose field patterns are variables or `_`, and an alias pattern
//   ((:match) in pattern position) of such patterns, where they are matched with a whole parameter, case subject
//   or match value (their variables are printed as subject.field).
//   Clauses become Silica `case` arms; a clause whose patterns are all variables or `_` is tested by its guard
//   alone (`case guard of { true -> ...; false -> ... }`). A function, `case` or `cond` whose last clause does not
//   match everything ends in a failing catch-all (contract H28): `{ _: int64 <- to_silica_gap(0); <a value> }`.
//   A guard is a Silica `if` guard when it uses a variable of its clause's patterns (Silica E2014 refuses any
//   other); otherwise it is tested inside the arm, and the clauses after it are printed a second time there.
//
// HOW NAMES AND TYPES ARE PRINTED
//   Parameters are p0, p1, ...; a variable bound by pattern node N is v<N>_; the subject of the case at node N,
//   when it must be named, is s<N>_; a list built at node N is l<N>_<k>_. A variable that is a whole parameter or
//   case subject is printed as that parameter or subject. A pattern variable that is not used is printed `_`
//   (Silica refuses an unused binding).
//   A Silica binding must state its type, and so must a catch-all arm and a statement whose value is dropped. The
//   type written is the one the sender stated (contract T8.9): expr answers it with every expression. Operators:
//   the two operands of an arithmetic or comparison operator must have one stated type (T8.11); an integer literal
//   takes the integer width of the other operand and a float literal its float width, nothing else adapts.
//
// NAMES (contract T9.11)
//   A function is printed under the sender's name; a name that is a Silica reserved word or builtin (an unqualified
//   call to a function named like a builtin is Silica error E2020) or `main` (Silica's entry point) is printed with
//   "__" appended, in its definition and in every call and reference (printed_name; the list is reserved_names
//   below, measured). A function whose name is not an identifier or starts with to_silica_ is NOT printed and gets
//   no stub (T4002); a call to such a name makes the caller a stub. A record field named like a reserved word is
//   not printed. A call or fun_ref whose module is the unit's own name is local.
//
// WHAT IS NOT PRINTED (T4002; the function becomes a stub when its signature is printable)
//   link, a spawn with link true, an exit_signal whose reason is not a symbol, a register of anything but a
//   spawn with literal arguments (contract T9.14b: a static child); a receive
//   that is not in tail position, a
//   receive clause whose message pattern is not a symbol or a tuple that starts with a symbol; a message that is
//   not one of those; a spawn of anything but a function of the unit; `try`; maps, bytes and binaries; lambdas
//   (a Silica function literal captures only integer literals), apply_mfa, a call to another module (the
//   contract gives it no meaning, T9.9); low-level (sl_) nodes other than an (:sl_call) of a Silica print
//   builtin (contract T9.16: print, println, print_int64, print_float64, print_boolean, atom_name); a record pattern with a field pattern that is
//   not a variable or `_`, or inside another pattern; list patterns of a fixed length or with a pattern inside; the types char, bytes and dynamic, a t_var in a signature, a declared
//   type that names itself; a function with such a type in its signature gets NO stub, because a stub needs the
//   signature, and neither does a function whose result type has no value this printer can write (a function
//   type, actor_ref). A function that receives needs no printable result type (a process's value goes to
//   nobody). An entry form answers ok false with sig set: unit_rest writes main.
//   NOT CHECKED HERE: a printed function that calls a function which could not be written (no stub) names a
//   function that does not exist; the types of a call's arguments against the callee's signature (the printer
//   does not know the callee; the Silica compiler does); a hint on a pattern variable that differs from the type
//   of what it is matched with.
//
// LIMITATIONS OBSERVED (Silica compilers 999919 and 999916, 2026-11-13), which shape the output
//   - A binding must state its type and an unused binding is an error (E1055).
//   - A guard must use a binding of its own pattern (E2014).
//   - An inline sum accepts atom literals, tagged tuples and records as alternatives; `int64 | :timeout` and
//     `(int64, int64) | :x` are refused (E2003), and `atom` as an alternative was not parsed (E1069).
//   - A value bound as `x: (atom, int64) <- (:tag, n)` is not accepted where `(:tag, int64) | ...` is expected
//     (E2003): a tagged tuple that is first bound to a variable and then returned as a union does not compile.
//   - A catch-all arm must be last (E2008); a redundant catch-all after `true` and `false`, or after the arms of
//     every alternative of a sum, is accepted.
//   - Silica has no record-update syntax, and no expression that fails outside a behaviour: the failing stub and
//     catch-all divide by zero in a helper (`1 / n` with n 0), which ends the actor with `badarith`.
//   - No builtin converts an integer to a float or a float to an integer: the conversions are helper functions.
//   - A list is built only inside a `sequence proc[mem(normal)]`, and a sequence cannot be a case arm (E1057):
//     every list expression is a sequence in a block.
//   - A `{ sequence ... }` block that stands directly as an argument of a call compiles and faults when the
//     program runs; bound to a name first it does not. A list argument and the operands of `++` are bound.
//   - Processes: the notes are with the code ("processes") and in process_runtime.silica.tmpl.
module ts_print;

use ts_text;

export form_source/2;
export node_text/1;
export atom_manifest/1;
export options_text/1;
export unit_rest/6;
export unit_notes/2;

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ what could not be printed

// A construct that cannot be printed is written into the text as a mark: \x01 construct \x02 node \x02 code \x02
// note \x03. No printed text can hold these bytes (literals are escaped), so a text with \x01 in it is not Silica,
// and the first mark says what stopped the printer. code is "T4001" (the sender sent a gap) or "T4002".
fn gap(construct: string, node: int64, code: string, note: string) -> string {
    concat(ts_text@concat4("\x01", construct, "\x02", ts_text@itoa(node)), concat(ts_text@concat4("\x02", code, "\x02", note), "\x03"))
}

fn bad(s: string) -> boolean {
    contains(s, "\x01")
}

fn no(construct: string, node: int64, note: string) -> $EX$ {
    { text: gap(construct, node, "T4002", note), type: "" }
}

// A type the contract requires and the sender did not state (contract T8.10, letter a to e; code T3101).
fn miss(what: string, node: int64, letter: string) -> $EX$ {
    { text: gap(what, node, "T3101", ts_text@concat3("no type is stated for it (contract T8.10 ", letter, "): the sender must state it with a hint; the transpiler infers no type")), type: "" }
}

// Typing the sender sent that does not agree with itself (code T3103).
fn clash(what: string, node: int64, note: string) -> $EX$ {
    { text: gap(what, node, "T3103", note), type: "" }
}

// The mark of a type text, moved to node i (a type's own mark names no node).
fn at_node(mark: string, i: int64) -> string {
    g: $STOPPED$ <- first_gap(mark);
    gap(g.construct, i, g.code, g.note)
}

// The hole a failing catch-all leaves for the value of its type (filled by finish).
fn hole() -> string {
    "\x04"
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ tables

fn node_at(ns: $NODES$, i: int64) -> $NODE$ {
    case ns of {
        []: $NODES$ -> (:wild, 0 - 1);
        [n: $NODE$, t: $NODES$] -> case i == 0 of {
            true -> n;
            false -> node_at(t, i - 1)
        }
    }
}

fn type_at(ts: $TYPES$, i: int64) -> $TYPENODE$ {
    case ts of {
        []: $TYPES$ -> (:t_basic, :dynamic);
        [x: $TYPENODE$, t: $TYPES$] -> case i == 0 of {
            true -> x;
            false -> type_at(t, i - 1)
        }
    }
}

// The (line, column) of location index i, or (0, 0).
fn location_at(ls: $LII$, i: int64) -> (int64, int64) {
    case ls of {
        []: $LII$ -> (0, 0);
        [x: (int64, int64), t: $LII$] -> case i == 0 of {
            true -> x;
            false -> location_at(t, i - 1)
        }
    }
}

fn count(xs: $LI$, acc: int64) -> int64 {
    case xs of {
        []: $LI$ -> acc;
        [_x: int64, t: $LI$] -> count(t, acc + 1)
    }
}

fn count_s(xs: $LS$, acc: int64) -> int64 {
    case xs of {
        []: $LS$ -> acc;
        [_x: string, t: $LS$] -> count_s(t, acc + 1)
    }
}

fn count_ss(xs: $LSS$, acc: int64) -> int64 {
    case xs of {
        []: $LSS$ -> acc;
        [_x: (string, string), t: $LSS$] -> count_ss(t, acc + 1)
    }
}

// Element i of xs, or "".
fn nth_s(xs: $LS$, i: int64) -> string {
    case xs of {
        []: $LS$ -> "";
        [x: string, t: $LS$] -> case i == 0 of {
            true -> x;
            false -> nth_s(t, i - 1)
        }
    }
}

fn first_of(xs: $LI$) -> int64 {
    case xs of {
        []: $LI$ -> 0 - 1;
        [x: int64, _t: $LI$] -> x
    }
}

fn second_of(xs: $LI$) -> int64 {
    case xs of {
        []: $LI$ -> 0 - 1;
        [_x: int64, t: $LI$] -> first_of(t)
    }
}

// The value of key in a list of (key, value) pairs, or "".
fn lookup(pairs: $LSS$, key: string) -> string {
    case pairs of {
        []: $LSS$ -> "";
        [p: (string, string), t: $LSS$] -> {
            (k: string, v: string) <- p;
            case k == key of {
                true -> v;
                false -> lookup(t, key)
            }
        }
    }
}

fn none_of() -> $LS$ {
    sequence proc[mem(normal)]
        out: $LS$ <- empty[string, mem(normal)]()
    produces
        pure out
    end
}

fn none_i() -> $LI$ {
    sequence proc[mem(normal)]
        out: $LI$ <- empty[int64, mem(normal)]()
    produces
        pure out
    end
}

fn cons_s(s: string, t: $LS$) -> $LS$ {
    sequence proc[mem(normal)]
        out: $LS$ <- prepend[string, mem(normal)](s, t)
    produces
        pure out
    end
}

fn no_pairs() -> $LSS$ {
    sequence proc[mem(normal)]
        out: $LSS$ <- empty[(string, string), mem(normal)]()
    produces
        pure out
    end
}

fn pair_on(a: string, b: string, t: $LSS$) -> $LSS$ {
    sequence proc[mem(normal)]
        out: $LSS$ <- prepend[(string, string), mem(normal)]((a, b), t)
    produces
        pure out
    end
}

// The environment: what each source variable in scope is printed as, and its Silica type ("" when not known).
fn no_bindings() -> $ENV$ {
    sequence proc[mem(normal)]
        out: $ENV$ <- empty[(string, string, string), mem(normal)]()
    produces
        pure out
    end
}

fn bind(env: $ENV$, name: string, text: string, ty: string) -> $ENV$ {
    sequence proc[mem(normal)]
        out: $ENV$ <- prepend[(string, string, string), mem(normal)]((name, text, ty), env)
    produces
        pure out
    end
}

fn find(env: $ENV$, name: string) -> $EX$ {
    case env of {
        []: $ENV$ -> { text: "", type: "" };
        [b: (string, string, string), t: $ENV$] -> {
            (k: string, x: string, ty: string) <- b;
            case k == name of {
                true -> { text: x, type: ty };
                false -> find(t, name)
            }
        }
    }
}

// Contract Appendix B operator -> Silica operator, for the binary operators this printer covers.
fn binary_operators() -> $LSS$ {
    sequence proc[mem(normal)]
        out: $LSS$ <- [("+", "+"), ("-", "-"), ("*", "*"), ("div", "/"), ("rem", "%"), ("/", "/"),
                       ("==", "=="), ("/=", "!="), ("<", "<"), ("=<", "<="), (">", ">"), (">=", ">="),
                       ("=:=", "=="), ("=/=", "!="),
                       ("and", "and"), ("andalso", "and"), ("or", "or"), ("orelse", "or")]
    produces
        pure out
    end
}

fn is_arithmetic(op: string) -> boolean {
    op == "+" or op == "-" or op == "*" or op == "div" or op == "rem" or op == "/"
}

// The names a printed function cannot have and a printed call cannot name: Silica's reserved words, its builtins
// (an unqualified call to a function named like a builtin is Silica error E2020), `main` (Silica's entry point) and
// this printer's own helper. Measured with compiler 999919 on 2026-11-13: each name was tried as a function that is
// defined and called. How such names are to be mangled is not decided, so nothing is mangled here.
fn reserved_names() -> string {
        " actor actor_carrier_index actor_id actor_ref actor_ref_bits actor_ref_equal actor_ref_not_equal actor_ref_of_word add_child alloc_buf alloc_buf_retained alloc_rec alloc_ref alloc_region alloc_region_on_numa_node and append_file atom atom_bits atom_index_of_name atom_name atom_of_bits band bnot bool boolean bor buf_load buf_store build byte_at byte_slice bytes Bytes bytes_of c_wrapper call call_registered call_supervisor cancel_timer carried_on case cast cast_dangerous_registered cast_device cast_device_registered cast_exit cast_registered char char_code char_of_code checked_int64_add checked_int64_add1 checked_int64_byte_size checked_int64_mul child_table_first_ref child_table_row_ref compact_state comparator_result_valid comparator_result_validate concat concatenate concurrency contains core_id core_set current_time dangerous_actor_ref decode delete_file demonitor device device_actor_ref device_io effect efficiency_cores empty encode end ends_with export external_danger fail_self failure_agent_type failure_reason failure_reason_atom failure_reason_tag failure_release false file_exists float16 float16_inf float16_is_finite float16_is_inf float16_is_nan float16_nan float16_neg_inf float16_to_float32 float32 float32_bits float32_inf float32_is_finite float32_is_inf float32_is_nan float32_nan float32_neg_inf float32_of_bits float32_to_float16 float32_to_float64 float64 float64_bits float64_inf float64_is_finite float64_is_inf float64_is_nan float64_nan float64_neg_inf float64_of_bits float64_to_float32 fn for foreign fresh_lifetime get_actor_memory_usage get_core_capabilities get_cpu_topology get_efficiency_cores get_performance_cores get_pid_registry get_registry_actor head if impl int16 int32 int64 int8 join_bytes kill_abnormal length length_bytes length_chars lifetime link List list_at list_nth mailbox main map_device mem meta migrate_actor module monitor monitor_ref monotonic_time move negate_float16 negate_float32 negate_float64 negate_int16 negate_int32 negate_int64 negate_int8 negate_unit normal normal_noncacheable normal_writeback normal_writethrough not of or ordering_identity_bundle_make ordering_identity_fresh_env ordering_identity_materialize ordering_identity_same peek performance_cores pin_actor_realtime pin_actor_to_core pin_actor_to_efficiency_core pin_actor_to_numa_node pin_actor_to_performance_core pin_mode pin_pull pin_read pin_write poke prepend print print_atom print_boolean print_char print_float16 print_float32 print_float64 print_int16 print_int32 print_int64 print_int8 print_string print_string_stderr print_uint16 print_uint32 print_uint64 print_uint8 println println_stderr proc produces provided pure read_buf read_lines read_ref rec recreate recv ref_eq register_actor register_failure_reporter remove_actor remove_head required retire return self send send_after sequence set_actor_priority set_scheduler_policy shl shr spawn spawn_dangerous spawn_dangerous_registered spawn_device spawn_device_registered spawn_linked spawn_registered spawn_registered_supervisor stack_policy start_child starts_with state_area_bytes state_policy stop_self string String struct substring substring_until_char supervision_ingress_enqueue supervision_wait_and_drain_one supervisor_ref timer_ref to_int16 to_int32 to_int64 to_int8 to_silica_gap to_uint16 to_uint32 to_uint64 to_uint8 trait true uint16 uint32 uint64 uint8 unit unpin_actor use wait_for_exit wrapper_meta write_buf write_ref "
}

// True when name can be printed as a Silica function name.
fn usable_name(name: string) -> boolean {
    case ts_text@is_identifier(name) of {
        true -> not contains(reserved_names(), ts_text@concat3(" ", name, " ")) and not starts_with(name, "to_silica_");
        false -> false
    }
}

// The kind of a node (its tag) and its `at` (the index of its location), for diagnostics.
fn node_info(n: $NODE$) -> (string, int64) {
    case n of {
        (:int, a: int64, _x1: int64) -> ("int", a);
        (:float, a: int64, _x1: string) -> ("float", a);
        (:text, a: int64, _x1: string) -> ("text", a);
        (:bytes, a: int64, _x1: string) -> ("bytes", a);
        (:symbol, a: int64, _x1: string) -> ("symbol", a);
        (:boolean, a: int64, _x1: boolean) -> ("boolean", a);
        (:nil, a: int64) -> ("nil", a);
        (:tuple, a: int64, _x1: $LI$) -> ("tuple", a);
        (:cons, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: int64) -> ("cons", a);
        (:list, a: int64, _x1: $LI$, _x2: int64) -> ("list", a);
        (:map, a: int64, _x1: $LII$, _x2: int64) -> ("map", a);
        (:record, a: int64, _x1: string, _x2: $LSI$, _x3: int64) -> ("record", a);
        (:field, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: string) -> ("field", a);
        (:bits, a: int64, _x1: $LI$) -> ("bits", a);
        (:var, a: int64, _x1: string) -> ("var", a);
        (:wild, a: int64) -> ("wild", a);
        (:match, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: int64) -> ("match", a);
        (:block, a: int64, _x1: $LI$) -> ("block", a);
        (:case, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: $LI$) -> ("case", a);
        (:clause, a: int64, _x1: $LI$, _x2: int64, _x3: int64) -> ("clause", a);
        (:cond, a: int64, _x1: $LI$) -> ("cond", a);
        (:op, a: int64, _x1: string, _x2: $LI$) -> ("op", a);
        (:call, a: int64, _x1: string, _x2: string, _x3: $LI$) -> ("call", a);
        (:apply, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: $LI$) -> ("apply", a);
        (:apply_mfa, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: int64, _x3: $LI$) -> ("apply_mfa", a);
        (:fun_ref, a: int64, _x1: string, _x2: string, _x3: int64) -> ("fun_ref", a);
        (:lambda, a: int64, _x1: $LI$) -> ("lambda", a);
        (:loop_hint, a: int64, _x1: int64) -> ("loop_hint", a);
        (:self, a: int64) -> ("self", a);
        (:spawn, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: $LI$, _x3: boolean) -> ("spawn", a);
        (:send, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: int64) -> ("send", a);
        (:receive, a: int64, _x1: $LI$, _x2: int64, _x3: int64) -> ("receive", a);
        (:link, a: int64, _x1: int64) -> ("link", a);
        (:exit_signal, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: int64) -> ("exit_signal", a);
        (:fail, a: int64, _x1: int64) -> ("fail", a);
        (:try, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: $LI$, _x3: $LI$, _x4: int64) -> ("try", a);
        (:register, a: int64, _x1: string, _x2: int64) -> ("register", a);
        (:send_named, a: int64, _x1: string, _x2: int64) -> ("send_named", a);
        (:gap_node, a: int64, _x1: string, _x2: string) -> ("gap_node", a);
        (:sl_call, a: int64, _x1: string, _x2: string, _x3: $LI$) -> ("sl_call", a);
        (:sl_cast, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: int64) -> ("sl_cast", a);
        (:sl_spawn_child, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: string, _x3: string, _x4: int64, _x5: $SPAWNPOL$) -> ("sl_spawn_child", a);
        (:sl_fail_self, a: int64, _x1: int64) -> ("sl_fail_self", a);
        (:sl_stop_self, a: int64) -> ("sl_stop_self", a);
        (:sl_phase, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: $LI$, _x3: string) -> ("sl_phase", a);
        (:sl_yield, a: int64, _x1: string, _x2: $LI$) -> ("sl_yield", a);
        (:sl_behaviour, a: int64, _x1: int64, _x2: int64, _x3: int64) -> ("sl_behaviour", a);
        _: $NODE$ -> ("segment", 0 - 1)
    }
}

fn kind_note(kind: string) -> string {
    case kind == "self" or kind == "spawn" or kind == "send" or kind == "receive" or kind == "link" or kind == "exit_signal" or kind == "fail" or kind == "register" or kind == "send_named" of {
        true -> case kind == "link" of {
            true -> "a link has no lowering: BEES A5.5 supervisor_request sends only exit requests to a supervisor, and silica_link is not built (Silica admits link only directly in a behaviour, and what a linked actor receives when its partner ends is not written)";
            false -> case kind == "exit_signal" of {
                true -> "an exit request is printed by exit_ex";
                false -> case kind == "receive" of {
                    true -> "a receive is printed only in tail position of its function (with each clause the function ends or goes on in a function); here code of the same function runs after it. THE SENDER MUST SPLIT THE FUNCTION AT THIS RECEIVE (contract T9.13a): send the code after it as a function of its own whose parameters are the variables that are live there and the receive's value, and end each clause of the receive with a tail call of that function. What runs before and after a receive is the source language's business; the transpiler splits nothing";
                    false -> "a (:register) and a (:send_named) are printed by register_ex and send_named_ex"
                }
            }
        };
        false -> case kind == "map" or kind == "bits" or kind == "bytes" of {
            true -> "maps, binaries and byte strings are not printed yet";
            false -> case kind == "lambda" of {
                true -> "closures are not printed yet: a Silica function literal captures only integer literals (limitation observed), so a closure needs a lowering (app design 5)";
                false -> case starts_with(kind, "sl_") of {
                    true -> "of the low-level nodes only (:sl_call) of a Silica print builtin is printed (contract T9.16)";
                    false -> "the printer does not cover this node kind yet"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// "(:kind)" for node i, for diagnostics.
fn node_label(c: $CTX$, i: int64) -> string {
    (kind: string, _at: int64) <- node_info(node_at(c.ns, i));
    ts_text@concat3("(:", kind, ")")
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ type texts

fn byte_in(s: string, i: int64) -> int64 {
    sequence proc[transport]
        b: int64 <- byte_at(s, i)
    produces
        pure b
    end
}

fn trim(s: string) -> string {
    n: int64 <- length_bytes(s);
    case n == 0 of {
        true -> s;
        false -> case byte_in(s, 0) == 32 of {
            true -> trim(substring(s, 1, n));
            false -> case byte_in(s, n - 1) == 32 of {
                true -> trim(substring(s, 0, n - 1));
                false -> s
            }
        }
    }
}

fn depth_step(b: int64) -> int64 {
    case b == 40 or b == 123 or b == 91 of {
        true -> 1;
        false -> case b == 41 or b == 125 or b == 93 of {
            true -> 0 - 1;
            false -> 0
        }
    }
}

fn split_from(s: string, i: int64, start: int64, depth: int64, sep: int64, n: int64) -> $LS$ {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> cons_s(trim(substring(s, start, n)), none_of());
        false -> {
            b: int64 <- byte_in(s, i);
            case b == sep and depth == 0 of {
                true -> cons_s(trim(substring(s, start, i)), split_from(s, i + 1, i + 1, 0, sep, n));
                false -> split_from(s, i + 1, start, depth + depth_step(b), sep, n)
            }
        }
    }
}

// A type text (always ASCII: names in it are identifiers) cut at the separator byte sep outside any brackets.
fn split_top(s: string, sep: int64) -> $LS$ {
    split_from(s, 0, 0, 0, sep, length_bytes(s))
}

// What is inside the outer brackets of t when t is one bracketed type opened by the byte open, or "".
fn inside(t: string, open: int64) -> string {
    n: int64 <- length_bytes(t);
    case n < 2 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> case byte_in(t, 0) == open and count_s(split_top(t, 124), 0) == 1 of {
            true -> substring(t, 1, n - 1);
            false -> ""
        }
    }
}

// The element types of the tuple type t, or no elements when t is not one tuple type.
fn tuple_elems(t: string) -> $LS$ {
    inner: string <- inside(t, 40);
    case length_bytes(inner) == 0 of {
        true -> none_of();
        false -> split_top(inner, 44)
    }
}

// The "name: type" entries of the record type t, or none.
fn record_entries(t: string) -> $LS$ {
    inner: string <- inside(t, 123);
    case length_bytes(inner) == 0 of {
        true -> none_of();
        false -> split_top(inner, 44)
    }
}

fn entry_type(entries: $LS$, name: string) -> string {
    case entries of {
        []: $LS$ -> "";
        [e: string, t: $LS$] -> case starts_with(e, concat(name, ":")) of {
            true -> trim(substring(e, length_bytes(name) + 1, length_bytes(e)));
            false -> entry_type(t, name)
        }
    }
}

fn entry_name(e: string) -> string {
    substring_until_char(e, 0, ':')
}

fn tag_fits(first: string, tag: string) -> boolean {
    case starts_with(first, ":") and length_bytes(tag) > 0 of {
        true -> first == tag;
        false -> true
    }
}

fn pick(alts: $LS$, arity: int64, tag: string) -> $LS$ {
    case alts of {
        []: $LS$ -> none_of();
        [a: string, rest: $LS$] -> {
            el: $LS$ <- tuple_elems(a);
            case count_s(el, 0) == arity and tag_fits(nth_s(el, 0), tag) of {
                true -> el;
                false -> pick(rest, arity, tag)
            }
        }
    }
}

// The result type of the function type t ("fn(A, B) -> R"), or "".
fn fn_result(t: string) -> string {
    case starts_with(t, "fn(") of {
        true -> fn_result_from(t, 3, 1, length_bytes(t));
        false -> ""
    }
}

fn fn_result_from(t: string, i: int64, depth: int64, n: int64) -> string {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            d: int64 <- depth + depth_step(byte_in(t, i));
            case d == 0 of {
                true -> case i + 5 < n of {
                    true -> substring(t, i + 5, n);
                    false -> ""
                };
                false -> fn_result_from(t, i + 1, d, n)
            }
        }
    }
}

fn or_type(a: string, b: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(a) == 0 of {
        true -> b;
        false -> a
    }
}

fn is_list(t: string) -> boolean {
    starts_with(t, "List[") and ends_with(t, ", mem(normal)]")
}

// The element type of the list type t, or "".
fn list_elem(t: string) -> string {
    case is_list(t) of {
        true -> substring(t, 5, length_bytes(t) - 14);
        false -> ""
    }
}

fn is_int_type(t: string) -> boolean {
    starts_with(t, "int") or starts_with(t, "uint")
}

fn is_float_type(t: string) -> boolean {
    starts_with(t, "float")
}

// The types the transpiler compares when it checks that the sender's typing agrees with itself.
fn scalar(t: string) -> boolean {
    is_int_type(t) or is_float_type(t) or t == "boolean" or t == "string"
}

// A list expression: Silica builds a list only inside a sequence, and a sequence stands in a block.
fn list_block(i: int64, k: int64, lt: string, rhs: string) -> string {
    name: string <- concat(ts_text@concat4("l", ts_text@itoa(i), "_", ts_text@itoa(k)), "_");
    concat(ts_text@concat4("{ sequence proc[mem(normal)] ", name, ": ", lt), ts_text@concat4(" <- ", rhs, " produces pure ", concat(name, " end }")))
}

fn defaults(ts: $LS$, acc: string) -> string {
    case ts of {
        []: $LS$ -> acc;
        [t: string, rest: $LS$] -> {
            d: string <- default_value(t);
            case length_bytes(d) == 0 of {
                true -> "";
                false -> case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
                    true -> defaults(rest, d);
                    false -> defaults(rest, ts_text@concat3(acc, ", ", d))
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn entry_defaults(es: $LS$, acc: string) -> string {
    case es of {
        []: $LS$ -> acc;
        [e: string, rest: $LS$] -> {
            name: string <- entry_name(e);
            d: string <- default_value(trim(substring(e, length_bytes(name) + 1, length_bytes(e))));
            item: string <- ts_text@concat3(name, ": ", d);
            case length_bytes(d) == 0 of {
                true -> "";
                false -> case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
                    true -> entry_defaults(rest, item);
                    false -> entry_defaults(rest, ts_text@concat3(acc, ", ", item))
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn first_default(alts: $LS$) -> string {
    case alts of {
        []: $LS$ -> "";
        [a: string, rest: $LS$] -> {
            d: string <- default_value(a);
            case length_bytes(d) == 0 of {
                true -> first_default(rest);
                false -> d
            }
        }
    }
}

// A value of the Silica type t, for the line after a failing call (it is never reached), or "" when this printer
// can write none (function types).
fn default_value(t: string) -> string {
    case t == smode() of {
        true -> done_state();
        false -> plain_default(t)
    }
}

fn plain_default(t: string) -> string {
    case starts_with(t, "int") or starts_with(t, "uint") of {
        true -> "0";
        false -> case starts_with(t, "float") of {
            true -> "0.0";
            false -> case t == "boolean" of {
                true -> "false";
                false -> case t == "string" of {
                    true -> "\"\"";
                    false -> case t == "atom" of {
                        true -> ":gap";
                        false -> case is_list(t) of {
                            true -> list_block(0, 0, t, ts_text@concat3("empty[", list_elem(t), ", mem(normal)]()"));
                            false -> structured_default(t)
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn structured_default(t: string) -> string {
    alts: $LS$ <- split_top(t, 124);
    case count_s(alts, 0) > 1 of {
        true -> first_default(alts);
        false -> case starts_with(t, ":") of {
            true -> t;
            false -> case starts_with(t, "(") of {
                true -> {
                    ds: string <- defaults(tuple_elems(t), "");
                    case length_bytes(ds) == 0 of {
                        true -> "";
                        false -> ts_text@concat3("(", ds, ")")
                    }
                };
                false -> case starts_with(t, "{") of {
                    true -> {
                        es: string <- entry_defaults(record_entries(t), "");
                        case length_bytes(es) == 0 of {
                            true -> "";
                            false -> ts_text@concat3("{ ", es, " }")
                        }
                    };
                    false -> ""
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ types (contract 8.5)

fn int_type(w: :i8 | :i16 | :i32 | :i64 | :u8 | :u16 | :u32 | :u64) -> string {
    case w of {
        :i8 -> "int8";
        :i16 -> "int16";
        :i32 -> "int32";
        :i64 -> "int64";
        :u8 -> "uint8";
        :u16 -> "uint16";
        :u32 -> "uint32";
        :u64 -> "uint64"
    }
}

fn float_type(w: :f32 | :f64) -> string {
    case w of {
        :f32 -> "float32";
        :f64 -> "float64"
    }
}

fn type_gap(construct: string, note: string) -> string {
    gap(construct, 0 - 1, "T4002", note)
}

fn basic_type(kind: :boolean | :char | :text | :bytes | :symbol | :dynamic) -> string {
    case kind of {
        :boolean -> "boolean";
        :text -> "string";
        :symbol -> "atom";
        :char -> type_gap("the type char", "characters are not printed yet");
        // PROVISIONAL: a byte string is a Silica string (contract 8.5 says so for :silica; the profile is not consulted).
        :bytes -> "string";
        :dynamic -> type_gap("the type dynamic", "there is no untyped representation yet")
    }
}

// ":a | :b" for the names, or a mark.
fn atoms_type(names: $LS$, acc: string) -> string {
    case names of {
        []: $LS$ -> case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
            true -> type_gap("a symbol type with no symbols", "nothing to print");
            false -> acc
        };
        [n: string, t: $LS$] -> case ts_text@is_identifier(n) of {
            false -> type_gap(concat("the symbol ", n), "it is not a Silica atom name");
            true -> case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
                true -> atoms_type(t, concat(":", n));
                false -> atoms_type(t, ts_text@concat3(acc, " | :", n))
            }
        }
    }
}

// The Silica type of entry i, or a text with a mark when this printer does not cover it. in_union: the entry is an
// alternative of a union (a set of symbols is then printed as its atoms; anywhere else it is `atom`).
fn type_text(ts: $TYPES$, i: int64, in_union: boolean, d: string) -> string {
    case type_at(ts, i) of {
        (:t_int, w: :i8 | :i16 | :i32 | :i64 | :u8 | :u16 | :u32 | :u64) -> int_type(w);
        (:t_float, w: :f32 | :f64) -> float_type(w);
        (:t_basic, kind: :boolean | :char | :text | :bytes | :symbol | :dynamic) -> basic_type(kind);
        (:t_symbols, names: $LS$) -> case in_union of {
            true -> atoms_type(names, "");
            false -> "atom"
        };
        (:t_tuple, es: $LI$) -> case count(es, 0) < 2 of {
            true -> type_gap("a tuple type of fewer than two elements", "Silica has no such tuple");
            false -> ts_text@concat3("(", type_items(ts, es, "", ", ", false, d), ")")
        };
        (:t_tagged, tag: string, es: $LI$) -> case ts_text@is_identifier(tag) and count(es, 0) > 0 of {
            true -> ts_text@concat3("(", type_items(ts, es, concat(":", tag), ", ", false, d), ")");
            false -> type_gap(concat("the tagged type ", tag), "its tag is not a Silica atom name, or it has no elements")
        };
        (:t_record, fs: $LSI$) -> ts_text@concat3("{ ", field_types(ts, fs, "", d), " }");
        (:t_list, e: int64) -> ts_text@concat3("List[", type_text(ts, e, false, d), ", mem(normal)]");
        (:t_union, alts: $LI$) -> case count(alts, 0) < 1 of {
            true -> type_gap("a union type with no alternatives", "nothing to print");
            false -> union_items(ts, alts, "", d)
        };
        (:t_fun, ps: $LI$, r: int64) -> concat(ts_text@concat3("fn(", type_items(ts, ps, "", ", ", false, d), ") -> "), type_text(ts, r, false, d));
        (:t_actor, _m: int64) -> "actor_ref";
        (:t_named, name: string, as: $LI$) -> named_text(d, name, arg_texts(ts, as, d));
        (:t_var, name: string) -> case starts_with(d, "\x07") and ts_text@is_identifier(name) of {
            true -> ts_text@concat3("\x05", name, "\x06");
            false -> type_gap(concat("the type parameter ", name), "a type parameter is printed only inside a type declaration: Silica cannot make a function generic, so send the specialised type (contract T8.7, T8.14)")
        }
    }
}

// The entries es joined by sep (after acc, when acc is not empty).
fn type_items(ts: $TYPES$, es: $LI$, acc: string, sep: string, in_union: boolean, d: string) -> string {
    case es of {
        []: $LI$ -> acc;
        [e: int64, t: $LI$] -> case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
            true -> type_items(ts, t, type_text(ts, e, in_union, d), sep, in_union, d);
            false -> type_items(ts, t, ts_text@concat3(acc, sep, type_text(ts, e, in_union, d)), sep, in_union, d)
        }
    }
}

fn arg_texts(ts: $TYPES$, as: $LI$, d: string) -> $LS$ {
    case as of {
        []: $LI$ -> none_of();
        [a: int64, t: $LI$] -> cons_s(type_text(ts, a, false, d), arg_texts(ts, t, d))
    }
}

fn replace_all(s: string, key: string, with: string) -> string {
    at: int64 <- ts_text@find(s, key, 0);
    case at < 0 of {
        true -> s;
        false -> concat(concat(substring(s, 0, at), with), replace_all(substring(s, at + length_bytes(key), length_bytes(s)), key, with))
    }
}

fn subst(text: string, params: $LS$, args: $LS$) -> string {
    case params of {
        []: $LS$ -> text;
        [p: string, rest: $LS$] -> case args of {
            []: $LS$ -> text;
            [a: string, more: $LS$] -> subst(replace_all(text, ts_text@concat3("\x05", p, "\x06"), a), rest, more)
        }
    }
}

fn joined(xs: $LS$, acc: string) -> string {
    case xs of {
        []: $LS$ -> acc;
        [x: string, t: $LS$] -> case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
            true -> joined(t, x);
            false -> joined(t, ts_text@concat3(acc, ",", x))
        }
    }
}

// THE DECLARED TYPES OF THE SESSION (contract T8.14). d holds one entry for each (:type) form printed so far, the
// newest first: \x10 name \x11 parameter names joined by "," \x11 the Silica type \x12. In the Silica type a type
// parameter is \x05 name \x06. d starts with \x07 while a declaration itself is printed (type parameters allowed).
fn decl_entry(name: string, params: $LS$, text: string) -> string {
    concat(ts_text@concat4("\x10", name, "\x11", joined(params, "")), ts_text@concat3("\x11", text, "\x12"))
}

// The Silica type the declared type `name` stands for with these arguments, or a mark (T3104).
fn named_text(d: string, name: string, args: $LS$) -> string {
    key: string <- ts_text@concat3("\x10", name, "\x11");
    at: int64 <- ts_text@find(d, key, 0);
    case at < 0 of {
        true -> gap(concat("the declared type ", name), 0 - 1, "T3104", "no (:type) form sent earlier in the session declares it (contract T8.14: a type form comes before every form that names it)");
        false -> {
            a: int64 <- at + length_bytes(key);
            b: int64 <- ts_text@find(d, "\x11", a);
            e: int64 <- ts_text@find(d, "\x12", b);
            params: $LS$ <- case b == a of {
                true -> none_of();
                false -> split_top(substring(d, a, b), 44)
            };
            case count_s(params, 0) == count_s(args, 0) of {
                false -> gap(concat("the declared type ", name), 0 - 1, "T3104", concat(ts_text@concat4("it is declared with ", ts_text@itoa(count_s(params, 0)), " parameters and named here with ", ts_text@itoa(count_s(args, 0))), " arguments (contract T8.14)"));
                true -> subst(substring(d, b + 1, e), params, args)
            }
        }
    }
}

// False for an entry Silica does not accept as an alternative of an inline sum. Measured with compiler 999919:
// atom literals, tagged tuples and records are accepted; `int64 | :timeout` and `(int64, int64) | :x` are refused
// (E2003, "OR'd return types are atom option lists").
fn alternative_ok(t: $TYPENODE$) -> boolean {
    case t of {
        (:t_int, _w: :i8 | :i16 | :i32 | :i64 | :u8 | :u16 | :u32 | :u64) -> false;
        (:t_float, _w: :f32 | :f64) -> false;
        (:t_basic, _k: :boolean | :char | :text | :bytes | :symbol | :dynamic) -> false;
        (:t_tuple, _es: $LI$) -> false;
        (:t_list, _e: int64) -> false;
        (:t_actor, _m: int64) -> false;
        (:t_fun, _ps: $LI$, _r: int64) -> false;
        _: $TYPENODE$ -> true
    }
}

// "A | B" for the alternatives of a union.
fn union_items(ts: $TYPES$, alts: $LI$, acc: string, d: string) -> string {
    case alts of {
        []: $LI$ -> acc;
        [e: int64, t: $LI$] -> {
            x: string <- case alternative_ok(type_at(ts, e)) of {
                true -> type_text(ts, e, true, d);
                false -> type_gap("a union with an alternative that is not a symbol, a tagged tuple or a record", "Silica accepts only atom literals, tagged tuples and records as the alternatives of an inline sum (limitation observed, E2003)")
            };
            case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
                true -> union_items(ts, t, x, d);
                false -> union_items(ts, t, ts_text@concat3(acc, " | ", x), d)
            }
        }
    }
}

fn field_types(ts: $TYPES$, fs: $LSI$, acc: string, d: string) -> string {
    case fs of {
        []: $LSI$ -> case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
            true -> type_gap("a record type with no fields", "nothing to print");
            false -> acc
        };
        [f: (string, int64), t: $LSI$] -> {
            (name: string, e: int64) <- f;
            item: string <- case usable_name(name) of {
                true -> ts_text@concat3(name, ": ", type_text(ts, e, false, d));
                false -> type_gap(concat("the record field ", name), "its name is a Silica reserved word or not an identifier")
            };
            case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
                true -> field_types(ts, t, item, d);
                false -> field_types(ts, t, ts_text@concat3(acc, ", ", item), d)
            }
        }
    }
}

// "p0: A, p1: B" for the parameter types ps (marks included).
fn params_text(ts: $TYPES$, ps: $LI$, k: int64, acc: string, d: string) -> string {
    case ps of {
        []: $LI$ -> acc;
        [p: int64, t: $LI$] -> {
            item: string <- ts_text@concat4("p", ts_text@itoa(k), ": ", type_text(ts, p, false, d));
            case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
                true -> params_text(ts, t, k + 1, item, d);
                false -> params_text(ts, t, k + 1, ts_text@concat3(acc, ", ", item), d)
            }
        }
    }
}

// The parameters as case subjects: (p0, A), (p1, B), ...
fn param_subjects(ts: $TYPES$, ps: $LI$, k: int64, d: string) -> $LSS$ {
    case ps of {
        []: $LI$ -> no_pairs();
        [p: int64, t: $LI$] -> pair_on(concat("p", ts_text@itoa(k)), type_text(ts, p, false, d), param_subjects(ts, t, k + 1, d))
    }
}

// The type index of the first hint on node (the form's own signature is node -1), or -1.
fn hint_index(hs: $HINTS$, node: int64) -> int64 {
    case hs of {
        []: $HINTS$ -> 0 - 1;
        [h: $HINT$, t: $HINTS$] -> case h.node == node of {
            true -> h.type;
            false -> hint_index(t, node)
        }
    }
}

// The Silica type the sender's hint states for node i (contract T8.5), "" when the node has no hint, or a mark.
fn hint_text(c: $CTX$, i: int64) -> string {
    t: int64 <- hint_index(c.hs, i);
    case t < 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> type_text(c.ts, t, false, c.d)
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ literals

fn byte_of(ch: string) -> int64 {
    sequence proc[transport]
        b: int64 <- byte_at(ch, 0)
    produces
        pure b
    end
}

fn hex_digit(d: int64) -> string {
    substring("0123456789abcdef", d, d + 1)
}

// One character of a text literal, escaped for Silica (specification 2.2.3: \n \t \r \\ \" and \xNN).
fn escaped(ch: string) -> string {
    case ch == "\"" of {
        true -> "\\\"";
        false -> case ch == "\\" of {
            true -> "\\\\";
            false -> case length_bytes(ch) == 1 of {
                false -> ch;
                true -> {
                    b: int64 <- byte_of(ch);
                    case b == 10 of {
                        true -> "\\n";
                        false -> case b == 9 of {
                            true -> "\\t";
                            false -> case b == 13 of {
                                true -> "\\r";
                                false -> case b < 32 or b == 127 of {
                                    true -> ts_text@concat3("\\x", hex_digit(b / 16), hex_digit(b % 16));
                                    false -> ch
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn quoted_from(s: string, i: int64, n: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> concat(acc, "\"");
        false -> quoted_from(s, i + 1, n, concat(acc, escaped(substring(s, i, i + 1))))
    }
}

// s as a Silica string literal.
fn quoted(s: string) -> string {
    quoted_from(s, 0, length_chars(s), "\"")
}

// The index after the run of decimal digits of s that starts at i.
fn digits_end(s: string, i: int64, n: int64) -> int64 {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> i;
        false -> {
            b: int64 <- byte_in(s, i);
            case b >= 48 and b <= 57 of {
                true -> digits_end(s, i + 1, n);
                false -> i
            }
        }
    }
}

fn exponent_ok(s: string, f: int64, n: int64) -> boolean {
    case f + 1 < n and (byte_in(s, f) == 101 or byte_in(s, f) == 69) of {
        false -> false;
        true -> {
            sign: int64 <- byte_in(s, f + 1);
            j: int64 <- case sign == 43 or sign == 45 of {
                true -> f + 2;
                false -> f + 1
            };
            k: int64 <- digits_end(s, j, n);
            k > j and k == n
        }
    }
}

// True when s is digits "." digits with an optional exponent (e or E, an optional sign, digits): Silica's float
// literal (lexer: digit+ "." digit+ [exponent]).
fn float_ok(s: string) -> boolean {
    n: int64 <- length_bytes(s);
    w: int64 <- digits_end(s, 0, n);
    case w > 0 and w + 1 < n of {
        false -> false;
        true -> case byte_in(s, w) == 46 of {
            false -> false;
            true -> {
                f: int64 <- digits_end(s, w + 1, n);
                case f > w + 1 of {
                    false -> false;
                    true -> case f == n of {
                        true -> true;
                        false -> exponent_ok(s, f, n)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// The float text of contract H2 as a Silica expression (pattern false) or pattern, or a mark.
fn float_text(s: string, node: int64, pattern: boolean) -> string {
    case float_ok(s) of {
        true -> s;
        false -> case starts_with(s, "-") and float_ok(substring(s, 1, length_bytes(s))) of {
            true -> case pattern of {
                true -> s;
                false -> ts_text@concat3("(0.0 - ", substring(s, 1, length_bytes(s)), ")")
            };
            false -> gap(concat("the float text ", s), node, "T4002", "it is not digits.digits with an optional exponent, the only form of Silica's float literal")
        }
    }
}

fn is_least(v: int64) -> boolean {
    case v < 0 of {
        true -> v + 9223372036854775807 < 0;
        false -> false
    }
}

fn int_text(v: int64) -> string {
    case is_least(v) of {
        true -> "((0 - 9223372036854775807) - 1)";
        false -> case v < 0 of {
            true -> ts_text@concat3("(0 - ", ts_text@itoa(0 - v), ")");
            false -> ts_text@itoa(v)
        }
    }
}

fn int_pattern(v: int64) -> string {
    case is_least(v) of {
        true -> "-9223372036854775808";
        false -> case v < 0 of {
            true -> concat("-", ts_text@itoa(0 - v));
            false -> ts_text@itoa(v)
        }
    }
}

fn boolean_text(b: boolean) -> string {
    case b of {
        true -> "true";
        false -> "false"
    }
}

fn symbol_text(name: string, node: int64) -> string {
    case ts_text@is_identifier(name) of {
        true -> concat(":", name);
        false -> gap(concat("the symbol ", name), node, "T4002", "it is not a Silica atom name (letters, digits and _)")
    }
}

fn int_type_of(want: string) -> string {
    case starts_with(want, "int") or starts_with(want, "uint") of {
        true -> want;
        false -> "int64"
    }
}

fn float_type_of(want: string) -> string {
    case want == "float32" of {
        true -> want;
        false -> "float64"
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ names the printer makes

// A pattern variable at node p is printed as v<p>_, the subject of the case at node i as s<i>_. The closing
// underscore keeps one name from being the start of another, so `contains` tells whether a name is used.
fn vname(p: int64) -> string {
    ts_text@concat3("v", ts_text@itoa(p), "_")
}

fn sname(i: int64) -> string {
    ts_text@concat3("s", ts_text@itoa(i), "_")
}

// A value that can be named again without evaluating anything twice: a parameter or a name made here.
fn simple(text: string) -> boolean {
    ts_text@is_identifier(text)
}

// text as the left side of `.field` or of a call.
fn operand(text: string) -> string {
    case simple(text) of {
        true -> text;
        false -> ts_text@concat3("(", text, ")")
    }
}

// The failing expression of type ty: the helper divides by zero, which ends the actor (`badarith`).
fn fail_text(ty: string, node: int64) -> string {
    d: string <- default_value(ty);
    case length_bytes(d) == 0 of {
        true -> no_value(ty, node);
        false -> ts_text@concat3("{ _: int64 <- to_silica_gap(0); ", d, " }")
    }
}

fn fill(s: string, i: int64, n: int64, start: int64, d: string, acc: string) -> string {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> concat(acc, substring(s, start, n));
        false -> case substring(s, i, i + 1) == hole() of {
            true -> fill(s, i + 1, n, i + 1, d, concat(acc, concat(substring(s, start, i), d)));
            false -> fill(s, i + 1, n, start, d, acc)
        }
    }
}

// Fills the holes the failing catch-alls of one chain left, now that the chain's type is known.
fn finish(x: $EX$, node: int64) -> $EX$ {
    case contains(x.text, hole()) of {
        false -> x;
        true -> {
            d: string <- default_value(x.type);
            with: string <- case length_bytes(d) == 0 of {
                true -> no_value(x.type, node);
                false -> d
            };
            { text: fill(x.text, 0, length_chars(x.text), 0, with, ""), type: x.type }
        }
    }
}

fn fail_hole() -> string {
    ts_text@concat3("{ _: int64 <- to_silica_gap(0); ", hole(), " }")
}

// Why no failing value of type ty can be written at node.
fn no_value(ty: string, node: int64) -> string {
    case length_bytes(ty) == 0 of {
        true -> gap("the case, cond or failure whose value is needed here", node, "T3101", "no type is stated for it (contract T8.10 e): the sender must state it with a hint; the transpiler infers no type");
        false -> gap("a failing catch-all", node, "T4002", ts_text@concat3("this printer can write no value of the type ", ty, " to stand after the failure"))
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ patterns

// ":tag" when the first of the element nodes es is a symbol, else "".
fn tag_of(ns: $NODES$, es: $LI$) -> string {
    case node_at(ns, first_of(es)) of {
        (:symbol, _a: int64, name: string) -> concat(":", name);
        _: $NODE$ -> ""
    }
}

// The element types a tuple of the nodes es has in the type ty (a tuple type, or a union with a tuple alternative
// of that arity and tag); no elements when ty has none.
fn elems_for(ns: $NODES$, ty: string, es: $LI$) -> $LS$ {
    pick(split_top(ty, 124), count(es, 0), tag_of(ns, es))
}

// The bindings pattern p adds when matched with a value of type ty. subj is the text of that value when it can be
// named again (the variable is then printed as it), or "".
// The type of the variable bound at pattern node p: its own hint, else the type ty of what it is matched with
// (contract T8.10 b).
fn var_type(c: $CTX$, p: int64, ty: string) -> string {
    h: string <- hint_text(c, p);
    case length_bytes(h) == 0 or bad(h) of {
        true -> ty;
        false -> h
    }
}

fn pat_env(c: $CTX$, p: int64, ty: string, subj: string, env: $ENV$) -> $ENV$ {
    case node_at(c.ns, p) of {
        (:var, _a: int64, name: string) -> case length_bytes(subj) == 0 of {
            true -> bind(env, name, vname(p), var_type(c, p, ty));
            false -> bind(env, name, subj, var_type(c, p, ty))
        };
        (:tuple, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> pats_env(c, es, elems_for(c.ns, ty, es), 0, env);
        (:cons, _a: int64, h: int64, t: int64) -> pat_env(c, t, ty, "", pat_env(c, h, list_elem(ty), "", env));
        (:list, _a: int64, es: $LI$, t: int64) -> case count(es, 0) == 1 and t >= 0 of {
            true -> pat_env(c, t, ty, "", pat_env(c, first_of(es), list_elem(ty), "", env));
            false -> env
        };
        // A record pattern binds a field's variable as subject.field, so it needs a subject that can be named.
        (:record, _a: int64, _n: string, fields: $LSI$, _b: int64) -> case length_bytes(subj) == 0 of {
            true -> env;
            false -> fields_env(c, fields, record_entries(ty), subj, env)
        };
        // An alias pattern P1 = P2: both patterns are matched with the same value.
        (:match, _a: int64, x: int64, y: int64) -> pat_env(c, y, ty, subj, pat_env(c, x, ty, subj, env));
        _: $NODE$ -> env
    }
}

fn fields_env(c: $CTX$, fields: $LSI$, entries: $LS$, subj: string, env: $ENV$) -> $ENV$ {
    case fields of {
        []: $LSI$ -> env;
        [f: (string, int64), t: $LSI$] -> {
            (name: string, p: int64) <- f;
            fields_env(c, t, entries, subj, pat_env(c, p, entry_type(entries, name), ts_text@concat3(operand(subj), ".", name), env))
        }
    }
}

fn pats_env(c: $CTX$, es: $LI$, tys: $LS$, k: int64, env: $ENV$) -> $ENV$ {
    case es of {
        []: $LI$ -> env;
        [e: int64, t: $LI$] -> pats_env(c, t, tys, k + 1, pat_env(c, e, nth_s(tys, k), "", env))
    }
}

fn open_pattern(ty: string, p: int64, what: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(ty) == 0 of {
        true -> gap(what, p, "T3101", "no type is stated for it, and none for what it is matched with (contract T8.10 b): the sender must state it with a hint; the transpiler infers no type");
        false -> concat("_: ", ty)
    }
}

// Pattern p as a Silica case pattern. used is the text the pattern's variables may be used in: a variable that is
// not in it is printed as `_` (Silica refuses an unused binding, E1055).
fn pat_text(c: $CTX$, p: int64, ty: string, subj: string, used: string) -> string {
    case node_at(c.ns, p) of {
        (:var, _a: int64, name: string) -> {
            h: string <- hint_text(c, p);
            vt: string <- var_type(c, p, ty);
            case bad(h) of {
                true -> at_node(h, p);
                false -> case length_bytes(subj) == 0 and length_bytes(vt) > 0 and contains(used, vname(p)) of {
                    true -> ts_text@concat3(vname(p), ": ", vt);
                    false -> open_pattern(vt, p, concat("the pattern variable ", name))
                }
            }
        };
        (:wild, _a: int64) -> open_pattern(ty, p, "the pattern _");
        (:int, _a: int64, v: int64) -> int_pattern(v);
        (:float, _a: int64, s: string) -> float_text(s, p, true);
        (:text, _a: int64, s: string) -> quoted(s);
        (:bytes, _a: int64, s: string) -> quoted(s);
        (:symbol, _a: int64, name: string) -> symbol_text(name, p);
        (:boolean, _a: int64, b: boolean) -> boolean_text(b);
        (:tuple, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> case count(es, 0) < 2 of {
            true -> gap("a tuple pattern of fewer than two elements", p, "T4002", "Silica has no such tuple");
            false -> ts_text@concat3("(", pats_text(c, es, elems_for(c.ns, ty, es), 0, used), ")")
        };
        (:nil, _a: int64) -> nil_pattern(p, ty);
        (:cons, _a: int64, h: int64, t: int64) -> cons_pattern(c, p, h, t, ty, used);
        (:list, _a: int64, es: $LI$, t: int64) -> case count(es, 0) == 0 and t < 0 of {
            true -> nil_pattern(p, ty);
            false -> case count(es, 0) == 1 and t >= 0 of {
                true -> cons_pattern(c, p, first_of(es), t, ty, used);
                false -> gap("a list pattern of a fixed length", p, "T4002", "only [] and [head | tail] are printed as list patterns")
            }
        };
        (:gap_node, _a: int64, construct: string, note: string) -> gap(construct, p, "T4001", note);
        (:op, _a: int64, op: string, as: $LI$) -> negative_pattern(c.ns, p, op, as);
        other: $NODE$ -> {
            (kind: string, _at: int64) <- node_info(other);
            case is_open(c.ns, p) and length_bytes(subj) > 0 of {
                // a record pattern or an alias pattern that matches everything: its variables are named from the subject
                true -> open_pattern(ty, p, ts_text@concat3("the pattern (:", kind, ")"));
                false -> gap(ts_text@concat3("the pattern (:", kind, ")"), p, "T4002", "only variables, _, literals, tuples, [] and [head | tail] are printed as patterns; a record pattern or an alias pattern is printed where it is matched with a whole parameter, case subject or match value and its parts are variables or _")
            }
        }
    }
}

fn nil_pattern(p: int64, ty: string) -> string {
    case is_list(ty) of {
        true -> concat("[]: ", ty);
        false -> list_pattern_gap(p, ty)
    }
}

fn list_pattern_gap(p: int64, ty: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(ty) == 0 of {
        true -> gap("a list pattern", p, "T3101", "no type is stated for what it is matched with (contract T8.10 e): the sender must state it with a hint; the transpiler infers no type");
        false -> gap("a list pattern", p, "T3103", ts_text@concat3("it is matched with a value of the type ", ty, ", which is not a list"))
    }
}

// One part of [head | tail]: Silica's list pattern binds two names and takes nothing else apart.
fn list_part(c: $CTX$, q: int64, ty: string, used: string) -> string {
    case is_open(c.ns, q) of {
        true -> pat_text(c, q, ty, "", used);
        false -> gap("a pattern inside a list pattern", q, "T4002", "only a variable or _ is printed as the head or the tail of a list pattern")
    }
}

fn cons_pattern(c: $CTX$, p: int64, h: int64, t: int64, ty: string, used: string) -> string {
    case is_list(ty) of {
        true -> concat(ts_text@concat4("[", list_part(c, h, list_elem(ty), used), ", ", list_part(c, t, ty, used)), "]");
        false -> list_pattern_gap(p, ty)
    }
}

// The pattern -N, which a sender may send as the operator neg on a literal.
fn negative_pattern(ns: $NODES$, p: int64, op: string, as: $LI$) -> string {
    case op == "neg" and count(as, 0) == 1 of {
        false -> gap(ts_text@concat3("the operator ", op, " in a pattern"), p, "T4002", "only variables, _, literals and tuples are printed as patterns");
        true -> case node_at(ns, first_of(as)) of {
            (:int, _a: int64, v: int64) -> int_pattern(0 - v);
            (:float, _a: int64, s: string) -> float_text(concat("-", s), p, true);
            _: $NODE$ -> gap("the operator neg in a pattern", p, "T4002", "it is printed only on a number")
        }
    }
}

fn is_list_pattern(ns: $NODES$, p: int64) -> boolean {
    case node_at(ns, p) of {
        (:nil, _a: int64) -> true;
        (:cons, _a: int64, _h: int64, _t: int64) -> true;
        (:list, _a: int64, _es: $LI$, _t: int64) -> true;
        _: $NODE$ -> false
    }
}

fn nested_list_gap(p: int64) -> string {
    gap("a list pattern inside a tuple pattern", p, "T4002", "limitation observed: Silica compiles a list pattern inside a tuple pattern and then takes the wrong arm, so it is not printed")
}

fn pats_text(c: $CTX$, es: $LI$, tys: $LS$, k: int64, used: string) -> string {
    case es of {
        []: $LI$ -> "";
        [e: int64, t: $LI$] -> {
            x: string <- case is_list_pattern(c.ns, e) of {
                true -> nested_list_gap(e);
                false -> pat_text(c, e, nth_s(tys, k), "", used)
            };
            case t of {
                []: $LI$ -> x;
                [_e2: int64, _t2: $LI$] -> ts_text@concat3(x, ", ", pats_text(c, t, tys, k + 1, used))
            }
        }
    }
}

// True when the pattern matches every value: a variable or `_`.
fn is_open(ns: $NODES$, p: int64) -> boolean {
    case node_at(ns, p) of {
        (:var, _a: int64, _n: string) -> true;
        (:wild, _a: int64) -> true;
        (:record, _a: int64, _n: string, fields: $LSI$, b: int64) -> b < 0 and fields_open(ns, fields);
        (:match, _a: int64, x: int64, y: int64) -> is_open(ns, x) and is_open(ns, y);
        _: $NODE$ -> false
    }
}

fn fields_open(ns: $NODES$, fields: $LSI$) -> boolean {
    case fields of {
        []: $LSI$ -> true;
        [f: (string, int64), t: $LSI$] -> {
            (name: string, p: int64) <- f;
            case usable_name(name) and is_open(ns, p) of {
                true -> fields_open(ns, t);
                false -> false
            }
        }
    }
}

// True when the pattern takes its value apart by name (a record or alias pattern): it needs a subject it can name.
fn needs_subject(ns: $NODES$, p: int64) -> boolean {
    case node_at(ns, p) of {
        (:record, _a: int64, _n: string, _f: $LSI$, _b: int64) -> true;
        (:match, _a: int64, _x: int64, _y: int64) -> true;
        _: $NODE$ -> false
    }
}

fn all_open(ns: $NODES$, ps: $LI$) -> boolean {
    case ps of {
        []: $LI$ -> true;
        [p: int64, t: $LI$] -> case is_open(ns, p) of {
            true -> all_open(ns, t);
            false -> false
        }
    }
}

// True when the pattern can fail to match: it holds a literal.
fn refutable(ns: $NODES$, p: int64) -> boolean {
    case node_at(ns, p) of {
        (:var, _a: int64, _n: string) -> false;
        (:wild, _a: int64) -> false;
        (:tuple, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> any_refutable(ns, es);
        _: $NODE$ -> not is_open(ns, p)
    }
}

fn any_refutable(ns: $NODES$, es: $LI$) -> boolean {
    case es of {
        []: $LI$ -> false;
        [e: int64, t: $LI$] -> case refutable(ns, e) of {
            true -> true;
            false -> any_refutable(ns, t)
        }
    }
}

// True when text names a variable the patterns ps bind (as v<p>_).
fn names_used(ns: $NODES$, ps: $LI$, text: string) -> boolean {
    case ps of {
        []: $LI$ -> false;
        [p: int64, t: $LI$] -> case name_used(ns, p, text) of {
            true -> true;
            false -> names_used(ns, t, text)
        }
    }
}

fn name_used(ns: $NODES$, p: int64, text: string) -> boolean {
    case node_at(ns, p) of {
        (:var, _a: int64, _n: string) -> contains(text, vname(p));
        (:tuple, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> names_used(ns, es, text);
        _: $NODE$ -> false
    }
}

// The top-level patterns ps of a clause against the subjects ss. named: the variables get names of their own
// (needed when the clause has a guard: a Silica guard must use a binding of its pattern, E2014).
// A subject whose text starts with \x08 is NOT part of the Silica case: every clause has a variable or _ there, so
// the variable is printed as the subject itself (native narrows the case to the subjects that are taken apart).
fn is_marked(text: string) -> boolean {
    starts_with(text, "\x08")
}

fn unmarked(text: string) -> string {
    case is_marked(text) of {
        true -> substring(text, 1, length_bytes(text));
        false -> text
    }
}

fn tops_env(c: $CTX$, ps: $LI$, ss: $LSS$, named: boolean, env: $ENV$) -> $ENV$ {
    case ps of {
        []: $LI$ -> env;
        [p: int64, pt: $LI$] -> case ss of {
            []: $LSS$ -> env;
            [s: (string, string), st: $LSS$] -> {
                (text: string, ty: string) <- s;
                subj: string <- case named and not is_marked(text) and not needs_subject(c.ns, p) of {
                    true -> "";
                    false -> unmarked(text)
                };
                tops_env(c, pt, st, named, pat_env(c, p, ty, subj, env))
            }
        }
    }
}

fn tops_text(c: $CTX$, ps: $LI$, ss: $LSS$, named: boolean, used: string) -> string {
    case ps of {
        []: $LI$ -> "";
        [p: int64, pt: $LI$] -> case ss of {
            []: $LSS$ -> "";
            [s: (string, string), st: $LSS$] -> {
                (text: string, ty: string) <- s;
                subj: string <- case named and not needs_subject(c.ns, p) of {
                    true -> "";
                    false -> text
                };
                more: string <- tops_text(c, pt, st, named, used);
                case is_marked(text) of {
                    true -> more;
                    false -> {
                        x: string <- case live(ss, 0) > 1 and is_list_pattern(c.ns, p) of {
                            true -> nested_list_gap(p);
                            false -> pat_text(c, p, ty, subj, used)
                        };
                        case length_bytes(more) == 0 of {
                            true -> x;
                            false -> ts_text@concat3(x, ", ", more)
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// How many subjects are part of the Silica case.
fn live(ss: $LSS$, acc: int64) -> int64 {
    case ss of {
        []: $LSS$ -> acc;
        [s: (string, string), t: $LSS$] -> {
            (text: string, _ty: string) <- s;
            case is_marked(text) of {
                true -> live(t, acc);
                false -> live(t, acc + 1)
            }
        }
    }
}

fn subject_texts(ss: $LSS$) -> string {
    case ss of {
        []: $LSS$ -> "";
        [s: (string, string), t: $LSS$] -> {
            (text: string, _ty: string) <- s;
            more: string <- subject_texts(t);
            case is_marked(text) of {
                true -> more;
                false -> case length_bytes(more) == 0 of {
                    true -> text;
                    false -> ts_text@concat3(text, ", ", more)
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// "A, B" for the subjects' types, or "" when one is not known.
fn subject_types(ss: $LSS$) -> string {
    case ss of {
        []: $LSS$ -> "";
        [s: (string, string), t: $LSS$] -> {
            (text: string, ty: string) <- s;
            case is_marked(text) of {
                true -> subject_types(t);
                false -> case live(t, 0) == 0 of {
                    true -> ty;
                    false -> {
                        more: string <- subject_types(t);
                        case length_bytes(ty) == 0 or length_bytes(more) == 0 of {
                            true -> "";
                            false -> ts_text@concat3(ty, ", ", more)
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// One subject is itself; several are matched as a tuple.
fn grouped(ss: $LSS$, inner: string) -> string {
    case live(ss, 0) > 1 and length_bytes(inner) > 0 of {
        true -> ts_text@concat3("(", inner, ")");
        false -> inner
    }
}


fn any_top_var(ns: $NODES$, cs: $LI$) -> boolean {
    case cs of {
        []: $LI$ -> false;
        [k: int64, rest: $LI$] -> case node_at(ns, k) of {
            (:clause, _a: int64, ps: $LI$, _g: int64, _b: int64) -> case node_at(ns, first_of(ps)) of {
                (:var, _a2: int64, _n: string) -> true;
                _: $NODE$ -> case needs_subject(ns, first_of(ps)) of {
                    true -> true;
                    false -> any_top_var(ns, rest)
                }
            };
            _: $NODE$ -> false
        }
    }
}

// 1 when clause k is `true` alone with no guard, 0 when it is `false` alone, -1 otherwise.
fn boolean_clause(ns: $NODES$, k: int64) -> int64 {
    case node_at(ns, k) of {
        (:clause, _a: int64, ps: $LI$, g: int64, _b: int64) -> case g < 0 and count(ps, 0) == 1 of {
            false -> 0 - 1;
            true -> case node_at(ns, first_of(ps)) of {
                (:boolean, _a2: int64, v: boolean) -> case v of {
                    true -> 1;
                    false -> 0
                };
                _: $NODE$ -> 0 - 1
            }
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> 0 - 1
    }
}

// True when the clauses are exactly `true` and `false`: the Silica case needs no catch-all.
fn boolean_pair(ns: $NODES$, cs: $LI$) -> boolean {
    case count(cs, 0) == 2 of {
        false -> false;
        true -> boolean_clause(ns, first_of(cs)) + boolean_clause(ns, second_of(cs)) == 1 and boolean_clause(ns, first_of(cs)) >= 0 and boolean_clause(ns, second_of(cs)) >= 0
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ expressions

// The arguments as of the call at node i as { text, type }: text is "a, b"; type is the bindings that must stand
// before the call ("g7_0_: T <- value; "), one for each argument that is a list built in place. Limitation
// observed: a `{ sequence ... }` block that stands directly as an argument of a call faults when the program runs.
fn bound_args(c: $CTX$, i: int64, as: $LI$, env: $ENV$, k: int64) -> $EX$ {
    case as of {
        []: $LI$ -> { text: "", type: "" };
        [a: int64, t: $LI$] -> {
            x: $EX$ <- expr(c, a, env, "");
            more: $EX$ <- bound_args(c, i, t, env, k + 1);
            name: string <- concat(ts_text@concat4("g", ts_text@itoa(i), "_", ts_text@itoa(k)), "_");
            lifted: boolean <- starts_with(x.text, "{ sequence ") and is_list(x.type);
            this: string <- case lifted of {
                true -> name;
                false -> x.text
            };
            { text: case length_bytes(more.text) == 0 of {
                  true -> this;
                  false -> ts_text@concat3(this, ", ", more.text)
              },
              type: case lifted of {
                  true -> concat(concat(ts_text@concat4(name, ": ", x.type, " <- "), x.text), concat("; ", more.type));
                  false -> more.type
              } }
        }
    }
}

// The call of `callee` with the arguments as of node i.
fn call_text(c: $CTX$, i: int64, callee: string, as: $LI$, env: $ENV$) -> string {
    b: $EX$ <- bound_args(c, i, as, env, 0);
    case length_bytes(b.type) == 0 of {
        true -> ts_text@concat4(callee, "(", b.text, ")");
        false -> concat(ts_text@concat4("{ ", b.type, callee, "("), concat(b.text, ") }"))
    }
}

fn args_text(c: $CTX$, as: $LI$, env: $ENV$, acc: string) -> string {
    case as of {
        []: $LI$ -> acc;
        [a: int64, t: $LI$] -> case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
            true -> args_text(c, t, env, expr(c, a, env, "").text);
            false -> args_text(c, t, env, ts_text@concat3(acc, ", ", expr(c, a, env, "").text))
        }
    }
}

// The elements es as "a, b" with their types "A, B" ("" when one is not known). tys: the types wanted, if any.
fn items_ex(c: $CTX$, es: $LI$, tys: $LS$, k: int64, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    case es of {
        []: $LI$ -> { text: "", type: "" };
        [e: int64, t: $LI$] -> {
            x: $EX$ <- expr(c, e, env, nth_s(tys, k));
            case t of {
                []: $LI$ -> x;
                [_e2: int64, _t2: $LI$] -> {
                    more: $EX$ <- items_ex(c, t, tys, k + 1, env);
                    { text: ts_text@concat3(x.text, ", ", more.text),
                      type: case length_bytes(x.type) == 0 or length_bytes(more.type) == 0 of {
                          true -> "";
                          false -> ts_text@concat3(x.type, ", ", more.type)
                      } }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn tuple_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, es: $LI$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case count(es, 0) < 2 of {
        true -> no("a tuple of fewer than two elements", i, "Silica has no such tuple");
        false -> {
            items: $EX$ <- items_ex(c, es, elems_for(c.ns, want, es), 0, env);
            { text: ts_text@concat3("(", items.text, ")"),
              type: case length_bytes(want) == 0 of {
                  false -> want;
                  true -> case length_bytes(items.type) == 0 of {
                      true -> "";
                      false -> ts_text@concat3("(", items.type, ")")
                  }
              } }
        }
    }
}

fn is_literal(ns: $NODES$, i: int64) -> boolean {
    case node_at(ns, i) of {
        (:int, _a: int64, _v: int64) -> true;
        (:float, _a: int64, _s: string) -> true;
        _: $NODE$ -> false
    }
}

// The type a numeric literal operand is given: other when it is of the literal's kind, else "" (its own default).
fn literal_want(ns: $NODES$, i: int64, other: string) -> string {
    case node_at(ns, i) of {
        (:int, _a: int64, _v: int64) -> case is_int_type(other) of {
            true -> other;
            false -> ""
        };
        (:float, _a: int64, _s: string) -> case is_float_type(other) of {
            true -> other;
            false -> ""
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> ""
    }
}

fn operand_miss(c: $CTX$, a: int64, side: string, op: string) -> $EX$ {
    miss(concat(ts_text@concat4("the ", side, "operand ", node_label(c, a)), concat(" of the operator ", op)), a, "c")
}

// The conversion operators of contract T8.12. Silica has no builtin for them (limitation observed), so each is a
// helper function written into the unit (helpers_for).
fn conversion_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, op: string, a: int64, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    x: $EX$ <- expr(c, a, env, "");
    case bad(x.text) of {
        true -> x;
        false -> case length_bytes(x.type) == 0 of {
            true -> operand_miss(c, a, "", op);
            false -> case op == "to_float" of {
                true -> case x.type == "int64" of {
                    true -> { text: ts_text@concat3("to_silica_i2f(", x.text, ")"), type: "float64" };
                    false -> case is_int_type(x.type) of {
                        true -> { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("{ w", ts_text@itoa(i), "_: ", x.type), concat(ts_text@concat4(" <- ", x.text, "; to_silica_i2f(to_int64(w", ts_text@itoa(i)), "_)) }")), type: "float64" };
                        false -> clash("the operator to_float", i, ts_text@concat3("to_float takes an integer (contract T8.12) and its operand has the type ", x.type, ""))
                    }
                };
                false -> case x.type == "float64" of {
                    true -> case op == "trunc" of {
                        true -> { text: ts_text@concat3("to_silica_f2i(", x.text, ")"), type: "int64" };
                        false -> { text: ts_text@concat3("to_silica_round(", x.text, ")"), type: "int64" }
                    };
                    false -> clash(concat("the operator ", op), i, concat(ts_text@concat3(op, " takes a float64 (contract T8.12) and its operand has the type ", x.type), ""))
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn unary_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, op: string, a: int64, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case op == "neg" of {
        true -> {
            x: $EX$ <- expr(c, a, env, literal_want(c.ns, a, want));
            case bad(x.text) of {
                true -> x;
                false -> case length_bytes(x.type) == 0 of {
                    true -> operand_miss(c, a, "", op);
                    false -> case is_int_type(x.type) or is_float_type(x.type) of {
                        true -> { text: ts_text@concat3("(0 - ", x.text, ")"), type: x.type };
                        false -> clash("the operator neg", i, concat("neg takes an integer or a float (contract Appendix B) and its operand has the type ", x.type))
                    }
                }
            }
        };
        false -> case op == "not" of {
            true -> { text: ts_text@concat3("(not ", expr(c, a, env, "boolean").text, ")"), type: "boolean" };
            false -> case op == "to_float" or op == "trunc" or op == "round" of {
                true -> conversion_ex(c, i, op, a, env);
                false -> no(ts_text@concat3("the operator ", op, " with one operand"), i, "the printer does not cover it (contract Appendix B: the bitwise and list operators are not printed yet)")
            }
        }
    }
}

fn is_logic(op: string) -> boolean {
    op == "and" or op == "andalso" or op == "or" or op == "orelse"
}

fn kind_ok(op: string, t: string) -> boolean {
    case op == "div" or op == "rem" of {
        true -> is_int_type(t);
        false -> case op == "/" of {
            true -> is_float_type(t);
            false -> case is_arithmetic(op) of {
                true -> is_int_type(t) or is_float_type(t);
                false -> true
            }
        }
    }
}

fn kind_rule(op: string) -> string {
    case op == "div" or op == "rem" of {
        true -> "div and rem take integers (contract Appendix B)";
        false -> case op == "/" of {
            true -> "/ takes floats (contract Appendix B, T8.11): for an integer division send div; for a float division of integers send to_float on each operand (T8.12)";
            false -> "+, - and * take integers or floats (contract Appendix B)"
        }
    }
}

// An arithmetic or comparison operator: both operands must have one stated type (contract T8.10 c, T8.11). Nothing
// is converted here: a conversion is an operator the sender writes (T8.12).
fn typed_binary(c: $CTX$, i: int64, op: string, silica_op: string, a: int64, b: int64, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    la: boolean <- is_literal(c.ns, a);
    lb: boolean <- is_literal(c.ns, b);
    r1: $EX$ <- case lb of {
        true -> { text: "", type: "" };
        false -> expr(c, b, env, "")
    };
    lw: string <- case la of {
        false -> "";
        true -> case lb of {
            false -> literal_want(c.ns, a, r1.type);
            true -> case is_arithmetic(op) of {
                true -> literal_want(c.ns, a, want);
                false -> ""
            }
        }
    };
    l: $EX$ <- expr(c, a, env, lw);
    r: $EX$ <- case lb of {
        true -> expr(c, b, env, literal_want(c.ns, b, l.type));
        false -> r1
    };
    case bad(l.text) or bad(r.text) of {
        true -> { text: concat(l.text, r.text), type: "" };
        false -> case length_bytes(l.type) == 0 of {
            true -> operand_miss(c, a, "left ", op);
            false -> case length_bytes(r.type) == 0 of {
                true -> operand_miss(c, b, "right ", op);
                false -> case l.type == r.type of {
                    false -> { text: gap(concat("the operator ", op), i, "T3102", concat(ts_text@concat4("its left operand has the type ", l.type, " and its right operand the type ", r.type), ", and no conversion was sent (contract T8.11): the sender must send to_float, trunc or round on one of them (T8.12); the transpiler converts nothing")), type: "" };
                    true -> case kind_ok(op, l.type) of {
                        false -> clash(concat("the operator ", op), i, concat(ts_text@concat3("its operands have the type ", l.type, ", and "), kind_rule(op)));
                        true -> { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("(", l.text, " ", silica_op), ts_text@concat3(" ", r.text, ")")),
                                  type: case is_arithmetic(op) of {
                                      true -> l.type;
                                      false -> "boolean"
                                  } }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn binary_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, op: string, as: $LI$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    silica_op: string <- lookup(binary_operators(), op);
    case op == "<>" of {
        true -> { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("concat(", expr(c, first_of(as), env, "string").text, ", ", expr(c, second_of(as), env, "string").text), ")"), type: "string" };
        false -> case op == "++" of {
          true -> append_ex(c, i, first_of(as), second_of(as), env, want);
          false -> case length_bytes(silica_op) == 0 of {
            true -> no(ts_text@concat3("the operator ", op, " with two operands"), i, "the printer does not cover it (contract Appendix B: the bitwise and list operators are not printed yet)");
            false -> case is_logic(op) of {
                true -> { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("(", expr(c, first_of(as), env, "boolean").text, " ", silica_op), ts_text@concat3(" ", expr(c, second_of(as), env, "boolean").text, ")")), type: "boolean" };
                false -> typed_binary(c, i, op, silica_op, first_of(as), second_of(as), env, want)
            }
          }
        }
    }
}

// The element types a list append is written for: one helper function for each (to_silica_append_<type>).
fn append_word(elem: string) -> string {
    case elem == "int64" or elem == "float64" or elem == "boolean" or elem == "string" or elem == "atom" or elem == "actor_ref" of {
        true -> elem;
        false -> ""
    }
}

// `++` (contract Appendix B): both operands and the result are one list type, stated by a hint or by the place.
fn append_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, a: int64, b: int64, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    ax: $EX$ <- expr(c, a, env, want);
    bx: $EX$ <- expr(c, b, env, or_type(want, ax.type));
    t: string <- or_type(want, or_type(ax.type, bx.type));
    case bad(ax.text) of {
        true -> ax;
        false -> case bad(bx.text) of {
            true -> bx;
            false -> case is_list(t) of {
                false -> case length_bytes(t) == 0 of {
                    true -> miss("the list append ++", i, "e");
                    false -> clash("the list append ++", i, ts_text@concat3("its stated type is ", t, ", which is not a list"))
                };
                true -> case ax.type == t and bx.type == t of {
                    false -> clash("the list append ++", i, concat(ts_text@concat4("its operands have the stated types ", ax.type, " and ", bx.type), ts_text@concat3(" and its result ", t, " (contract T8.11: one type)")));
                    true -> case length_bytes(append_word(list_elem(t))) == 0 of {
                        true -> no("the list append ++", i, ts_text@concat3("it is written for lists of int64, float64, boolean, string, atom and process references; this one is a ", t, ""));
                        // Limitation observed: a `{ sequence ... }` block that stands directly as an argument of a call
                        // faults when the program runs; bound to a name first it does not. So the operands are bound.
                        false -> { text: concat(concat(ts_text@concat4("{ x", ts_text@itoa(i), "_: ", t), ts_text@concat4(" <- ", ax.text, "; y", ts_text@itoa(i))), concat(concat(ts_text@concat4("_: ", t, " <- ", bx.text), ts_text@concat4("; to_silica_append_", list_elem(t), "(x", ts_text@itoa(i))), ts_text@concat3("_, y", ts_text@itoa(i), "_) }"))), type: t }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn op_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, op: string, as: $LI$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    n: int64 <- count(as, 0);
    case n == 1 of {
        true -> unary_ex(c, i, op, first_of(as), env, want);
        false -> case n == 2 of {
            true -> binary_ex(c, i, op, as, env, want);
            false -> no(concat("the operator ", op), i, "it has neither one nor two operands")
        }
    }
}

fn call_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, module_name: string, name: string, as: $LI$, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    case local_module(c, module_name) of {
        false -> no(concat(ts_text@concat4("a call to ", module_name, ":", name), concat("/", ts_text@itoa(count(as, 0)))), i, "the contract gives a call to another module no meaning yet (T9.9 has no foreign call)");
        true -> case length_bytes(printed_name(name)) > 0 of {
            false -> no(concat(ts_text@concat3("a call to ", name, "/"), ts_text@itoa(count(as, 0))), i, "the name is not an identifier (letters, digits and _), or starts with to_silica_");
            // The result's type is stated only by a hint on the call or by its place (contract T8.9, T8.10 d).
            true -> { text: call_text(c, i, printed_name(name), as, env), type: "" }
        }
    }
}

fn field_node(fields: $LSI$, name: string) -> int64 {
    case fields of {
        []: $LSI$ -> 0 - 1;
        [f: (string, int64), t: $LSI$] -> {
            (k: string, v: int64) <- f;
            case k == name of {
                true -> v;
                false -> field_node(t, name)
            }
        }
    }
}

// The fields of a record construction as "a: X, b: Y" with their types "a: T, b: U" ("" when one is not known).
fn fields_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, fields: $LSI$, entries: $LS$, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    case fields of {
        []: $LSI$ -> { text: "", type: "" };
        [f: (string, int64), t: $LSI$] -> {
            (name: string, v: int64) <- f;
            x: $EX$ <- case usable_name(name) of {
                true -> expr(c, v, env, entry_type(entries, name));
                false -> no(concat("the record field ", name), i, "its name is a Silica reserved word or not an identifier")
            };
            case t of {
                []: $LSI$ -> { text: ts_text@concat3(name, ": ", x.text),
                               type: case length_bytes(x.type) == 0 of {
                                   true -> "";
                                   false -> ts_text@concat3(name, ": ", x.type)
                               } };
                [_f2: (string, int64), _t2: $LSI$] -> {
                    more: $EX$ <- fields_ex(c, i, t, entries, env);
                    { text: concat(ts_text@concat4(name, ": ", x.text, ", "), more.text),
                      type: case length_bytes(x.type) == 0 or length_bytes(more.type) == 0 of {
                          true -> "";
                          false -> concat(ts_text@concat4(name, ": ", x.type, ", "), more.type)
                      } }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// Every field of the record type, taken from the update's fields or else from the base (Silica has no
// record-update syntax).
fn update_text(c: $CTX$, entries: $LS$, fields: $LSI$, base: string, env: $ENV$) -> string {
    case entries of {
        []: $LS$ -> "";
        [e: string, t: $LS$] -> {
            name: string <- entry_name(e);
            v: int64 <- field_node(fields, name);
            item: string <- case v < 0 of {
                true -> concat(ts_text@concat4(name, ": ", base, "."), name);
                false -> ts_text@concat3(name, ": ", expr(c, v, env, entry_type(entries, name)).text)
            };
            case t of {
                []: $LS$ -> item;
                [_e2: string, _t2: $LS$] -> ts_text@concat3(item, ", ", update_text(c, t, fields, base, env))
            }
        }
    }
}

fn record_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, fields: $LSI$, base: int64, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case base < 0 of {
        true -> {
            fs: $EX$ <- fields_ex(c, i, fields, record_entries(want), env);
            case length_bytes(fs.text) == 0 of {
                true -> no("a record with no fields", i, "nothing to print");
                false -> { text: ts_text@concat3("{ ", fs.text, " }"),
                           type: case length_bytes(want) == 0 of {
                               false -> want;
                               true -> case length_bytes(fs.type) == 0 of {
                                   true -> "";
                                   false -> ts_text@concat3("{ ", fs.type, " }")
                               }
                           } }
            }
        };
        false -> {
            b: $EX$ <- expr(c, base, env, want);
            bt: string <- or_type(b.type, want);
            entries: $LS$ <- record_entries(bt);
            case count_s(entries, 0) == 0 of {
                true -> case bad(b.text) of {
                    true -> b;
                    false -> no("a record update", i, "the type of the record is not known, and Silica has no record-update syntax: every field must be written")
                };
                false -> { text: ts_text@concat3("{ ", update_text(c, entries, fields, operand(b.text), env), " }"), type: bt }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn case_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, s: int64, cs: $LI$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    sx: $EX$ <- expr(c, s, env, "");
    t: string <- sx.type;
    case bad(sx.text) of {
        true -> sx;
        false -> case length_bytes(t) == 0 of {
            true -> miss(ts_text@concat3("the subject ", node_label(c, s), " of a case"), s, "e");
            false -> case simple(sx.text) or not any_top_var(c.ns, cs) of {
                true -> chain(c, cs, pair_on(sx.text, t, no_pairs()), env, want);
                false -> {
                    r: $EX$ <- chain(c, cs, pair_on(sname(i), t, no_pairs()), env, want);
                    { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("{ ", sname(i), ": ", t), concat(ts_text@concat4(" <- ", sx.text, "; ", r.text), " }")), type: r.type }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// The elements es as "a, b", each of the type ty.
fn items_all(c: $CTX$, es: $LI$, ty: string, env: $ENV$) -> string {
    case es of {
        []: $LI$ -> "";
        [e: int64, t: $LI$] -> case t of {
            []: $LI$ -> expr(c, e, env, ty).text;
            [_e2: int64, _t2: $LI$] -> ts_text@concat3(expr(c, e, env, ty).text, ", ", items_all(c, t, ty, env))
        }
    }
}

// es in front of the list tail, one prepend for each element.
fn prepends(c: $CTX$, i: int64, es: $LI$, k: int64, env: $ENV$, lt: string, tail: string) -> string {
    case es of {
        []: $LI$ -> tail;
        [e: int64, t: $LI$] -> list_block(i, k, lt, concat(ts_text@concat4("prepend[", list_elem(lt), ", mem(normal)](", expr(c, e, env, list_elem(lt)).text), ts_text@concat3(", ", prepends(c, i, t, k + 1, env, lt, tail), ")")))
    }
}

// A list (contract H7, H9, H10). Its type is the hint on the node or what its place states (T8.9).
fn list_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, es: $LI$, tail: int64, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case is_list(want) of {
        false -> case length_bytes(want) == 0 of {
            true -> miss(ts_text@concat3("the list ", node_label(c, i), ""), i, "e");
            false -> clash(ts_text@concat3("the list ", node_label(c, i), ""), i, ts_text@concat3("its hint or its place states the type ", want, ", which is not a list"))
        };
        true -> case tail < 0 of {
            true -> case count(es, 0) == 0 of {
                true -> { text: list_block(i, 0, want, ts_text@concat3("empty[", list_elem(want), ", mem(normal)]()")), type: want };
                false -> { text: list_block(i, 0, want, ts_text@concat3("[", items_all(c, es, list_elem(want), env), "]")), type: want }
            };
            false -> { text: prepends(c, i, es, 0, env, want, expr(c, tail, env, want).text), type: want }
        }
    }
}

// L1 (contract T9.16): a call of a Silica builtin by its Silica name, as the sender wrote it. Only the builtins
// below, which write to standard output or name an atom, with unit "" (a builtin belongs to no unit). The type
// of the call and of its one argument is the builtin's own, fixed by Silica: an argument whose stated type is
// another is T3103, one with no stated type T3101. A print builtin needs the device_io effect, so it is called
// through a helper function to_silica_b_<name> that unit_rest writes (helpers_for).
fn builtin_result(name: string) -> string {
    case name == "print" or name == "println" or name == "print_int64" or name == "print_float64" or name == "print_boolean" of {
        true -> "atom";
        false -> case name == "atom_name" of {
            true -> "string";
            false -> ""
        }
    }
}

fn builtin_param(name: string) -> string {
    case name == "print_int64" of {
        true -> "int64";
        false -> case name == "print_float64" of {
            true -> "float64";
            false -> case name == "print_boolean" of {
                true -> "boolean";
                false -> case name == "atom_name" of {
                    true -> "atom";
                    false -> "string"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sl_call_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, bu: string, name: string, as: $LI$, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    sep: string <- case length_bytes(bu) == 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> "@"
    };
    what: string <- ts_text@concat4("(:sl_call) of ", bu, sep, name);
    case length_bytes(bu) == 0 and length_bytes(builtin_result(name)) > 0 of {
        false -> no(what, i, "only the Silica builtins print, println, print_int64, print_float64, print_boolean and atom_name, with unit \"\", are printed (contract T9.16); a BEES unit or any other builtin is not");
        true -> case count(as, 0) == 1 of {
            false -> no(what, i, "the builtin takes one argument");
            true -> {
                a: $EX$ <- expr(c, first_of(as), env, builtin_param(name));
                case bad(a.text) of {
                    true -> a;
                    false -> case length_bytes(a.type) == 0 of {
                        true -> miss(concat("the argument of ", what), first_of(as), "e");
                        false -> case a.type == builtin_param(name) of {
                            false -> clash(what, i, concat(ts_text@concat4("its argument has the type ", a.type, " and the builtin takes ", builtin_param(name)), " (contract T9.16): the transpiler converts nothing"));
                            true -> { text: case name == "atom_name" of {
                                          true -> ts_text@concat3("atom_name(", a.text, ")");
                                          false -> concat(ts_text@concat4("to_silica_b_", name, "(", a.text), ")")
                                      },
                                      type: builtin_result(name) }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn one(x: int64) -> $LI$ {
    sequence proc[mem(normal)]
        out: $LI$ <- [x]
    produces
        pure out
    end
}

// What the type stated for a node (its hint, or its place) makes of the node's own type (contract T8.9): a node
// with no type of its own takes it; a scalar type that differs is inconsistent typing (T3103), never converted.
fn placed(c: $CTX$, i: int64, x: $EX$, want: string, hinted: boolean) -> $EX$ {
    case bad(x.text) or length_bytes(want) == 0 of {
        true -> x;
        false -> case length_bytes(x.type) == 0 of {
            true -> { text: x.text, type: want };
            false -> case scalar(x.type) and scalar(want) and not (x.type == want) of {
                true -> clash(node_label(c, i), i, concat(ts_text@concat4("it has the type ", x.type, " and ", case hinted of {
                    true -> "its hint";
                    false -> "its place"
                }), ts_text@concat3(" states ", want, " (contract T8.9, T8.11): the transpiler converts nothing; the sender must send a conversion operator (T8.12) or correct the types")));
                false -> case hinted of {
                    true -> { text: x.text, type: want };
                    false -> x
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// The Silica text and type of expression node i. want: the type its place states ("" when none). A hint on the
// node (contract T8.5) is used before everything else. The text holds a mark when a construct is outside this
// printer or a type the contract requires is not stated.
fn expr(c: $CTX$, i: int64, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case want == smode() of {
        true -> tail_ex(c, i, env);
        false -> case node_at(c.ns, i) of {
            (:send, _a: int64, dest: int64, m: int64) -> send_ex(c, i, "", dest, m, env, false, want);
            (:send_named, _a: int64, name: string, m: int64) -> send_named_ex(c, i, name, m, env, false, want);
            _: $NODE$ -> hinted_expr(c, i, env, want)
        }
    }
}

fn hinted_expr(c: $CTX$, i: int64, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    h: string <- hint_text(c, i);
    case length_bytes(h) == 0 of {
        true -> placed(c, i, expr1(c, i, env, want), want, false);
        false -> case bad(h) of {
            true -> { text: at_node(h, i), type: "" };
            false -> placed(c, i, expr1(c, i, env, h), h, true)
        }
    }
}

// Node i itself, before its hint and its place are looked at (expr).
fn expr1(c: $CTX$, i: int64, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case node_at(c.ns, i) of {
        (:int, _a: int64, v: int64) -> { text: int_text(v), type: int_type_of(want) };
        (:float, _a: int64, s: string) -> { text: float_text(s, i, false), type: float_type_of(want) };
        (:text, _a: int64, s: string) -> { text: quoted(s), type: "string" };
        (:bytes, _a: int64, s: string) -> { text: quoted(s), type: "string" };
        (:symbol, _a: int64, name: string) -> { text: symbol_text(name, i), type: or_type(want, "atom") };
        (:boolean, _a: int64, b: boolean) -> { text: boolean_text(b), type: "boolean" };
        (:var, _a: int64, name: string) -> {
            bound: $EX$ <- find(env, name);
            case length_bytes(bound.text) == 0 of {
                true -> no(concat("the variable ", name), i, "it is not bound where it is used (it may be bound by a construct the printer does not follow)");
                false -> bound
            }
        };
        (:tuple, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> tuple_ex(c, i, es, env, want);
        (:record, _a: int64, _name: string, fields: $LSI$, base: int64) -> record_ex(c, i, fields, base, env, want);
        (:field, _a: int64, r: int64, name: string) -> {
            x: $EX$ <- expr(c, r, env, "");
            case usable_name(name) of {
                true -> { text: ts_text@concat3(operand(x.text), ".", name), type: entry_type(record_entries(x.type), name) };
                false -> no(concat("the record field ", name), i, "its name is a Silica reserved word or not an identifier")
            }
        };
        (:op, _a: int64, op: string, as: $LI$) -> op_ex(c, i, op, as, env, want);
        (:call, _a: int64, m: string, f: string, as: $LI$) -> call_ex(c, i, m, f, as, env);
        (:sl_call, _a: int64, u: string, f: string, as: $LI$) -> sl_call_ex(c, i, u, f, as, env);
        (:apply, _a: int64, f: int64, as: $LI$) -> {
            fx: $EX$ <- expr(c, f, env, "");
            case simple(fx.text) or bad(fx.text) of {
                true -> { text: call_text(c, i, fx.text, as, env), type: fn_result(fx.type) };
                false -> no("a call through a function value", i, "the function is not a parameter or a named local function")
            }
        };
        (:fun_ref, _a: int64, m: string, name: string, _arity: int64) -> case local_module(c, m) and length_bytes(printed_name(name)) > 0 of {
            true -> { text: printed_name(name), type: "" };
            false -> no(ts_text@concat4("a reference to the function ", m, ":", name), i, "it is in another module, or its name is not an identifier")
        };
        (:self, _a: int64) -> { text: "to_silica_self()", type: "actor_ref" };
        (:spawn, _a: int64, f: int64, as: $LI$, linked: boolean) -> spawn_ex(c, i, f, as, linked, env);
        (:send, _a: int64, dest: int64, m: int64) -> send_ex(c, i, "", dest, m, env, false, want);
        (:send_named, _a: int64, name: string, m: int64) -> send_named_ex(c, i, name, m, env, false, want);
        (:register, _a: int64, name: string, p: int64) -> register_ex(c, i, name, p, env);
        (:exit_signal, _a: int64, dest: int64, r: int64) -> exit_ex(c, i, dest, r, env);
        (:case, _a: int64, s: int64, cs: $LI$) -> case_ex(c, i, s, cs, env, want);
        (:cond, _a: int64, cs: $LI$) -> chain(c, cs, no_pairs(), env, want);
        (:block, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> case count(es, 0) == 1 of {
            true -> expr(c, first_of(es), env, want);
            false -> {
                b: $EX$ <- block(c, i, es, env, want);
                { text: ts_text@concat3("{ ", b.text, " }"), type: b.type }
            }
        };
        (:match, _a: int64, p: int64, v: int64) -> case is_open(c.ns, p) of {
            true -> expr(c, v, env, want);
            false -> no("a match used as a value", i, "only a match that is a statement of a block, or that binds one variable, is printed")
        };
        (:gap_node, _a: int64, construct: string, note: string) -> { text: gap(construct, i, "T4001", note), type: "" };
        (:nil, _a: int64) -> list_ex(c, i, none_i(), 0 - 1, env, want);
        (:cons, _a: int64, h: int64, t: int64) -> list_ex(c, i, one(h), t, env, want);
        (:list, _a: int64, es: $LI$, t: int64) -> list_ex(c, i, es, t, env, want);
        (:loop_hint, _a: int64, b: int64) -> expr(c, b, env, want);
        // PROVISIONAL (contract H26): the actor ends; the reason is not carried.
        (:fail, _a: int64, _r: int64) -> case length_bytes(want) == 0 of {
            true -> { text: fail_hole(), type: "" };
            false -> { text: fail_text(want, i), type: want }
        };
        other: $NODE$ -> {
            (kind: string, _at: int64) <- node_info(other);
            no(ts_text@concat3("(:", kind, ")"), i, kind_note(kind))
        }
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ blocks (contract H18, H19)

// The statements es as "a; b; value" (the caller adds the braces).
fn block(c: $CTX$, i: int64, es: $LI$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case es of {
        []: $LI$ -> no("an empty block", i, "it has no value");
        [e: int64, rest: $LI$] -> case rest of {
            []: $LI$ -> expr(c, e, env, want);
            [_r: int64, _t: $LI$] -> case node_at(c.ns, e) of {
                (:match, _a: int64, p: int64, v: int64) -> match_then(c, p, v, rest, env, want);
                (:send, _a: int64, dest: int64, m: int64) -> discard_then(c, e, send_ex(c, e, "", dest, m, env, true, ""), rest, env, want);
                (:send_named, _a: int64, name: string, m: int64) -> discard_then(c, e, send_named_ex(c, e, name, m, env, true, ""), rest, env, want);
                _: $NODE$ -> discard_then(c, e, expr(c, e, env, ""), rest, env, want)
            }
        }
    }
}

// A statement whose value is not used: Silica still needs its type to write `_: T <- value;`.
fn discard_then(c: $CTX$, e: int64, x: $EX$, rest: $LI$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case length_bytes(x.type) == 0 of {
        true -> case bad(x.text) of {
            true -> x;
            false -> miss(ts_text@concat3("the statement ", node_label(c, e), " whose value is not used"), e, "e")
        };
        false -> {
            r: $EX$ <- block(c, e, rest, env, want);
            { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("_: ", x.type, " <- ", x.text), concat("; ", r.text)), type: r.type }
        }
    }
}

// `pattern = value` followed by the statements rest.
fn match_then(c: $CTX$, p: int64, v: int64, rest: $LI$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case node_at(c.ns, p) of {
        (:var, _a: int64, name: string) -> {
            h: string <- hint_text(c, p);
            // The variable's own hint states the value's type too (contract T8.10 b).
            val: $EX$ <- case bad(h) of {
                true -> { text: at_node(h, p), type: "" };
                false -> expr(c, v, env, h)
            };
            case bad(val.text) of {
                true -> val;
                false -> case length_bytes(val.type) == 0 of {
                    true -> miss(concat(ts_text@concat4("the binding of the variable ", name, " to a ", node_label(c, v)), ""), p, "b");
                    false -> {
                        r: $EX$ <- block(c, p, rest, bind(env, name, vname(p), val.type), want);
                        bound: string <- case contains(r.text, vname(p)) of {
                            true -> vname(p);
                            false -> "_"
                        };
                        { text: concat(ts_text@concat4(bound, ": ", val.type, " <- "), ts_text@concat3(val.text, "; ", r.text)), type: r.type }
                    }
                }
            }
        };
        (:wild, _a: int64) -> discard_then(c, p, expr(c, v, env, ""), rest, env, want);
        _: $NODE$ -> {
            val: $EX$ <- expr(c, v, env, "");
            t: string <- val.type;
            case bad(val.text) of {
                true -> val;
                false -> case length_bytes(t) == 0 of {
                    true -> miss(ts_text@concat3("the value ", node_label(c, v), " of a match against a pattern"), v, "e");
                    false -> case needs_subject(c.ns, p) and is_open(c.ns, p) of {
                      true -> case simple(val.text) of {
                        true -> block(c, p, rest, pat_env(c, p, t, val.text, env), want);
                        false -> {
                            r: $EX$ <- block(c, p, rest, pat_env(c, p, t, sname(p), env), want);
                            { text: concat(ts_text@concat4(sname(p), ": ", t, " <- "), ts_text@concat3(val.text, "; ", r.text)), type: r.type }
                        }
                      };
                      false -> {
                        r: $EX$ <- block(c, p, rest, pat_env(c, p, t, "", env), want);
                        pt: string <- pat_text(c, p, t, "", r.text);
                        ty: string <- or_type(want, r.type);
                        case refutable(c.ns, p) of {
                            true -> { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("case ", val.text, " of { ", pt), concat(ts_text@concat4(" -> { ", r.text, " }; _: ", t), ts_text@concat3(" -> ", fail_text(ty, p), " }"))), type: ty };
                            false -> { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("case ", val.text, " of { ", pt), ts_text@concat3(" -> { ", r.text, " } }")), type: ty }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ clauses

fn guard_text(c: $CTX$, g: int64, env: $ENV$) -> string {
    case g < 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            t: string <- expr(c, g, env, "").text;
            case t == "true" of {
                true -> "";
                false -> t
            }
        }
    }
}

// A clause whose patterns match everything: its variables are printed as the subjects, and only its guard (if any)
// chooses.
fn open_clause(c: $CTX$, k: int64, rest: $LI$, ss: $LSS$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case node_at(c.ns, k) of {
        (:clause, _a: int64, ps: $LI$, g: int64, b: int64) -> {
            e2: $ENV$ <- tops_env(c, ps, ss, false, env);
            body: $EX$ <- expr(c, b, e2, want);
            gt: string <- guard_text(c, g, e2);
            case length_bytes(gt) == 0 of {
                true -> { text: body.text, type: or_type(want, body.type) };
                false -> {
                    r: $EX$ <- chain_raw(c, rest, ss, env, want);
                    { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("case ", gt, " of { true -> ", body.text), ts_text@concat3("; false -> ", r.text, " }")),
                      type: or_type(want, or_type(body.type, r.type)) }
                }
            }
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> no("a clause", k, "the node is not a (:clause)")
    }
}

// One arm of a Silica case for clause k, followed by the arms of the clauses after it.
fn arm(c: $CTX$, k: int64, rest: $LI$, ss: $LSS$, env: $ENV$, want: string, closed: boolean) -> $EX$ {
    case node_at(c.ns, k) of {
        (:clause, _a: int64, ps: $LI$, g: int64, b: int64) -> {
            named: boolean <- g >= 0;
            e2: $ENV$ <- tops_env(c, ps, ss, named, env);
            body: $EX$ <- expr(c, b, e2, want);
            gt: string <- guard_text(c, g, e2);
            pt: string <- grouped(ss, tops_text(c, ps, ss, named, concat(gt, body.text)));
            more: $EX$ <- case g < 0 and not any_refutable(c.ns, ps) of {
                true -> { text: "", type: "" };
                false -> arms(c, rest, ss, env, want, closed)
            };
            this: string <- case length_bytes(gt) == 0 of {
                true -> ts_text@concat3(pt, " -> ", body.text);
                false -> case names_used(c.ns, ps, gt) of {
                    true -> concat(ts_text@concat4(pt, " if ", gt, " -> "), body.text);
                    // A Silica guard must use a binding of its pattern (E2014); this one does not, so it is tested
                    // inside the arm and the clauses after it are written a second time for when it is false.
                    false -> concat(ts_text@concat4(pt, " -> case ", gt, " of { true -> "), ts_text@concat4(body.text, "; false -> ", chain_raw(c, rest, ss, env, want).text, " }"))
                }
            };
            { text: case length_bytes(more.text) == 0 of {
                  true -> this;
                  false -> ts_text@concat3(this, "; ", more.text)
              },
              type: or_type(want, or_type(body.type, more.type)) }
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> no("a clause", k, "the node is not a (:clause)")
    }
}

// The arms for the clauses cs. closed: the clauses are `true` and `false`, so no catch-all is needed; otherwise the
// arms end in a catch-all, which runs the clauses from the first one that matches everything, or fails.
fn arms(c: $CTX$, cs: $LI$, ss: $LSS$, env: $ENV$, want: string, closed: boolean) -> $EX$ {
    case cs of {
        []: $LI$ -> case closed of {
            true -> { text: "", type: want };
            false -> { text: ts_text@concat4("_: ", grouped(ss, subject_types(ss)), " -> ", fail_hole()), type: want }
        };
        [k: int64, rest: $LI$] -> case node_at(c.ns, k) of {
            (:clause, _a: int64, ps: $LI$, _g: int64, _b: int64) -> case count(ps, 0) == count_ss(ss, 0) of {
                false -> no("a clause", k, "it does not have one pattern for each value it is matched with");
                true -> case all_open(c.ns, ps) of {
                    true -> {
                        r: $EX$ <- chain_raw(c, cs, ss, env, want);
                        { text: ts_text@concat4("_: ", grouped(ss, subject_types(ss)), " -> ", r.text), type: r.type }
                    };
                    false -> arm(c, k, rest, ss, env, want, closed)
                }
            };
            (:gap_node, _a: int64, construct: string, note: string) -> { text: gap(construct, k, "T4001", note), type: "" };
            _: $NODE$ -> no("a clause", k, "the node is not a (:clause)")
        }
    }
}

// A Silica case over the subjects for the clauses cs, the first of which has a pattern that is not open.
// True when every clause of cs has a variable or _ as its pattern number k.
fn column_open(ns: $NODES$, cs: $LI$, k: int64) -> boolean {
    case cs of {
        []: $LI$ -> true;
        [x: int64, rest: $LI$] -> case node_at(ns, x) of {
            (:clause, _a: int64, ps: $LI$, _g: int64, _b: int64) -> case is_open(ns, nth_i(ps, k)) of {
                true -> column_open(ns, rest, k);
                false -> false
            };
            _: $NODE$ -> column_open(ns, rest, k)
        }
    }
}

fn nth_i(xs: $LI$, i: int64) -> int64 {
    case xs of {
        []: $LI$ -> 0 - 1;
        [x: int64, t: $LI$] -> case i == 0 of {
            true -> x;
            false -> nth_i(t, i - 1)
        }
    }
}

// The subjects with those marked that no clause takes apart (see is_marked); at least one stays.
fn narrowed(ns: $NODES$, cs: $LI$, ss: $LSS$, k: int64, kept: int64) -> $LSS$ {
    case ss of {
        []: $LSS$ -> no_pairs();
        [s: (string, string), t: $LSS$] -> {
            (text: string, ty: string) <- s;
            plain: string <- unmarked(text);
            last_chance: boolean <- kept == 0 and count_ss(t, 0) == 0;
            case column_open(ns, cs, k) and not last_chance of {
                true -> pair_on(concat("\x08", plain), ty, narrowed(ns, cs, t, k + 1, kept));
                false -> pair_on(plain, ty, narrowed(ns, cs, t, k + 1, kept + 1))
            }
        }
    }
}

// A Silica case over the subjects for the clauses cs, the first of which has a pattern that is not open. The case
// is over the subjects some clause takes apart; the others are named as they are.
fn native(c: $CTX$, cs: $LI$, ss: $LSS$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    ss1: $LSS$ <- narrowed(c.ns, cs, ss, 0, 0);
    t: string <- subject_types(ss1);
    case length_bytes(t) == 0 of {
        true -> miss("the value a case is matched with", first_of(cs), "e");
        false -> {
            a: $EX$ <- arms(c, cs, ss1, env, want, boolean_pair(c.ns, cs));
            { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("case ", grouped(ss1, subject_texts(ss1)), " of { ", a.text), " }"), type: a.type }
        }
    }
}

// The clauses cs tried in order against the subjects ss (none for a `cond`). A chain that runs out of clauses ends
// in the failing catch-all (contract H28); its value is a hole until the chain's type is known.
fn chain_raw(c: $CTX$, cs: $LI$, ss: $LSS$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case cs of {
        []: $LI$ -> { text: fail_hole(), type: want };
        [k: int64, rest: $LI$] -> case node_at(c.ns, k) of {
            (:clause, _a: int64, ps: $LI$, _g: int64, _b: int64) -> case count(ps, 0) == count_ss(ss, 0) of {
                false -> no("a clause", k, "it does not have one pattern for each value it is matched with");
                true -> case all_open(c.ns, ps) of {
                    true -> open_clause(c, k, rest, ss, env, want);
                    false -> native(c, cs, ss, env, want)
                }
            };
            (:gap_node, _a: int64, construct: string, note: string) -> { text: gap(construct, k, "T4001", note), type: "" };
            _: $NODE$ -> no("a clause", k, "the node is not a (:clause)")
        }
    }
}

fn chain(c: $CTX$, cs: $LI$, ss: $LSS$, env: $ENV$, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    finish(chain_raw(c, cs, ss, env, want), first_of(cs))
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ processes (contract H20 to H26, app design 5.5)
//
// HOW A PROCESS IS PRINTED. A function that holds a (:receive) is a PROCESS FUNCTION. It is printed in "tail
// mode": every expression in tail position gives the process's next state (the type S below) instead of a value.
//   to_silica_e_<f>_<n>(p0, ..., k) -> S      the function's body up to its first receive ("e" for enter)
//   to_silica_r_<f>_<n>_<node>(msg, a0, ..., k) -> S   one receive: the clause the message matches, run to the
//                                             next receive; a0... are the variables that are live at the receive
// S is { ph: P, k: K }. P is the sum of every phase of the unit: (:to_silica_s_<f>_<n>, args) a process that has
// not started, (:to_silica_w_<f>_<n>_<node>, live variables) a process waiting in that receive, and the fixed
// phases done, failed, nomatch and unstarted. K is { wait, up } (see the runtime). M is the sum of every message
// of the unit. P and M are known only when the whole unit has been printed, so a form is printed with the marks
// \x13P\x14, \x13M\x14, \x13S\x14 (and \x13C\x14 in the runtime) where they stand, and with marker lines that
// say what it adds to them; unit_rest spells them out:
//   //@to_silica proc<TAB>f_n                 the unit has to_silica_e_f_n
//   //@to_silica ph<TAB>alternative           an alternative of P
//   //@to_silica arm<TAB>pattern -> call      its arm in to_silica_dispatch
//   //@to_silica msg<TAB>alternative          an alternative of M
//   //@to_silica spawn<TAB>f_n<TAB>f/n<TAB>printed name<TAB>alternative     f/n is spawned (or is the entry)
// A tail call of another function of the unit is the mark \x15 f_n \x16 printed name \x16 arguments \x16 result
// type \x17: unit_rest writes to_silica_e_f_n(arguments, k) when the unit has it, and otherwise an ordinary call
// after which the process ends.
// Text that belongs after the function being printed (a to_silica_r_ function, a marker line) travels inside
// the expression's text between \x0e and \x0f; inline_of and hoisted_of take the two apart.

fn smode() -> string {
    "\x13S\x14"
}

fn mtype() -> string {
    "\x13M\x14"
}

fn ktype() -> string {
    "{ wait: int64, up: actor_ref }"
}

fn until(s: string, from: int64, stop: string) -> string {
    e: int64 <- ts_text@find(s, stop, from);
    case e < 0 of {
        true -> substring(s, from, length_bytes(s));
        false -> substring(s, from, e)
    }
}

// THE SESSION'S CONTEXT travels in d beside the declared types: \x1c unit name \x1f for the unit being printed
// (the newest first) and \x1d options \x1e, the hello's lowering choices as options_text writes them.
fn unit_of(d: string) -> string {
    case contains(d, "\x1c") of {
        false -> "";
        true -> until(d, ts_text@find(d, "\x1c", 0) + 1, "\x1f")
    }
}

// The session's choice for a requirement ("a5_5"), or a parameter of it ("a4_2.pool_size"); "" when not stated.
fn option(d: string, key: string) -> string {
    k: string <- ts_text@concat3("|", key, "=");
    case contains(d, k) of {
        false -> "";
        true -> until(d, ts_text@find(d, k, 0) + length_bytes(k), "|")
    }
}

fn params_options(req: string, ps: $LSS$, acc: string) -> string {
    case ps of {
        []: $LSS$ -> acc;
        [p: (string, string), t: $LSS$] -> {
            (k: string, v: string) <- p;
            params_options(req, t, concat(acc, concat(ts_text@concat4(req, ".", k, "="), concat(v, "|"))))
        }
    }
}

fn options_from(cs: $CHOICES$, acc: string) -> string {
    case cs of {
        []: $CHOICES$ -> acc;
        [c: $CHOICE$, t: $CHOICES$] -> {
            req: string <- atom_name(c.requirement);
            options_from(t, params_options(req, c.params, concat(acc, ts_text@concat4(req, "=", atom_name(c.choice), "|"))))
        }
    }
}

// The hello's lowering choices (contract 7.2) as "|a4_2=single_pool|a4_2.pool_size=1024|...".
fn options_text(cs: $CHOICES$) -> string {
    options_from(cs, "|")
}

fn local_module(c: $CTX$, m: string) -> boolean {
    length_bytes(m) == 0 or m == unit_of(c.d)
}

// The Silica name of the sender's function `name` (contract T9.11): the name itself, or with "__" appended when
// it is a Silica reserved word or builtin (or `main`); "" when it is not an identifier or starts with to_silica_.
fn printed_name(name: string) -> string {
    case ts_text@is_identifier(name) and not starts_with(name, "to_silica_") of {
        false -> "";
        true -> case contains(reserved_names(), ts_text@concat3(" ", name, " ")) of {
            true -> concat(name, "__");
            false -> name
        }
    }
}

fn hoist(text: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(text) == 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> ts_text@concat3("\x0e", text, "\x0f")
    }
}

// text without what is hoisted out of it.
fn inline_of(text: string) -> string {
    case contains(text, "\x0e") of {
        false -> text;
        true -> {
            a: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\x0e", 0);
            b: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\x0f", a);
            concat(substring(text, 0, a), inline_of(substring(text, b + 1, length_bytes(text))))
        }
    }
}

// What is hoisted out of text, in order.
fn hoisted_of(text: string) -> string {
    case contains(text, "\x0e") of {
        false -> "";
        true -> {
            a: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\x0e", 0);
            b: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\x0f", a);
            concat(substring(text, a + 1, b), hoisted_of(substring(text, b + 1, length_bytes(text))))
        }
    }
}

fn marker(kind: string, text: string) -> string {
    concat(ts_text@concat4("//@to_silica ", kind, "\t", text), "\n")
}

fn state_text(ph: string, k: string) -> string {
    concat(ts_text@concat4("{ ph: ", ph, ", k: ", k), " }")
}

fn done_state() -> string {
    state_text("(:to_silica_done, 0)", "k")
}

fn with_k(args: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(args) == 0 of {
        true -> "k";
        false -> concat(args, ", k")
    }
}

fn with_comma(items: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(items) == 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> concat(items, ", ")
    }
}

// A phase with no variables still holds one element (Silica has no tuple of one).
fn phase_alt(tag: string, types: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(types) == 0 of {
        true -> ts_text@concat3("(:", tag, ", int64)");
        false -> concat(ts_text@concat4("(:", tag, ", ", types), ")")
    }
}

fn phase_value(tag: string, texts: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(texts) == 0 of {
        true -> ts_text@concat3("(:", tag, ", 0)");
        false -> concat(ts_text@concat4("(:", tag, ", ", texts), ")")
    }
}

fn phase_pattern(tag: string, params: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(params) == 0 of {
        true -> ts_text@concat3("(:", tag, ", _z: int64)");
        false -> concat(ts_text@concat4("(:", tag, ", ", params), ")")
    }
}

// The arm of to_silica_dispatch for a process that has not started: it starts on the start message.
fn start_arm(key: string, aparams: string, anames: string) -> string {
    concat(ts_text@concat4(phase_pattern(concat("to_silica_s_", key), aparams), " -> case to_silica_is_go(msg) of { true -> to_silica_e_", key, "("),
           ts_text@concat4(with_k(anames), "); false -> ", state_text("(:to_silica_unstarted, 0)", "k"), " }"))
}

// The types whose values a process's end reports to its watcher (runtime: to_silica_result_<type>).
fn result_word(t: string) -> string {
    case t == "int64" or t == "float64" or t == "boolean" or t == "atom" or t == "string" of {
        true -> t;
        false -> ""
    }
}

// The process ends with the value `text` of type ty.
fn ending(text: string, ty: string) -> string {
    w: string <- result_word(ty);
    case length_bytes(w) == 0 of {
        true -> concat(ts_text@concat4("{ _: ", ty, " <- ", text), ts_text@concat3("; ", done_state(), " }"));
        false -> concat(ts_text@concat4("{ _: boolean <- to_silica_result_", w, "(k.up, ", text), ts_text@concat3("); ", done_state(), " }"))
    }
}

fn seen_key(name: string) -> string {
    ts_text@concat3("\x1f", name, "\x1f")
}

// THE VARIABLES LIVE AT A RECEIVE: every source variable of env that has a type, the newest binding of each. They
// are kept in the waiting phase and are the parameters a0, a1, ... of the to_silica_r_ function.
fn saved_env(env: $ENV$, seen: string, k: int64) -> $ENV$ {
    case env of {
        []: $ENV$ -> no_bindings();
        [b: (string, string, string), t: $ENV$] -> {
            (name: string, _text: string, ty: string) <- b;
            case length_bytes(ty) == 0 or contains(seen, seen_key(name)) of {
                true -> saved_env(t, seen, k);
                false -> bind(saved_env(t, concat(seen, seen_key(name)), k + 1), name, concat("a", ts_text@itoa(k)), ty)
            }
        }
    }
}

fn saved_count(env: $ENV$, seen: string, n: int64) -> int64 {
    case env of {
        []: $ENV$ -> n;
        [b: (string, string, string), t: $ENV$] -> {
            (name: string, _text: string, ty: string) <- b;
            case length_bytes(ty) == 0 or contains(seen, seen_key(name)) of {
                true -> saved_count(t, seen, n);
                false -> saved_count(t, concat(seen, seen_key(name)), n + 1)
            }
        }
    }
}

// what: 0 the texts they are printed as here, 1 their types, 2 "a0: T0", 3 "a0".
fn saved_item(what: int64, text: string, ty: string, k: int64) -> string {
    case what of {
        0 -> text;
        1 -> ty;
        2 -> ts_text@concat4("a", ts_text@itoa(k), ": ", ty);
        _: int64 -> concat("a", ts_text@itoa(k))
    }
}

fn saved_join(env: $ENV$, seen: string, k: int64, what: int64) -> string {
    case env of {
        []: $ENV$ -> "";
        [b: (string, string, string), t: $ENV$] -> {
            (name: string, text: string, ty: string) <- b;
            case length_bytes(ty) == 0 or contains(seen, seen_key(name)) of {
                true -> saved_join(t, seen, k, what);
                false -> {
                    more: string <- saved_join(t, concat(seen, seen_key(name)), k + 1, what);
                    case length_bytes(more) == 0 of {
                        true -> saved_item(what, text, ty, k);
                        false -> ts_text@concat3(saved_item(what, text, ty, k), ", ", more)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn last_of(xs: $LI$) -> int64 {
    case xs of {
        []: $LI$ -> 0 - 1;
        [x: int64, t: $LI$] -> case t of {
            []: $LI$ -> x;
            [_y: int64, _t2: $LI$] -> last_of(t)
        }
    }
}

fn receives(ns: $NODES$, acc: int64) -> int64 {
    case ns of {
        []: $NODES$ -> acc;
        [n: $NODE$, t: $NODES$] -> case n of {
            (:receive, _a: int64, _cs: $LI$, _t: int64, _b: int64) -> receives(t, acc + 1);
            _: $NODE$ -> receives(t, acc)
        }
    }
}

// True when a tail position under node i calls a function of this unit other than the one being printed.
fn tail_other(c: $CTX$, i: int64) -> boolean {
    case node_at(c.ns, i) of {
        (:block, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> tail_other(c, last_of(es));
        (:case, _a: int64, _s: int64, cs: $LI$) -> any_tail_other(c, cs);
        (:cond, _a: int64, cs: $LI$) -> any_tail_other(c, cs);
        (:receive, _a: int64, cs: $LI$, _t: int64, b: int64) -> case b < 0 of {
            true -> any_tail_other(c, cs);
            false -> any_tail_other(c, cs) or tail_other(c, b)
        };
        (:clause, _a: int64, _ps: $LI$, _g: int64, b: int64) -> tail_other(c, b);
        (:loop_hint, _a: int64, b: int64) -> tail_other(c, b);
        (:call, _a: int64, m: string, f: string, as: $LI$) -> local_module(c, m) and not (ts_text@concat3(f, "_", ts_text@itoa(count(as, 0))) == c.f);
        _: $NODE$ -> false
    }
}

fn any_tail_other(c: $CTX$, cs: $LI$) -> boolean {
    case cs of {
        []: $LI$ -> false;
        [k: int64, rest: $LI$] -> case tail_other(c, k) of {
            true -> true;
            false -> any_tail_other(c, rest)
        }
    }
}

// (:self) is printed in expr1. (:spawn, fun, args, link): a new process that runs a function of this unit.
// The function is named by a (:fun_ref) with the spawn's args, or by a (:lambda) of no parameters whose body is
// one call. The answer's name is "" when the spawn is neither.
fn spawn_call(c: $CTX$, b: int64) -> { name: string, args: $LI$ } {
    case node_at(c.ns, b) of {
        (:call, _a: int64, m: string, name: string, as: $LI$) -> case local_module(c, m) of {
            true -> { name: name, args: as };
            false -> { name: "", args: none_i() }
        };
        (:block, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> case count(es, 0) == 1 of {
            true -> spawn_call(c, first_of(es));
            false -> { name: "", args: none_i() }
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> { name: "", args: none_i() }
    }
}

fn spawn_target(c: $CTX$, f: int64, as: $LI$) -> { name: string, args: $LI$ } {
    case node_at(c.ns, f) of {
        (:fun_ref, _a: int64, m: string, name: string, arity: int64) -> case local_module(c, m) and arity == count(as, 0) of {
            true -> { name: name, args: as };
            false -> { name: "", args: none_i() }
        };
        (:lambda, _a: int64, cls: $LI$) -> case count(cls, 0) == 1 and count(as, 0) == 0 of {
            false -> { name: "", args: none_i() };
            true -> case node_at(c.ns, first_of(cls)) of {
                (:clause, _a2: int64, ps: $LI$, g: int64, b: int64) -> case count(ps, 0) == 0 and g < 0 of {
                    true -> spawn_call(c, b);
                    false -> { name: "", args: none_i() }
                };
                _: $NODE$ -> { name: "", args: none_i() }
            }
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> { name: "", args: none_i() }
    }
}

fn spawn_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, f: int64, as: $LI$, linked: boolean, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    tg: { name: string, args: $LI$ } <- spawn_target(c, f, as);
    n: int64 <- count(tg.args, 0);
    key: string <- ts_text@concat3(tg.name, "_", ts_text@itoa(n));
    tag: string <- concat("to_silica_s_", key);
    case linked of {
        true -> no("(:spawn) with link true", i, concat(ts_text@concat3("a link has no lowering under the session's choice a5_5 ", option(c.d, "a5_5"), ""), ": BEES A5.5 supervisor_request sends only exit requests to a supervisor, and silica_link is not built (Silica admits link only directly in a behaviour, and what a linked actor receives when its partner ends is not written); trapping exits has no node"));
        false -> case length_bytes(printed_name(tg.name)) == 0 or n > 7 of {
            true -> no("(:spawn)", i, "only a function of this unit is spawned, named by a (:fun_ref) or by a (:lambda) of no parameters whose body is one call to it, with at most seven arguments; any other fun needs closures (not printed)");
            false -> {
                items: $EX$ <- items_ex(c, tg.args, none_of(), 0, env);
                case bad(items.text) of {
                    true -> items;
                    false -> case n > 0 and length_bytes(items.type) == 0 of {
                        true -> miss("an argument of the (:spawn)", i, "e");
                        false -> { text: concat(ts_text@concat3("to_silica_spawn(", phase_value(tag, items.text), ")"),
                                                hoist(marker("spawn", concat(ts_text@concat4(key, "\t", tg.name, "/"), concat(ts_text@concat4(ts_text@itoa(n), "\t", printed_name(tg.name), "\t"), phase_alt(tag, items.type)))))),
                                   type: "actor_ref" }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// The message node m of a send as { text, type }: text is the M value that is cast, type the alternative of M
// it adds ("" for a symbol, which travels as (:to_silica_sym, symbol)).
fn message_ex(c: $CTX$, m: int64, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    x: $EX$ <- expr(c, m, env, "");
    case bad(x.text) of {
        true -> x;
        false -> case x.type == "atom" of {
            true -> { text: ts_text@concat3("(:to_silica_sym, ", x.text, ")"), type: "" };
            false -> case starts_with(x.type, "(:") and count_s(split_top(x.type, 124), 0) == 1 of {
                true -> x;
                // a hint that states a whole sum of tagged tuples (a typed language's message type): the message
                // is the alternative of the tuple's own tag and size
                false -> case length_bytes(message_alt(c, m, x.type)) > 0 of {
                  true -> { text: x.text, type: message_alt(c, m, x.type) };
                  // a (:symbol) whose hint states a whole sum that has the symbol (a typed language's message type
                  // with a constructor of no fields): it travels as every symbol does (contract T9.12)
                  false -> case length_bytes(symbol_alt(c, m, x.type)) > 0 of {
                   true -> { text: ts_text@concat3("(:to_silica_sym, ", symbol_alt(c, m, x.type), ")"), type: "" };
                   false -> case length_bytes(x.type) == 0 of {
                    true -> miss(ts_text@concat3("the message ", node_label(c, m), " of a send"), m, "e");
                    false -> no(ts_text@concat3("the message ", node_label(c, m), " of a send"), m, ts_text@concat3("its stated type is ", x.type, ": only a symbol, or a tuple whose first element is a symbol with a (:t_tagged) hint (or a sum that has that tagged tuple), is sent (the messages of a unit's processes are one Silica sum of tagged tuples)"))
                   }
                  }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn alt_for(alts: $LS$, arity: int64, tag: string) -> string {
    case alts of {
        []: $LS$ -> "";
        [a: string, rest: $LS$] -> case starts_with(a, ts_text@concat3("(", tag, ",")) and count_s(tuple_elems(a), 0) == arity of {
            true -> a;
            false -> alt_for(rest, arity, tag)
        }
    }
}

// The alternative of the sum ty that the (:tuple) node m is: the tagged tuple of its first element's symbol and
// its size; "" when m is no such tuple or ty has no such alternative.
fn message_alt(c: $CTX$, m: int64, ty: string) -> string {
    case node_at(c.ns, m) of {
        (:tuple, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> case length_bytes(tag_of(c.ns, es)) == 0 of {
            true -> "";
            false -> alt_for(split_top(ty, 124), count(es, 0), tag_of(c.ns, es))
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> ""
    }
}

fn has_alt(alts: $LS$, a: string) -> boolean {
    case alts of {
        []: $LS$ -> false;
        [h: string, rest: $LS$] -> case h == a of {
            true -> true;
            false -> has_alt(rest, a)
        }
    }
}

// The alternative of the sum ty that the (:symbol) node m is: its atom, when ty is a sum that has it; "" when m
// is no symbol or ty has no such alternative.
fn symbol_alt(c: $CTX$, m: int64, ty: string) -> string {
    case node_at(c.ns, m) of {
        (:symbol, _a: int64, name: string) -> case ts_text@is_identifier(name) and has_alt(split_top(ty, 124), concat(":", name)) of {
            true -> concat(":", name);
            false -> ""
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> ""
    }
}

// (:send, to, message). statement: its value is not used, and the text is the cast (a boolean). Otherwise its
// value is the message (contract H22), which is then written a second time: only a message with no call in it is
// printed so, and a hint on the send, or its place (want), that states another type is inconsistent typing.
// named: "" for a (:send); for a (:send_named) the registered name, and dest is not looked at.
fn send_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, named: string, dest: int64, m: int64, env: $ENV$, statement: boolean, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    tx: $EX$ <- case length_bytes(named) == 0 of {
        true -> expr(c, dest, env, "");
        false -> { text: concat(":", named), type: "actor_ref" }
    };
    send_fn: string <- case length_bytes(named) == 0 of {
        true -> "to_silica_send(";
        false -> "to_silica_send_named("
    };
    mx: $EX$ <- message_ex(c, m, env);
    vx: $EX$ <- expr(c, m, env, "");
    h: string <- hint_text(c, i);
    // what the send's own hint, or its place, states for its value
    stated: string <- case length_bytes(h) == 0 or bad(h) of {
        true -> want;
        false -> h
    };
    sent: string <- concat(concat(ts_text@concat4(send_fn, tx.text, ", ", mx.text), ")"), case length_bytes(mx.type) == 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> hoist(marker("msg", mx.type))
    });
    case bad(tx.text) of {
        true -> tx;
        false -> case bad(mx.text) of {
            true -> mx;
            false -> case tx.type == "actor_ref" of {
                false -> case length_bytes(tx.type) == 0 of {
                    true -> miss(ts_text@concat3("the process ", node_label(c, dest), " a message is sent to"), dest, "e");
                    false -> clash(ts_text@concat3("the process ", node_label(c, dest), " a message is sent to"), dest, ts_text@concat3("its stated type is ", tx.type, ", which is not a process reference (:t_actor)"))
                };
                true -> case statement of {
                    true -> { text: sent, type: "boolean" };
                    false -> case length_bytes(stated) == 0 or contains(stated, vx.type) or (vx.type == "atom" and starts_with(stated, ":")) of {
                        false -> clash("the (:send) whose value is used", i, concat(ts_text@concat4("its value is the message (contract H22), of the type ", vx.type, ", and its hint or its place states ", stated), ": a language whose send has another value sends the (:send) as a statement of a (:block), followed by that value"));
                        true -> case contains(substring(vx.text, 1, length_bytes(vx.text)), "(") of {
                            true -> no("a (:send) whose value is used", i, "the message holds a call, and the send's value is the message: it would be evaluated twice");
                            false -> { text: concat(ts_text@concat4("{ _: boolean <- ", sent, "; ", vx.text), " }"), type: vx.type }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// (:send_named, name, message) (contract H39, T9.14c): a send to a registered name, which is the name of a
// static child (T9.14b). It is a (:send) in everything but its destination.
fn send_named_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, name: string, m: int64, env: $ENV$, statement: boolean, want: string) -> $EX$ {
    case ts_text@is_identifier(name) and not starts_with(name, "to_silica_") of {
        true -> send_ex(c, i, name, 0 - 1, m, env, statement, want);
        false -> no("(:send_named)", i, ts_text@concat3("the name ", name, " is not an identifier, or starts with to_silica_: a registered name is written as a Silica atom"))
    }
}

// The restart policy an A4.4 override on node i states (contract T7.6): the value of its parameter key, "" when
// the node has no such override or the override has no such parameter.
fn param_of(ps: $LSS$, key: string) -> string {
    case ps of {
        []: $LSS$ -> "";
        [p: (string, string), t: $LSS$] -> {
            (k: string, v: string) <- p;
            case k == key of {
                true -> v;
                false -> param_of(t, key)
            }
        }
    }
}

fn override_a4_4(os: $OVERRIDES$, i: int64, key: string) -> string {
    case os of {
        []: $OVERRIDES$ -> "";
        [o: $OVERRIDE$, t: $OVERRIDES$] -> case o.node == i and o.requirement == :a4_4 of {
            true -> param_of(o.detail.params, key);
            false -> override_a4_4(t, i, key)
        }
    }
}

// True when every node of es is a literal the supervisor's child list can hold: an integer, a float, a symbol
// or a boolean.
fn all_literals(ns: $NODES$, es: $LI$) -> boolean {
    case es of {
        []: $LI$ -> true;
        [e: int64, t: $LI$] -> case node_at(ns, e) of {
            (:int, _a: int64, _v: int64) -> all_literals(ns, t);
            (:float, _a: int64, _v: string) -> all_literals(ns, t);
            (:symbol, _a: int64, _v: string) -> all_literals(ns, t);
            (:boolean, _a: int64, _v: boolean) -> all_literals(ns, t);
            _: $NODE$ -> false
        }
    }
}

// (:register, name, process) (contract H38, T9.14b): written only when process is a (:spawn) of a function of
// this unit whose arguments are literals. That is a STATIC CHILD: it stands in the child list the unit's
// supervisor has from its start (the marker line `static`, which unit_rest writes into init), with the child id
// `name`, under which Silica registers it, and the restart policy of the A4.4 override on the (:spawn) (contract
// T7.6), or else the session's. Where the node stands the child is sent its start message (to_silica_static); the
// value is true. The unit has one supervisor and so one strategy, the session's: an override that states another
// is reported (T2001) and not followed.
fn register_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, name: string, p: int64, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    case node_at(c.ns, p) of {
        (:spawn, _a: int64, f: int64, as: $LI$, linked: boolean) -> {
            sx: $EX$ <- spawn_ex(c, p, f, as, linked, env);
            tg: { name: string, args: $LI$ } <- spawn_target(c, f, as);
            over: string <- override_a4_4(c.os, p, "restart");
            restart: string <- case length_bytes(over) == 0 of {
                true -> option_or(c.d, "a4_4.restart", "transient");
                false -> over
            };
            strategy: string <- override_a4_4(c.os, p, "strategy");
            call: string <- inline_of(sx.text);
            case bad(sx.text) of {
                true -> sx;
                false -> case ts_text@is_identifier(name) and not starts_with(name, "to_silica_") of {
                    false -> no("(:register)", i, ts_text@concat3("the name ", name, " is not an identifier, or starts with to_silica_: a static child's name is its child id, a Silica atom"));
                    true -> case all_literals(c.ns, tg.args) of {
                        false -> no("(:register) of a (:spawn)", i, "an argument of the spawn is not a literal (an integer, a float, a symbol or a boolean): a static child stands in the child list the supervisor has from its start, and nothing computed when the program runs can stand there (contract T9.14b)");
                        true -> case restart == "permanent" or restart == "transient" or restart == "temporary" of {
                            false -> no("(:register) of a (:spawn)", i, ts_text@concat3("its A4.4 override states the restart policy ", restart, ", which is not permanent, transient or temporary"));
                            true -> { text: concat(ts_text@concat3("to_silica_static(:", name, ")"),
                                                   hoist(concat(concat(hoisted_of(sx.text), marker("static", concat(ts_text@concat4(name, "\t", restart, "\t"), substring(call, 16, length_bytes(call) - 1)))),
                                                                case length_bytes(strategy) == 0 or strategy == option_or(c.d, "a4_4.strategy", "one_for_one") of {
                                                                    true -> "";
                                                                    false -> concat(ts_text@concat4("// to-silica: CHOICE the a4_4 override of the static child ", name, " states the strategy ", strategy), concat(ts_text@concat3(", which is not followed: a unit has one supervisor, whose strategy is the session's (", option_or(c.d, "a4_4.strategy", "one_for_one"), ")"), "\n"))
                                                                }))),
                                      type: "boolean" }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> no("(:register)", i, "its process is not a (:spawn): a name is given only to a static child, a (:register) whose process is a (:spawn) of a function of this unit with literal arguments (contract T9.14b); a process that is running is not given a name (Silica registers a supervised actor under its child id, which is fixed when it is added)")
    }
}

// (:exit_signal, to, reason): an exit request to another process, under the session's choice a5_5
// supervisor_request (BEES A5.5): the unit's supervisor ends the process, which is not started again. The reason
// must be a (:symbol): `normal` does nothing (a process that does not trap exits takes no notice of it, and
// trapping exits has no node); with any other the process ends. The reason itself is not carried (BEES A5.5,
// open): what the supervisor's report says of the process's end is Silica's, and nothing that is printed can
// observe it (links and monitors are not). The value is true.
fn exit_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, dest: int64, r: int64, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    tx: $EX$ <- expr(c, dest, env, "");
    choice: string <- option(c.d, "a5_5");
    case node_at(c.ns, r) of {
        (:symbol, _a: int64, name: string) -> case bad(tx.text) of {
            true -> tx;
            false -> case tx.type == "actor_ref" of {
                false -> case length_bytes(tx.type) == 0 of {
                    true -> miss(ts_text@concat3("the process ", node_label(c, dest), " of an exit request"), dest, "e");
                    false -> clash(ts_text@concat3("the process ", node_label(c, dest), " of an exit request"), dest, ts_text@concat3("its stated type is ", tx.type, ", which is not a process reference (:t_actor)"))
                };
                true -> case choice == "supervisor_request" of {
                    false -> no("(:exit_signal)", i, ts_text@concat3("the session's choice a5_5 is ", choice, ": an exit request is written only under supervisor_request (a request to the unit's supervisor, BEES A5.5); silica_link is not built"));
                    true -> case name == "normal" of {
                        true -> { text: ts_text@concat3("{ _: actor_ref <- ", tx.text, "; true }"), type: "boolean" };
                        false -> { text: ts_text@concat3("to_silica_exit(", tx.text, ")"), type: "boolean" }
                    }
                }
            }
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> no("(:exit_signal)", i, "its reason is not a (:symbol): whether the request does nothing (normal) or ends the process must be known when the unit is written, and no reason is carried to the process (BEES A5.5, open)")
    }
}

// ---- tail mode: the expression's value is the process's next state

fn tail_value(c: $CTX$, i: int64, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    x: $EX$ <- expr(c, i, env, "");
    case bad(x.text) of {
        true -> x;
        false -> case length_bytes(x.type) == 0 of {
            true -> miss(ts_text@concat3("the value ", node_label(c, i), " the process ends with"), i, "e");
            false -> { text: ending(x.text, x.type), type: smode() }
        }
    }
}

fn tail_call(c: $CTX$, i: int64, m: string, f: string, as: $LI$, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    n: int64 <- count(as, 0);
    key: string <- ts_text@concat3(f, "_", ts_text@itoa(n));
    h: string <- hint_text(c, i);
    case local_module(c, m) and length_bytes(printed_name(f)) > 0 and n <= 7 of {
        false -> tail_value(c, i, env);
        true -> {
            b: $EX$ <- bound_args(c, i, as, env, 0);
            call: string <- case key == c.f of {
                true -> concat(ts_text@concat4("to_silica_e_", key, "(", with_k(b.text)), ")");
                false -> concat(ts_text@concat4("\x15", key, "\x16", printed_name(f)), concat(ts_text@concat4("\x16", b.text, "\x16", case bad(h) of {
                    true -> "";
                    false -> h
                }), "\x17"))
            };
            case bad(b.text) of {
                true -> { text: b.text, type: "" };
                false -> { text: case length_bytes(b.type) == 0 of {
                               true -> call;
                               false -> ts_text@concat4("{ ", b.type, call, " }")
                           },
                           type: smode() }
            }
        }
    }
}

// (:fail, reason) in tail position: the actor ends with the reason when it is a symbol (fail_self in the
// behaviour); any other reason is not carried (the failing expression, as in an ordinary function).
fn tail_fail(c: $CTX$, i: int64, r: int64) -> $EX$ {
    case node_at(c.ns, r) of {
        (:symbol, _a: int64, name: string) -> case ts_text@is_identifier(name) of {
            true -> { text: state_text(ts_text@concat3("(:to_silica_failed, :", name, ")"), "k"), type: smode() };
            false -> { text: fail_text(smode(), i), type: smode() }
        };
        _: $NODE$ -> { text: fail_text(smode(), i), type: smode() }
    }
}

fn tail_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    case node_at(c.ns, i) of {
        (:block, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> case count(es, 0) == 1 of {
            true -> tail_ex(c, first_of(es), env);
            false -> {
                b: $EX$ <- block(c, i, es, env, smode());
                { text: ts_text@concat3("{ ", b.text, " }"), type: b.type }
            }
        };
        (:case, _a: int64, s: int64, cs: $LI$) -> case_ex(c, i, s, cs, env, smode());
        (:cond, _a: int64, cs: $LI$) -> chain(c, cs, no_pairs(), env, smode());
        (:loop_hint, _a: int64, b: int64) -> tail_ex(c, b, env);
        (:receive, _a: int64, cs: $LI$, t: int64, b: int64) -> receive_ex(c, i, cs, t, b, env);
        (:call, _a: int64, m: string, f: string, as: $LI$) -> tail_call(c, i, m, f, as, env);
        (:fail, _a: int64, r: int64) -> tail_fail(c, i, r);
        (:gap_node, _a: int64, construct: string, note: string) -> { text: gap(construct, i, "T4001", note), type: "" };
        _: $NODE$ -> tail_value(c, i, env)
    }
}

// One arm of a to_silica_r_ function. in_guard: the guard uses a variable of the pattern, so it is a Silica
// guard; any other guard is tested inside the arm, and the arms after it are written a second time there.
fn guarded_arm(pt: string, gt: string, in_guard: boolean, body: string, more: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(gt) == 0 of {
        true -> concat(ts_text@concat4(pt, " -> ", body, "; "), more);
        false -> case in_guard of {
            true -> concat(concat(ts_text@concat4(pt, " if ", gt, " -> "), body), concat("; ", more));
            false -> concat(concat(ts_text@concat4(pt, " -> case ", gt, " of { true -> "), ts_text@concat4(body, "; false -> case msg of { ", inline_of(more), " } }")), concat("; ", more))
        }
    }
}

// A receive clause: its message pattern p is a symbol, or a tuple that starts with a symbol and has a
// (:t_tagged) hint (contract T8.9 note 3, T8.16: the hint is the type of the messages the clause takes).
fn receive_arm(c: $CTX$, p: int64, g: int64, b: int64, rest: $LI$, env: $ENV$, closing: string) -> $EX$ {
    more: $EX$ <- receive_arms(c, rest, env, closing);
    case node_at(c.ns, p) of {
        (:symbol, _a: int64, name: string) -> {
            body: $EX$ <- expr(c, b, env, smode());
            { text: guarded_arm(ts_text@concat3("(:to_silica_sym, ", symbol_text(name, p), ")"), guard_text(c, g, env), false, body.text, more.text), type: more.type }
        };
        (:tuple, _a: int64, es: $LI$) -> {
            ty: string <- hint_text(c, p);
            case length_bytes(ty) == 0 of {
                true -> miss("the message pattern (:tuple) of a receive clause", p, "e");
                false -> case bad(ty) of {
                    true -> { text: at_node(ty, p), type: "" };
                    false -> case length_bytes(tag_of(c.ns, es)) > 0 and starts_with(ty, ts_text@concat3("(", tag_of(c.ns, es), ",")) and count_s(split_top(ty, 124), 0) == 1 of {
                        false -> no("the message pattern (:tuple) of a receive clause", p, ts_text@concat3("its hint states the type ", ty, ": only a tuple whose first element is a symbol, with a (:t_tagged) hint of that symbol, is taken as a message (the messages of a unit's processes are one Silica sum of tagged tuples)"));
                        true -> {
                            e2: $ENV$ <- pat_env(c, p, ty, "", env);
                            body: $EX$ <- expr(c, b, e2, smode());
                            gt: string <- guard_text(c, g, e2);
                            { text: guarded_arm(pat_text(c, p, ty, "", concat(gt, body.text)), gt, names_used(c.ns, one(p), gt), body.text, more.text), type: concat(marker("msg", ty), more.type) }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        };
        (:gap_node, _a: int64, construct: string, note: string) -> { text: gap(construct, p, "T4001", note), type: "" };
        other: $NODE$ -> {
            (kind: string, _at: int64) <- node_info(other);
            no(ts_text@concat3("the message pattern (:", kind, ") of a receive clause"), p, "only a symbol, or a tuple whose first element is a symbol, is taken as a message: a variable or _ would take any message, and the messages of a unit's processes are one Silica sum of tagged tuples, which no sender's type names")
        }
    }
}

// The arms for the receive clauses cs, then closing (the timeout arm, if any, and the arm for a message no clause
// takes). The answer's type holds the marker lines of the message alternatives the clauses take.
fn receive_arms(c: $CTX$, cs: $LI$, env: $ENV$, closing: string) -> $EX$ {
    case cs of {
        []: $LI$ -> { text: closing, type: "" };
        [k: int64, rest: $LI$] -> case node_at(c.ns, k) of {
            (:clause, _a: int64, ps: $LI$, g: int64, b: int64) -> case count(ps, 0) == 1 of {
                false -> no("a receive clause", k, "it does not have exactly one pattern (the message)");
                true -> receive_arm(c, first_of(ps), g, b, rest, env, closing)
            };
            (:gap_node, _a: int64, construct: string, note: string) -> { text: gap(construct, k, "T4001", note), type: "" };
            _: $NODE$ -> no("a receive clause", k, "the node is not a (:clause)")
        }
    }
}

// (:receive, clauses, timeout, after) in tail position (BEES A3.3 phase_field): the function ends here with the
// state "waiting in this receive"; the clauses become the function to_silica_r_<f>_<n>_<node>, hoisted.
fn receive_ex(c: $CTX$, i: int64, cs: $LI$, t: int64, b: int64, env: $ENV$) -> $EX$ {
    base: string <- ts_text@concat3(c.f, "_", ts_text@itoa(i));
    tag: string <- concat("to_silica_w_", base);
    env2: $ENV$ <- saved_env(env, "", 0);
    timed: boolean <- t >= 0 and b >= 0;
    closing: string <- concat(case timed of {
        true -> ts_text@concat3("(:to_silica_timeout, r_: int64) if r_ == k.wait -> ", expr(c, b, env2, smode()).text, "; ");
        false -> ""
    }, ts_text@concat4("_: ", mtype(), " -> ", state_text("(:to_silica_nomatch, 0)", "k")));
    arms: $EX$ <- receive_arms(c, cs, env2, closing);
    tm: $EX$ <- case timed of {
        true -> expr(c, t, env, "int64");
        false -> { text: "", type: "int64" }
    };
    here: string <- state_text(phase_value(tag, saved_join(env, "", 0, 0)), case timed of {
        true -> ts_text@concat3("{ wait: to_silica_arm(", tm.text, ", k.wait + 1), up: k.up }");
        false -> "k"
    });
    rfn: string <- concat(concat(ts_text@concat4("fn to_silica_r_", base, "(msg: ", mtype()), ts_text@concat4(", ", with_comma(saved_join(env, "", 0, 2)), "k: ", ktype())),
                          concat(ts_text@concat4(") -> ", smode(), " {\n    case msg of { ", inline_of(arms.text)), " }\n}\n"));
    marks: string <- concat(concat(marker("ph", phase_alt(tag, saved_join(env, "", 0, 1))),
                                   marker("arm", concat(ts_text@concat4(phase_pattern(tag, saved_join(env, "", 0, 2)), " -> to_silica_r_", base, "(msg, "), ts_text@concat3(with_comma(saved_join(env, "", 0, 3)), "k", ")")))),
                            arms.type);
    case length_bytes(c.f) == 0 of {
        true -> no("(:receive)", i, "it is not in tail position of its function: the sender must split the function at this receive (contract T9.13a)");
        false -> case saved_count(env, "", 0) > 6 of {
            true -> no("(:receive)", i, "more than six variables are live at it: they are the parameters of the function its clauses become, and Silica allows eight (packing them is not built)");
            false -> case bad(arms.text) of {
                true -> arms;
                false -> case bad(tm.text) of {
                    true -> tm;
                    false -> case is_int_type(tm.type) of {
                        false -> clash("the timeout of a (:receive)", t, ts_text@concat3("its stated type is ", tm.type, ", which is not an integer (milliseconds, contract H23)"));
                        true -> { text: concat(here, concat(hoist(concat(marks, rfn)), hoist(hoisted_of(arms.text)))), type: smode() }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn a_params(ts: $TYPES$, ps: $LI$, k: int64, acc: string, d: string) -> string {
    case ps of {
        []: $LI$ -> acc;
        [p: int64, t: $LI$] -> {
            item: string <- ts_text@concat4("a", ts_text@itoa(k), ": ", type_text(ts, p, false, d));
            case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
                true -> a_params(ts, t, k + 1, item, d);
                false -> a_params(ts, t, k + 1, ts_text@concat3(acc, ", ", item), d)
            }
        }
    }
}

// "p0, p1, ..." (n names).
fn name_list(prefix: string, k: int64, n: int64) -> string {
    case k >= n of {
        true -> "";
        false -> case k + 1 >= n of {
            true -> concat(prefix, ts_text@itoa(k));
            false -> ts_text@concat4(prefix, ts_text@itoa(k), ", ", name_list(prefix, k + 1, n))
        }
    }
}

// The spawn functions of a function that can run as a process: <name>__spawn(args) and, for a Silica caller
// that wants the value the process ends with, <name>__spawn_watched(args, up) (the value is sent to up as
// (:to_silica_result_<type>, value) when its type is int64, float64, boolean, atom or string).
fn spawn_functions(name: string, key: string, plist: string, n: int64, exported: boolean) -> $EX$ {
    value: string <- phase_value(concat("to_silica_s_", key), name_list("p", 0, n));
    plain: string <- concat(ts_text@concat4("fn ", name, "__spawn(", plist), ts_text@concat3(") -> actor_ref {\n    to_silica_spawn(", value, ")\n}\n"));
    watched: string <- case n < 8 of {
        true -> concat(ts_text@concat4("fn ", name, "__spawn_watched(", with_comma(plist)), ts_text@concat3("up: actor_ref) -> actor_ref {\n    to_silica_spawn_watched(", value, ", up)\n}\n"));
        false -> ""
    };
    { text: concat(plain, watched),
      type: case exported of {
          false -> "";
          true -> concat(concat(ts_text@concat4("export ", name, "__spawn/", ts_text@itoa(n)), ";\n"), case n < 8 of {
              true -> concat(ts_text@concat4("export ", name, "__spawn_watched/", ts_text@itoa(n + 1)), ";\n");
              false -> ""
          })
      } }
}

// The function f printed in tail mode, as { text, type }: text is to_silica_e_<f>_<n> with its markers, the
// functions hoisted out of it and its spawn functions (a mark when something in it is not printed); type is the
// export lines of the spawn functions.
fn process_source(f: $FUNCTION$, c: $CTX$, ps: $LI$) -> $EX$ {
    n: int64 <- count(ps, 0);
    plist: string <- params_text(f.types, ps, 0, "", c.d);
    body: $EX$ <- chain(c, f.code.clauses, param_subjects(f.types, ps, 0, c.d), no_bindings(), smode());
    tag: string <- concat("to_silica_s_", c.f);
    sp: $EX$ <- spawn_functions(printed_name(f.head.name), c.f, plist, n, f.head.exported);
    case bad(body.text) of {
        true -> body;
        false -> case n > 7 of {
            true -> no("the process function", 0 - 1, "it has more than seven parameters (Silica allows eight, and one carries the process's own data)");
            false -> { text: concat(concat(concat(marker("proc", c.f), marker("ph", phase_alt(tag, type_items(f.types, ps, "", ", ", false, c.d)))),
                                           concat(marker("arm", start_arm(c.f, a_params(f.types, ps, 0, "", c.d), name_list("a", 0, n))),
                                                  concat(ts_text@concat4("fn to_silica_e_", c.f, "(", with_comma(plist)), ts_text@concat4("k: ", ktype(), ") -> ", smode())))),
                                    concat(concat(ts_text@concat3(" {\n    ", inline_of(body.text), "\n}\n"), hoisted_of(body.text)), sp.text)),
                       type: sp.type }
        }
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ diagnostics

fn find_char(s: string, ch: string, i: int64, n: int64) -> int64 {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> n;
        false -> case substring(s, i, i + 1) == ch of {
            true -> i;
            false -> find_char(s, ch, i + 1, n)
        }
    }
}

fn number_from(s: string, i: int64, n: int64, acc: int64) -> int64 {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> number_from(s, i + 1, n, acc * 10 + (byte_in(s, i) - 48))
    }
}

// The decimal number s (as ts_text@itoa writes it).
fn number(s: string) -> int64 {
    case starts_with(s, "-") of {
        true -> 0 - number_from(s, 1, length_bytes(s), 0);
        false -> number_from(s, 0, length_bytes(s), 0)
    }
}

// The first mark of text (see gap), which must hold one.
fn first_gap(text: string) -> $STOPPED$ {
    n: int64 <- length_chars(text);
    a: int64 <- find_char(text, "\x01", 0, n);
    b: int64 <- find_char(text, "\x02", a, n);
    d: int64 <- find_char(text, "\x02", b + 1, n);
    e: int64 <- find_char(text, "\x02", d + 1, n);
    z: int64 <- find_char(text, "\x03", e, n);
    case z < n of {
        true -> { construct: substring(text, a + 1, b), node: number(substring(text, b + 1, d)), code: substring(text, d + 1, e), note: substring(text, e + 1, z) };
        false -> { construct: "a construct", node: 0 - 1, code: "T4002", note: "the printer could not say which" }
    }
}

// What the diagnostic says: the construct, its node, and why it is not printed.
fn why_text(g: $STOPPED$) -> string {
    where: string <- case g.node < 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> concat(" at node ", ts_text@itoa(g.node))
    };
    case g.code == "T4001" of {
        true -> concat(ts_text@concat4("the sender sent a gap", where, ": ", g.construct), ts_text@concat3(" (", g.note, ")"));
        false -> case g.code == "T4002" of {
            true -> ts_text@concat4(g.construct, where, " is not printed: ", g.note);
            false -> ts_text@concat4(g.construct, where, ": ", g.note)
        }
    }
}

// The place of node (or of the first clause, when node is -1) in the sender's source.
fn place(file: string, locations: $LII$, ns: $NODES$, node: int64, clauses: $LI$) -> { file: string, line: int64, column: int64 } {
    target: int64 <- case node < 0 of {
        true -> first_of(clauses);
        false -> node
    };
    (_kind: string, at: int64) <- node_info(node_at(ns, target));
    found: (int64, int64) <- case at < 0 of {
        true -> (0, 0);
        false -> location_at(locations, at)
    };
    (line: int64, column: int64) <- found;
    { file: file, line: line, column: column }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ forms

fn refused(sig: string, code: string, why: string, at: { file: string, line: int64, column: int64 }) -> $PRINTED$ {
    { ok: false, stub: false, exports: "", text: "", sig: sig, code: code, why: why, at: at, decl: "" }
}

// A function that does not receive: an ordinary Silica function. When a tail position of it calls another
// function of the unit, it is also printed in tail mode (to_silica_e_...), so that a process can go on in it.
fn plain_function(f: $FUNCTION$, c: $CTX$, ps: $LI$, plist: string, rtype: string, start: { file: string, line: int64, column: int64 }) -> $PRINTED$ {
    arity: int64 <- count(ps, 0);
    name: string <- printed_name(f.head.name);
    sig: string <- ts_text@concat3(f.head.name, "/", ts_text@itoa(f.head.arity));
    body: $EX$ <- chain(c, f.code.clauses, param_subjects(f.types, ps, 0, c.d), no_bindings(), rtype);
    head: string <- concat(ts_text@concat4("fn ", name, "(", plist), ts_text@concat3(") -> ", rtype, " {\n    "));
    exports: string <- case f.head.exported of {
        true -> concat(ts_text@concat4("export ", name, "/", ts_text@itoa(arity)), ";\n");
        false -> ""
    };
    case bad(body.text) of {
        false -> {
            pv: $EX$ <- case any_tail_other(c, f.code.clauses) of {
                true -> process_source(f, c, ps);
                false -> { text: "", type: "" }
            };
            also: boolean <- length_bytes(pv.text) > 0 and not bad(pv.text);
            { ok: true, stub: false,
              exports: concat(exports, case also of {
                  true -> pv.type;
                  false -> ""
              }),
              text: concat(concat(ts_text@concat3(head, inline_of(body.text), "\n}\n"), hoisted_of(body.text)), case also of {
                  true -> pv.text;
                  false -> ""
              }),
              sig: sig, code: "", why: "", at: start, decl: "" }
        };
        true -> {
            g: $STOPPED$ <- first_gap(body.text);
            dv: string <- default_value(rtype);
            at: { file: string, line: int64, column: int64 } <- place(f.head.file, f.code.locations, f.code.nodes, g.node, f.code.clauses);
            case length_bytes(dv) == 0 of {
                true -> refused(sig, g.code, concat(why_text(g), "; no stub can be written, because the printer has no value of its result type"), at);
                false -> { ok: false, stub: true, exports: exports, text: concat(head, ts_text@concat3("_: int64 <- to_silica_gap(0);\n    ", dv, "\n}\n")), sig: sig, code: g.code, why: why_text(g), at: at, decl: "" }
            }
        }
    }
}

// A function that receives: it runs only as a process (app design 5.5). Its text is to_silica_e_<f>_<n> and what
// belongs to it; under its own name stands a failing stub (when its result type can be written), so that an
// ordinary call of it compiles. code T4004 with ok true: it is written, with a warning (the answer's why).
fn process_function(f: $FUNCTION$, c: $CTX$, ps: $LI$, plist: string, rtype: string, start: { file: string, line: int64, column: int64 }) -> $PRINTED$ {
    arity: int64 <- count(ps, 0);
    name: string <- printed_name(f.head.name);
    sig: string <- ts_text@concat3(f.head.name, "/", ts_text@itoa(f.head.arity));
    pv: $EX$ <- process_source(f, c, ps);
    dv: string <- case bad(rtype) of {
        true -> "";
        false -> default_value(rtype)
    };
    exports: string <- case f.head.exported and length_bytes(dv) > 0 of {
        true -> concat(ts_text@concat4("export ", name, "/", ts_text@itoa(arity)), ";\n");
        false -> ""
    };
    stub: string <- case length_bytes(dv) == 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> concat(concat(ts_text@concat4("fn ", name, "(", plist), ts_text@concat3(") -> ", rtype, " {\n    ")), ts_text@concat3("_: int64 <- to_silica_gap(0);\n    ", dv, "\n}\n"))
    };
    loose: boolean <- receives(f.code.nodes, 0) > 1 or any_tail_other(c, f.code.clauses);
    case bad(pv.text) of {
        false -> { ok: true, stub: false, exports: concat(exports, pv.type),
                   text: concat(concat(concat(ts_text@concat3("// ", sig, " receives: it runs as a process. Called as an ordinary function it fails.\n"),
                                              concat(marker("receives", ts_text@concat3(sig, "\t", name)), case length_bytes(stub) == 0 of {
                                                  // no stub can stand under its name: a function that calls it is made a stub (fix_missing)
                                                  true -> marker("nostub", f.head.name);
                                                  false -> ""
                                              })), stub), pv.text),
                   sig: sig,
                   code: case loose of {
                       true -> "T4004";
                       false -> ""
                   },
                   why: case loose of {
                       true -> "it receives in more than one place, or goes on in another function: a message that no clause of the receive it waits in takes is dropped, where the source language keeps it for a later receive (selective receive needs a save queue, which is not written yet; app design 5.5)";
                       false -> ""
                   },
                   at: start, decl: "" };
        true -> {
            g: $STOPPED$ <- first_gap(pv.text);
            at: { file: string, line: int64, column: int64 } <- place(f.head.file, f.code.locations, f.code.nodes, g.node, f.code.clauses);
            case length_bytes(dv) == 0 of {
                true -> refused(sig, g.code, concat(why_text(g), "; no stub can be written, because the printer has no value of its result type"), at);
                false -> { ok: false, stub: true, exports: exports, text: stub, sig: sig, code: g.code, why: why_text(g), at: at, decl: "" }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn typed_function(f: $FUNCTION$, ps: $LI$, r: int64, d: string) -> $PRINTED$ {
    arity: int64 <- count(ps, 0);
    sig: string <- ts_text@concat3(f.head.name, "/", ts_text@itoa(f.head.arity));
    plist: string <- params_text(f.types, ps, 0, "", d);
    rtype: string <- type_text(f.types, r, false, d);
    start: { file: string, line: int64, column: int64 } <- place(f.head.file, f.code.locations, f.code.nodes, 0 - 1, f.code.clauses);
    c: $CTX$ <- { ns: f.code.nodes, ts: f.types, hs: f.notes.hints, os: f.notes.overrides, d: d, f: ts_text@concat3(f.head.name, "_", ts_text@itoa(f.head.arity)) };
    case arity == f.head.arity and arity <= 8 of {
        false -> case arity == f.head.arity of {
            false -> refused(sig, "T3103", concat(ts_text@concat4("the (:t_fun) of its signature hint has ", ts_text@itoa(arity), " parameters and the function has the arity ", ts_text@itoa(f.head.arity)), " (contract T8.10 a)"), start);
            true -> refused(sig, "T4002", "it has more than eight parameters (Silica's limit; packing them is not built)", start)
        };
        true -> case bad(plist) of {
            true -> refused(sig, first_gap(plist).code, concat("no stub can be written, because its signature cannot be: ", why_text(first_gap(plist))), start);
            false -> case receives(f.code.nodes, 0) > 0 of {
                // a process's value goes to nobody, so its result type need not be one this printer can write
                true -> process_function(f, c, ps, plist, rtype, start);
                false -> case bad(rtype) of {
                    true -> refused(sig, first_gap(rtype).code, concat("no stub can be written, because its signature cannot be: ", why_text(first_gap(rtype))), start);
                    false -> plain_function(f, c, ps, plist, rtype, start)
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn function_source(f: $FUNCTION$, d: string) -> $PRINTED$ {
    hint: int64 <- hint_index(f.notes.hints, 0 - 1);
    sig: string <- ts_text@concat3(f.head.name, "/", ts_text@itoa(f.head.arity));
    start: { file: string, line: int64, column: int64 } <- place(f.head.file, f.code.locations, f.code.nodes, 0 - 1, f.code.clauses);
    case length_bytes(printed_name(f.head.name)) > 0 of {
        false -> refused(sig, "T4002", ts_text@concat3("the function name ", f.head.name, " is not printed: it is not an identifier (letters, digits and _), or it starts with to_silica_ (contract T9.11); no stub can be written without a name"), start);
        true -> case hint < 0 of {
            true -> refused(sig, "T3101", "the function has no type hint on its signature (node -1; contract T8.10 a): the sender must state its parameter and result types; the transpiler infers no type, the untyped representation is not built, and no stub can be written without a signature", start);
            false -> case type_at(f.types, hint) of {
                (:t_fun, ps: $LI$, r: int64) -> typed_function(f, ps, r, d);
                _: $TYPENODE$ -> refused(sig, "T3103", "the hint on its signature (node -1) is not a (:t_fun) type (contract T8.10 a)", start)
            }
        }
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ a node declaration (contract T9.17)
// The files of a node program in BEAM mode, which BEES reads (compiler guide N1, B1b): the manifest (`<unit>.wire`) and
// `bees.config`. node_text answers "<manifest>\x1d<config>"; the transpile actor writes the two files. A name for a
// message is the message's tag followed by its fields: the wire type is the tuple (atom, F1, ..., Fn), which is the
// tagged tuple the unit's processes send and receive (contract T9.12), as BEES's manifest line states it.

fn wire_type(fields: $LS$) -> string {
    case fields of {
        []: $LS$ -> "atom";
        [_f: string, _t: $LS$] -> concat("(atom", concat(wire_fields(fields), ")"))
    }
}

fn wire_fields(fields: $LS$) -> string {
    case fields of {
        []: $LS$ -> "";
        [f: string, t: $LS$] -> ts_text@concat3(", ", f, wire_fields(t))
    }
}

fn peer_lines(ps: $NODEPEERS$, epmd_port: int64) -> string {
    case ps of {
        []: $NODEPEERS$ -> "";
        [p: $NODEPEER$, t: $NODEPEERS$] -> concat(ts_text@concat4(
            ts_text@concat4("peer ", p.name, " ", p.host),
            " ",
            ts_text@itoa(case p.port == 0 of { true -> epmd_port; false -> p.port }),
            case p.role == :dial of { true -> " dial\n"; false -> " listen\n" }), peer_lines(t, epmd_port))
    }
}

fn remote_lines(rs: $NODEREMOTES$) -> string {
    case rs of {
        []: $NODEREMOTES$ -> "";
        [r: $NODEREMOTE$, t: $NODEREMOTES$] -> concat(ts_text@concat4(ts_text@concat4("remote ", r.name, " @ ", r.peer), " cast ", wire_type(r.fields), "\n"), remote_lines(t))
    }
}

fn local_lines(ls: $NODELOCALS$) -> string {
    case ls of {
        []: $NODELOCALS$ -> "";
        [l: $NODELOCAL$, t: $NODELOCALS$] -> concat(ts_text@concat4("local ", l.name, " cast ", wire_type(l.fields)), concat("\n", local_lines(t)))
    }
}

fn config_peers(ps: $NODEPEERS$, first: boolean) -> string {
    case ps of {
        []: $NODEPEERS$ -> "";
        [p: $NODEPEER$, t: $NODEPEERS$] -> concat(ts_text@concat4(
            case first of { true -> "\n            "; false -> ",\n            " },
            ts_text@concat4("{\"", p.name, "\", [{host, \"", p.host),
            ts_text@concat3("\"}, {port, ", case p.port == 0 of { true -> "epmd"; false -> ts_text@itoa(p.port) }, "}, {role, "),
            case p.role == :dial of { true -> "dial}]}"; false -> "listen}]}" }), config_peers(t, false))
    }
}

fn has_dial(ps: $NODEPEERS$) -> boolean {
    case ps of {
        []: $NODEPEERS$ -> false;
        [p: $NODEPEER$, t: $NODEPEERS$] -> case p.role == :dial of { true -> true; false -> has_dial(t) }
    }
}

// BEES has no default for redial (N2c): a node with a dial-role peer states it, a node without one must not.
// initial_ms 0 is off; otherwise the delays of the redial actor (the first delay, and the most it grows to).
fn redial_text(n: $NODEDECL$) -> string {
    case has_dial(n.tables.peers) of {
        false -> "";
        true -> case n.timing.redial_initial_ms == 0 of {
            true -> ", {redial, false}";
            false -> ts_text@concat4(", {redial, true}, {redial_initial_ms, ", ts_text@itoa(n.timing.redial_initial_ms), "}, {redial_max_ms, ", concat(ts_text@itoa(n.timing.redial_max_ms), "}"))
        }
    }
}

fn manifest_text(n: $NODEDECL$) -> string {
    concat(ts_text@concat4("# to-silica: the manifest of node ", n.name, " (BEAM mode: EPMD). Generated; do not edit.\nnode ", n.name),
           concat(ts_text@concat3("\ncreation ", ts_text@itoa(n.timing.creation), "\n"), concat(peer_lines(n.tables.peers, n.net.epmd_port), concat(remote_lines(n.tables.remotes), local_lines(n.tables.locals)))))
}

fn config_text(n: $NODEDECL$) -> string {
    concat(ts_text@concat4("%% to-silica: bees.config of node ", n.name, " (BEAM mode, cookie, EPMD on port ", ts_text@itoa(n.net.epmd_port)),
        concat(ts_text@concat3("). Generated; do not edit.\n[ {mode, beam},\n  {node, [{name, \"", n.name, "\"}]},\n  {beam, [{transport, tcp}, {auth, cookie}, {cookie_file, \""),
        concat(ts_text@concat4(n.net.cookie_file, "\"}, {listen_address, \"", n.net.listen_address, "\"},\n          {listen_port, "),
        concat(ts_text@concat4(ts_text@itoa(n.net.listen_port), "}, {epmd, external}, {epmd_port, ", ts_text@itoa(n.net.epmd_port), "}, {net_ticktime_s, "),
        concat(ts_text@concat3(ts_text@itoa(n.timing.net_ticktime_s), "}", redial_text(n)), concat(",\n          {peers, [", concat(config_peers(n.tables.peers, true), "]}]} ].\n")))))))
}

fn node_text(n: $NODEDECL$) -> string {
    concat(manifest_text(n), concat("\x1d", config_text(n)))
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ the atoms of a unit (BEES compiler guide A1.2)
// atom_manifest answers the unit's `<unit>.atoms` manifest: every atom spelling the printed Silica writes as a literal,
// one for each line, each once. BEES generates its `bees_atoms` from the manifests of a program's units, so the atoms
// exist at both ends (the printed unit and the BEES units), and its check (tools/bees_config.py check) accepts the
// atoms a manifest lists. Comments and strings are skipped; a `:` is an atom when a letter follows and what precedes
// it is not an identifier character, `:`, `"` or `'` (the rule of BEES's own check).

fn atom_letter(b: int64) -> boolean {
    (b >= 97 and b <= 122) or (b >= 65 and b <= 90) or b == 95
}

fn atom_char(b: int64) -> boolean {
    atom_letter(b) or (b >= 48 and b <= 57)
}

fn atom_end(s: string, i: int64, n: int64) -> int64 {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> n;
        false -> {
            b: int64 <- ts_text@at(s, i);
            case atom_char(b) of {
                true -> atom_end(s, i + 1, n);
                false -> i
            }
        }
    }
}

fn add_atom(acc: string, name: string) -> string {
    case contains(acc, ts_text@concat3("\n", name, "\n")) of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> ts_text@concat3(acc, name, "\n")
    }
}

// mode: 0 code, 1 inside a string, 2 inside a line comment
fn atoms_scan(s: string, i: int64, n: int64, mode: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> {
            b: int64 <- ts_text@at(s, i);
            nb: int64 <- case i + 1 < n of { true -> ts_text@at(s, i + 1); false -> 0 };
            pb: int64 <- case i > 0 of { true -> ts_text@at(s, i - 1); false -> 32 };
            case mode == 1 of {
                true -> case b == 92 of {
                    true -> atoms_scan(s, i + 2, n, 1, acc);
                    false -> atoms_scan(s, i + 1, n, case b == 34 of { true -> 0; false -> 1 }, acc)
                };
                false -> case mode == 2 of {
                    true -> atoms_scan(s, i + 1, n, case b == 10 of { true -> 0; false -> 2 }, acc);
                    false -> case b == 34 of {
                        true -> atoms_scan(s, i + 1, n, 1, acc);
                        false -> case b == 47 and nb == 47 of {
                            true -> atoms_scan(s, i + 2, n, 2, acc);
                            false -> case b == 58 and atom_letter(nb) and not atom_char(pb) and pb != 58 and pb != 34 and pb != 39 of {
                                true -> {
                                    e: int64 <- atom_end(s, i + 1, n);
                                    atoms_scan(s, e, n, 0, add_atom(acc, substring(s, i + 1, e)))
                                };
                                false -> atoms_scan(s, i + 1, n, 0, acc)
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn atom_manifest(text: string) -> string {
    all: string <- atoms_scan(text, 0, length_bytes(text), 0, "\n");
    substring(all, 1, length_bytes(all))
}

// One form's Silica text; see the header for what the answer's fields mean.
// A (:type) form (contract T8.14). Silica has no type names: the declaration is written out wherever a later form
// names it, so what is kept is `decl`, the entry the transpile actor adds to the session's declared types.
fn type_source(t: $TYPEDECL$, d: string) -> $PRINTED$ {
    at: { file: string, line: int64, column: int64 } <- { file: t.head.file, line: t.at_line, column: 0 };
    name: string <- t.head.name;
    itself: string <- decl_entry(name, t.head.params, gap(concat("the declared type ", name), 0 - 1, "T4002", "it names itself, directly or through another declared type; Silica has no type names, so a type is written out at each use and a recursive type cannot be (limitation observed)"));
    text: string <- type_text(t.types, t.root, false, concat("\x07", concat(itself, d)));
    case ts_text@is_identifier(name) of {
        false -> refused("", "T4002", ts_text@concat3("the declared type ", name, " is not kept: its name is not an identifier (letters, digits and _)"), at);
        true -> case bad(text) of {
            true -> { ok: false, stub: false, exports: "", text: "", sig: "", code: first_gap(text).code, why: ts_text@concat4("the declared type ", name, " cannot be written out: ", why_text(first_gap(text))), at: at, decl: decl_entry(name, t.head.params, text) };
            false -> { ok: true, stub: false, exports: "", text: concat(ts_text@concat4("// type ", name, " = ", replace_all(replace_all(text, "\x05", ""), "\x06", "")), "\n"), sig: "", code: "", why: "", at: at, decl: decl_entry(name, t.head.params, text) }
        }
    }
}

// One form's Silica text; see the header for what the answer's fields mean. decls: the session's declared types
// so far (the `decl` of every (:type) form printed before this one, the newest first).
fn form_source(body: $BODY$, decls: string) -> $PRINTED$ {
    case body of {
        (:function, f: $FUNCTION$) -> function_source(f, decls);
        (:type, t: $TYPEDECL$) -> type_source(t, decls);
        (:entry, e: $ENTRY$) -> refused(ts_text@concat3(e.function, "/", ts_text@itoa(e.arity)), "T4002", "the entry point is not printed by form_source: the transpile actor writes main with ts_print@main_source when the entry function is printed", { file: "", line: 0, column: 0 });
        (:node, n: $NODEDECL$) -> refused(n.name, "T4002", "a node declaration is not Silica: the transpile actor writes its manifest and bees.config (contract T9.17)", { file: "", line: 0, column: 0 });
        (:gap, g: $FORMGAP$) -> refused("", "T4001", concat(ts_text@concat4("the sender sent the form as a gap: ", g.construct, " (", g.note), ")"), { file: g.place.file, line: g.place.line, column: 0 })
    }
}

// The helper every failing stub and every failing catch-all calls.
fn gap_helper() -> string {
    "// Called where the source had something to-silica could not translate, or where no clause matched: the\n// division by zero ends the actor (badarith).\nfn to_silica_gap(n: int64) -> int64 {\n    1 / n\n}\n"
}

// to_float (contract T8.12): exact up to 2^53.
fn i2f_helper() -> string {
    "// to_float (contract T8.12): an int64 as the float64 of the same value, exact up to 2^53. Silica has no builtin\n// for it.\nfn to_silica_i2f_pos(n: int64) -> float64 {\n    case n == 0 of { true -> 0.0; false -> case n % 2 == 0 of { true -> 2.0 * to_silica_i2f_pos(n / 2); false -> 2.0 * to_silica_i2f_pos(n / 2) + 1.0 } }\n}\nfn to_silica_i2f(n: int64) -> float64 {\n    case n < 0 of { true -> 0.0 - to_silica_i2f_pos(0 - n); false -> to_silica_i2f_pos(n) }\n}\n"
}

fn f2i_helper() -> string {
    "// trunc (contract T8.12): the integer part of a float64, toward zero. Not defined for a float that is not a\n// number, is infinite or is outside int64.\nfn to_silica_pow2(k: int64) -> int64 {\n    case k == 0 of { true -> 1; false -> 2 * to_silica_pow2(k - 1) }\n}\nfn to_silica_f2i_pos(f: float64) -> int64 {\n    bits: int64 <- float64_bits(f);\n    e: int64 <- (bits / 4503599627370496) % 2048 - 1023;\n    m: int64 <- bits % 4503599627370496 + 4503599627370496;\n    case e < 0 of { true -> 0; false -> case e <= 52 of { true -> m / to_silica_pow2(52 - e); false -> m * to_silica_pow2(e - 52) } }\n}\nfn to_silica_f2i(f: float64) -> int64 {\n    case f < 0.0 of { true -> 0 - to_silica_f2i_pos(0.0 - f); false -> to_silica_f2i_pos(f) }\n}\n"
}

fn round_helper() -> string {
    "// round (contract T8.12): the nearest integer, a half away from zero.\nfn to_silica_round(f: float64) -> int64 {\n    t: int64 <- to_silica_f2i(f);\n    d: float64 <- f - to_silica_i2f(t);\n    case d >= 0.5 of { true -> t + 1; false -> case d <= (0.0 - 0.5) of { true -> t - 1; false -> t } }\n}\n"
}

fn when(needed: boolean, text: string) -> string {
    case needed of {
        true -> concat(text, "\n");
        false -> ""
    }
}

// A Silica print builtin behind a function that declares its effect (contract T9.16).
fn builtin_helper(text: string, name: string) -> string {
    case contains(text, ts_text@concat3("to_silica_b_", name, "(")) of {
        false -> "";
        true -> replace_all(replace_all("// The Silica builtin @N@ (contract T9.16), behind a function that declares its effect.\nfn to_silica_b_@N@(x: @T@) -> atom {\n    sequence proc[device_io]\n        o: atom <- @N@(x)\n    produces pure o end\n}\n\n", "@N@", name), "@T@", builtin_param(name))
    }
}

// The helper functions a unit's text (its printed forms and stubs) calls; the caller writes them into the unit once.
fn helpers_for(text: string) -> string {
    round: boolean <- contains(text, "to_silica_round(");
    concat(concat(ts_text@concat3(builtin_helper(text, "print"), builtin_helper(text, "println"), builtin_helper(text, "print_int64")),
                  concat(builtin_helper(text, "print_float64"), builtin_helper(text, "print_boolean"))),
     concat(concat(ts_text@concat3(when(contains(text, "to_silica_gap("), gap_helper()),
                                  when(round or contains(text, "to_silica_i2f("), i2f_helper()),
                                  when(round or contains(text, "to_silica_f2i("), f2i_helper())),
                  when(round, round_helper())),
           concat(ts_text@concat3(append_helper(text, "int64"), append_helper(text, "float64"), append_helper(text, "boolean")),
                  ts_text@concat3(append_helper(text, "string"), append_helper(text, "atom"), append_helper(text, "actor_ref")))))
}

// `++` for lists of the element type e (contract Appendix B): Silica has no list append, and a function cannot be
// generic, so there is one helper for each element type a unit appends.
fn append_helper(text: string, e: string) -> string {
    case contains(text, ts_text@concat3("to_silica_append_", e, "(")) of {
        false -> "";
        true -> replace_all("// ++ for lists of @E@ (contract Appendix B).\nfn to_silica_append_@E@_none() -> List[@E@, mem(normal)] {\n    sequence proc[mem(normal)]\n        l: List[@E@, mem(normal)] <- empty[@E@, mem(normal)]()\n    produces pure l end\n}\nfn to_silica_append_@E@_push(x: @E@, l: List[@E@, mem(normal)]) -> List[@E@, mem(normal)] {\n    sequence proc[mem(normal)]\n        o: List[@E@, mem(normal)] <- prepend[@E@, mem(normal)](x, l)\n    produces pure o end\n}\nfn to_silica_append_@E@_onto(xs: List[@E@, mem(normal)], acc: List[@E@, mem(normal)]) -> List[@E@, mem(normal)] {\n    case xs of {\n        []: List[@E@, mem(normal)] -> acc;\n        [x: @E@, t: List[@E@, mem(normal)]] -> to_silica_append_@E@_onto(t, to_silica_append_@E@_push(x, acc))\n    }\n}\nfn to_silica_append_@E@(a: List[@E@, mem(normal)], b: List[@E@, mem(normal)]) -> List[@E@, mem(normal)] {\n    to_silica_append_@E@_onto(to_silica_append_@E@_onto(a, to_silica_append_@E@_none()), b)\n}\n\n", "@E@", e)
    }
}


// Silica's entry point around the entry function `function`, which takes no arguments and whose printed result
// type is result_type: it calls the function and returns 0. "" when the function's name cannot be printed (this
// includes an entry function named main: it would be Silica's main itself) or result_type is empty.
// PROVISIONAL: contract T9.6 also asks for BEES's failure reporter and root supervisor; no process is printed yet.
fn main_source(function: string, result_type: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(printed_name(function)) > 0 and length_bytes(result_type) > 0 of {
        false -> "";
        true -> concat(ts_text@concat4("fn main() -> int64 {\n    _: ", result_type, " <- ", printed_name(function)), "();\n    0\n}\n")
    }
}
// ------------------------------------------------------------------ the unit (app design 5.5, 6.5)

fn has_sig(sigs: string, sig: string) -> boolean {
    contains(sigs, ts_text@concat3("\x02", sig, "\x03"))
}

// The printed result type of the function sig ("name/arity") of the unit, from the transpile actor's list of
// what it has written ("\x02name/arity\x03result type\x04" each); "" when the unit has no such function.
fn sig_result(sigs: string, sig: string) -> string {
    key: string <- ts_text@concat3("\x02", sig, "\x03");
    case contains(sigs, key) of {
        false -> "";
        true -> until(sigs, ts_text@find(sigs, key, 0) + length_bytes(key), "\x04")
    }
}

// Every distinct line of text that starts with key (which begins with "\n"), without the key, each followed by
// sep, after acc.
fn marked_from(text: string, key: string, i: int64, acc: string, sep: string) -> string {
    a: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, key, i);
    case a < 0 of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> {
            s: int64 <- a + length_bytes(key);
            e: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\n", s);
            item: string <- concat(substring(text, s, e), sep);
            case contains(acc, item) of {
                true -> marked_from(text, key, e, acc, sep);
                false -> marked_from(text, key, e, concat(acc, item), sep)
            }
        }
    }
}

// The tail calls of text (the marks \x15 ... \x17) written out; all is the whole unit, which says which
// functions it has in tail mode.
fn resolve_tails(all: string, text: string) -> string {
    case contains(text, "\x15") of {
        false -> text;
        true -> {
            a: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\x15", 0);
            b: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\x16", a);
            c: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\x16", b + 1);
            d: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\x16", c + 1);
            e: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\x17", d);
            key: string <- substring(text, a + 1, b);
            args: string <- substring(text, c + 1, d);
            rty: string <- substring(text, d + 1, e);
            with: string <- case contains(all, concat("\n", marker("proc", key))) of {
                true -> concat(ts_text@concat4("to_silica_e_", key, "(", with_k(args)), ")");
                false -> case length_bytes(rty) == 0 of {
                    true -> concat(ts_text@concat3("{ _: int64 <- to_silica_gap(0); ", done_state(), " }"), hoist(ts_text@concat3("// to-silica: NOTE a process goes on in the function ", key, " (name_arity), which this unit does not have as a process function, and the call's result type is not stated (a hint on the (:call), contract T8.10 d): the process fails there\n")));
                    false -> ending(concat(ts_text@concat4(substring(text, b + 1, c), "(", args, ")"), ""), rty)
                }
            };
            concat(concat(substring(text, 0, a), with), resolve_tails(all, substring(text, e + 1, length_bytes(text))))
        }
    }
}

fn tail_s(xs: $LS$) -> $LS$ {
    case xs of {
        []: $LS$ -> none_of();
        [_x: string, t: $LS$] -> t
    }
}

// "p0: T0, p1: T1" for the types ts.
fn typed_list(ts: $LS$, prefix: string, k: int64) -> string {
    case ts of {
        []: $LS$ -> "";
        [t: string, rest: $LS$] -> {
            item: string <- ts_text@concat4(prefix, ts_text@itoa(k), ": ", t);
            more: string <- typed_list(rest, prefix, k + 1);
            case length_bytes(more) == 0 of {
                true -> item;
                false -> ts_text@concat3(item, ", ", more)
            }
        }
    }
}

// A spawned function (or the entry) that the unit does not have in tail mode: the process calls it as an
// ordinary function and ends with its value. line: "f_n<TAB>f/n<TAB>printed name<TAB>the start phase".
fn wrapper_for(line: string, sigs: string) -> string {
    parts: $LS$ <- split_top(line, 9);
    key: string <- nth_s(parts, 0);
    sig: string <- nth_s(parts, 1);
    n: int64 <- ts_text@atoi(substring(sig, ts_text@find(sig, "/", 0) + 1, length_bytes(sig)));
    types: $LS$ <- case n == 0 of {
        true -> none_of();
        false -> tail_s(tuple_elems(nth_s(parts, 3)))
    };
    rty: string <- sig_result(sigs, sig);
    known: boolean <- has_sig(sigs, sig) and length_bytes(rty) > 0 and not contains(rty, "\x13") and not contains(rty, "to_silica_");
    concat(concat(case known of {
                      true -> "";
                      false -> ts_text@concat3("// to-silica: NOTE the function ", sig, " is spawned as a process (or is the entry point) and this unit has no function of that name and arity that can be called: the process fails when it starts\n")
                  },
                  concat(concat(marker("proc", key), marker("ph", nth_s(parts, 3))), marker("arm", start_arm(key, typed_list(types, "a", 0), name_list("a", 0, n))))),
           concat(concat(ts_text@concat4("fn to_silica_e_", key, "(", with_comma(typed_list(types, "p", 0))), ts_text@concat4("k: ", ktype(), ") -> ", smode())),
                  ts_text@concat3(" {\n    ", case known of {
                      true -> ending(concat(ts_text@concat4(nth_s(parts, 2), "(", name_list("p", 0, n), ")"), ""), rty);
                      false -> ts_text@concat3("{ _: int64 <- to_silica_gap(0); ", done_state(), " }")
                  }, "\n}\n")))
}

fn spawn_wrappers(all: string, i: int64, sigs: string, done: string) -> string {
    key: string <- "\n//@to_silica spawn\t";
    a: int64 <- ts_text@find(all, key, i);
    case a < 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            s: int64 <- a + length_bytes(key);
            e: int64 <- ts_text@find(all, "\n", s);
            line: string <- substring(all, s, e);
            name: string <- until(line, 0, "\t");
            case contains(all, concat("\n", marker("proc", name))) or contains(done, ts_text@concat3("\t", name, "\t")) of {
                true -> spawn_wrappers(all, e, sigs, done);
                false -> concat(wrapper_for(line, sigs), spawn_wrappers(all, e, sigs, ts_text@concat3(done, name, "\t")))
            }
        }
    }
}

fn id_arms(uname: string, i: int64, stop: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    case i >= stop of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> id_arms(uname, i + 1, stop, concat(acc, concat(ts_text@concat4("        ", ts_text@itoa(i), " -> :", uname), ts_text@concat3("_p", ts_text@itoa(i), ";\n"))))
    }
}

fn id_chunks(uname: string, chunk: int64, pool: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    case chunk * 256 >= pool of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> {
            stop: int64 <- case (chunk + 1) * 256 < pool of {
                true -> (chunk + 1) * 256;
                false -> pool
            };
            id_chunks(uname, chunk + 1, pool, concat(acc, concat(ts_text@concat3("fn to_silica_id_", ts_text@itoa(chunk), "(i: int64) -> atom {\n    case i of {\n"),
                                                                 concat(id_arms(uname, chunk * 256, stop, ""), "        _: int64 -> :id_pool_exhausted\n    }\n}\n"))))
        }
    }
}

fn id_dispatch(chunk: int64, pool: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    case chunk * 256 >= pool of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> id_dispatch(chunk + 1, pool, concat(acc, concat(ts_text@concat4("        ", ts_text@itoa(chunk), " -> to_silica_id_", ts_text@itoa(chunk)), "(i);\n")))
    }
}

// The child ids of the unit's pool (BEES A4.2): atoms <unit>_p0 ..., in functions of at most 256 arms (BEES A6.5).
fn ids_text(uname: string, pool: int64) -> string {
    concat(id_chunks(uname, 0, pool, ""),
           ts_text@concat3("fn to_silica_id(i: int64) -> atom {\n    case i / 256 of {\n", id_dispatch(0, pool, ""), "        _: int64 -> :id_pool_exhausted\n    }\n}\n"))
}

// The static children of the unit (contract T9.14b), from the marker lines `static<TAB>name<TAB>restart<TAB>
// phase value`: the rows of the supervisor's init, and the test of to_silica_is_static. A marker that is written
// twice (the node stands in two places) is one child; two different children of one name are both written (not
// checked: the supervisor then refuses the second id when it starts).
fn static_rows(lines: string, i: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    e: int64 <- ts_text@find(lines, "\n", i);
    case e < 0 of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> {
            l: string <- substring(lines, i, e);
            a: int64 <- ts_text@find(l, "\t", 0);
            b: int64 <- ts_text@find(l, "\t", a + 1);
            row: string <- concat(ts_text@concat4("{ id: :", substring(l, 0, a), ", agent_type: :worker, initial_state: { ph: ", substring(l, b + 1, length_bytes(l))),
                                  ts_text@concat3(", k: { wait: 0, up: actor_ref_of_word(0) } }, behavior: to_silica_actor, restart: :", substring(l, a + 1, b), ", shutdown: 0, flavor: :plain, state_policy: state_policy(:keep_state_area) }"));
            static_rows(lines, e + 1, case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
                true -> row;
                false -> ts_text@concat3(acc, ", ", row)
            })
        }
    }
}

fn static_ids(lines: string, i: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    e: int64 <- ts_text@find(lines, "\n", i);
    case e < 0 of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> static_ids(lines, e + 1, concat(acc, ts_text@concat3("id == :", substring(lines, i, ts_text@find(lines, "\t", i)), " or ")))
    }
}

fn runtime_template() -> string {
    $PROCESS_RUNTIME$
}

fn main_template() -> string {
    $PROCESS_MAIN$
}

fn option_or(d: string, key: string, otherwise: string) -> string {
    v: string <- option(d, key);
    case ts_text@is_identifier(v) of {
        true -> v;
        false -> otherwise
    }
}

// The pool size the session chose (a4_2 single_pool, pool_size), 1 to 65536; 1024 when it chose none.
fn pool_size(d: string) -> int64 {
    n: int64 <- ts_text@atoi(option(d, "a4_2.pool_size"));
    case n >= 1 and n <= 65536 of {
        true -> n;
        false -> 1024
    }
}

fn reserve(d: string) -> string {
    n: int64 <- ts_text@atoi(option(d, "a3_2.reserve"));
    case n >= 0 of {
        true -> ts_text@itoa(n);
        false -> "0"
    }
}

fn fixed_messages() -> string {
    "(:to_silica_sym, atom) | (:to_silica_go, int64) | (:to_silica_timeout, int64) | (:to_silica_result_int64, int64) | (:to_silica_result_float64, float64) | (:to_silica_result_boolean, boolean) | (:to_silica_result_atom, atom) | (:to_silica_result_string, string)"
}

fn fixed_phases() -> string {
    "(:to_silica_done, int64) | (:to_silica_failed, atom) | (:to_silica_nomatch, int64) | (:to_silica_unstarted, int64) | (:to_silica_exit, int64)"
}

fn child_type() -> string {
    "{ id: atom, agent_type: :worker | :supervisor, initial_state: \x13S\x14, behavior: fn(msg: \x13M\x14, state: \x13S\x14) -> (:no_reply, \x13S\x14), restart: :permanent | :temporary | :transient, shutdown: int64, flavor: :plain | :dangerous, state_policy: state_policy }"
}

fn uses_processes(text: string) -> boolean {
    contains(text, "\x13") or contains(text, "//@to_silica spawn\t") or contains(text, "//@to_silica proc\t") or contains(text, "to_silica_send(") or contains(text, "to_silica_self(") or contains(text, "to_silica_exit(") or contains(text, "to_silica_static(") or contains(text, "to_silica_send_named(")
}

fn settings(text: string, uname: string, d: string) -> string {
    replace_all(replace_all(replace_all(replace_all(replace_all(text, "@UNIT@", uname), "@RESTART@", option_or(d, "a4_4.restart", "transient")),
                                        "@STRATEGY@", option_or(d, "a4_4.strategy", "one_for_one")),
                            "@RELEASE@", option_or(d, "a3_2.release", "release_on_return")),
                "@RESERVE@", reserve(d))
}

// A unit with processes: the marks of its forms are spelled out and the process runtime is written after them.
fn process_unit(silica_unit: string, d: string, exports: string, text: string, sigs: string, entry: string) -> string {
    esig: string <- concat(entry, "/0");
    ename: string <- concat(entry, "_0");
    with_entry: boolean <- length_bytes(entry) > 0 and has_sig(sigs, esig) and length_bytes(printed_name(entry)) > 0;
    t0: string <- concat(ts_text@concat3("\n", text, "\n"), case with_entry of {
        true -> marker("spawn", concat(ts_text@concat4(ename, "\t", esig, "\t"), ts_text@concat3(printed_name(entry), "\t", phase_alt(concat("to_silica_s_", ename), ""))));
        false -> ""
    });
    t1r: string <- resolve_tails(t0, t0);
    t1: string <- concat(inline_of(t1r), hoisted_of(t1r));
    t2: string <- concat(t1, spawn_wrappers(t1, 0, sigs, "\t"));
    msgs: string <- concat(marked_from(t2, "\n//@to_silica msg\t", 0, "", " | "), fixed_messages());
    phs: string <- concat(marked_from(t2, "\n//@to_silica ph\t", 0, "", " | "), fixed_phases());
    pool: int64 <- pool_size(d);
    statics: string <- marked_from(t2, "\n//@to_silica static\t", 0, "", "\n");
    rt: string <- replace_all(replace_all(replace_all(replace_all(replace_all(settings(runtime_template(), silica_unit, d), "@POOL@", ts_text@itoa(pool)),
                                                                  "@STATIC_IDS@", static_ids(statics, 0, "")),
                                                      "@STATIC@", static_rows(statics, 0, "")),
                                          "@ARMS@", marked_from(t2, "\n//@to_silica arm\t", 0, "", ";\n        ")),
                              "@IDS@", ids_text(silica_unit, pool));
    mn: string <- case with_entry of {
        true -> replace_all(settings(main_template(), silica_unit, d), "@ENTRY@", phase_value(concat("to_silica_s_", ename), ""));
        false -> ""
    };
    full: string <- replace_all(replace_all(replace_all(replace_all(concat(concat(concat(t2, rt), mn), concat(plain_call_notes(t2, exports, 0), choice_notes(d))), "\x13C\x14", child_type()),
                                                        "\x13S\x14", ts_text@concat3("{ ph: \x13P\x14, k: ", ktype(), " }")),
                                            "\x13M\x14", msgs),
                                "\x13P\x14", phs);
    concat(concat(ts_text@concat3("use Supervisor;\n\nimpl ", silica_unit, " for Supervisor;\n\n"), ts_text@concat3(exports, "export to_silica_start/0;\n\n", helpers_for(full))), full)
}

fn is_name_byte(b: int64) -> boolean {
    (b >= 97 and b <= 122) or (b >= 65 and b <= 90) or b == 95 or (b >= 48 and b <= 57)
}

// Where text calls the function whose printed name with "(" is key as an ordinary function, at or after i: the
// name stands alone (it is not the end of a longer name) and is not its own definition. -1: nowhere.
fn call_at(text: string, key: string, i: int64) -> int64 {
    a: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, key, i);
    case a < 3 of {
        true -> 0 - 1;
        false -> case is_name_byte(byte_in(text, a - 1)) or substring(text, a - 3, a) == "fn " of {
            true -> call_at(text, key, a + 1);
            false -> a
        }
    }
}

// The start of the function definition that holds position a: the last "\nfn " at or before a, or -1.
fn fn_start(text: string, a: int64, i: int64, last: int64) -> int64 {
    n: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\nfn ", i);
    case n < 0 or n > a of {
        true -> last;
        false -> fn_start(text, a, n + 1, n)
    }
}

fn last_arrow(h: string, i: int64, last: int64) -> int64 {
    n: int64 <- ts_text@find(h, ") -> ", i);
    case n < 0 of {
        true -> last;
        false -> last_arrow(h, n + 1, n)
    }
}

// text with the function that holds position a made a failing stub (its head stays, its body fails), or "" when
// that cannot be done (no value of its result type can be written). A printed function is its head line, one
// body line and a closing line.
fn stub_caller(text: string, a: int64) -> string {
    s: int64 <- fn_start(text, a, 0, 0 - 1);
    hb: int64 <- case s < 0 of {
        true -> 0 - 1;
        false -> ts_text@find(text, " {\n", s)
    };
    e: int64 <- case hb < 0 of {
        true -> 0 - 1;
        false -> ts_text@find(text, "\n}\n", hb)
    };
    case e < 0 or a < hb or a > e of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            header: string <- substring(text, s, hb);
            r: int64 <- last_arrow(header, 0, 0 - 1);
            dv: string <- case r < 0 of {
                true -> "";
                false -> default_value(substring(header, r + 5, length_bytes(header)))
            };
            case length_bytes(dv) == 0 of {
                true -> "";
                false -> concat(concat(substring(text, 0, hb), ts_text@concat3(" {\n    _: int64 <- to_silica_gap(0);\n    ", dv, "")), substring(text, e, length_bytes(text)))
            }
        }
    }
}

// Every function of text that calls key (a printed name and "(") is made a failing stub, with a NOTE line each.
fn stub_callers(text: string, key: string, who: string, tries: int64) -> string {
    a: int64 <- call_at(text, key, 0);
    case a < 0 or tries > 64 of {
        true -> text;
        false -> {
            t: string <- stub_caller(text, a);
            case length_bytes(t) == 0 of {
                true -> concat(text, ts_text@concat3("// to-silica: NOTE a function of this unit calls ", who, ", which this unit does not have as an ordinary function (nothing of it was written, or it is a process function with no stub: its own diagnostic or comment says why), and no stub can stand for the caller: the unit does not compile\n"));
                false -> stub_callers(concat(t, ts_text@concat3("// to-silica: NOTE a function of this unit calls ", who, ", which this unit does not have as an ordinary function (nothing of it was written, or it is a process function with no stub: its own diagnostic or comment says why): the caller is written as a failing stub\n")), key, who, tries + 1)
            }
        }
    }
}

// The transpile actor marks each form of which nothing was written ("//@to_silica missing<TAB>name"), and the
// printer each process function under whose name no stub can stand ("//@to_silica nostub<TAB>name"). A function
// of the unit that calls such a name as an ordinary function, when the unit has no function of that name (sigs;
// "" for the nostub marks, whose functions are in sigs), would name a function that does not exist: it is made
// a failing stub.
fn fix_missing(text: string, key: string, sigs: string, i: int64) -> string {
    a: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, key, i);
    case a < 0 of {
        true -> text;
        false -> {
            s: int64 <- a + length_bytes(key);
            e: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\n", s);
            name: string <- substring(text, s, e);
            case length_bytes(printed_name(name)) == 0 or contains(sigs, ts_text@concat3("\x02", name, "/")) of {
                true -> fix_missing(text, key, sigs, e);
                false -> fix_missing(stub_callers(text, concat(printed_name(name), "("), name, 0), key, sigs, e)
            }
        }
    }
}

// One NOTE line for each process function (a function that receives) that the unit also calls as an ordinary
// function: such a call compiles (the function's stub) and fails when it is reached.
// The name of the function whose definition holds position a ("" when none).
fn holder_name(text: string, a: int64) -> string {
    s: int64 <- fn_start(text, a, 0, 0 - 1);
    p: int64 <- case s < 0 of {
        true -> 0 - 1;
        false -> ts_text@find(text, "(", s)
    };
    case p < 0 or p > a of {
        true -> "";
        false -> substring(text, s + 4, p)
    }
}

// Is every ordinary call of the function `name` (key is name followed by "(") dead code: it stands in the
// ordinary version of a function that is not exported and that is itself called as an ordinary function only
// from such code? A function with a tail call is written twice, as an ordinary function and in tail mode
// (plain_function); when it is a piece of a process that only processes go on in, its ordinary version is never
// reached, and its tail call of a process function is no call anybody makes. depth: how far the chain is followed.
fn only_dead_calls(text: string, exports: string, name: string, i: int64, depth: int64) -> boolean {
    a: int64 <- call_at(text, concat(name, "("), i);
    case a < 0 of {
        true -> true;
        false -> {
            h: string <- holder_name(text, a);
            case h == name of {
                true -> only_dead_calls(text, exports, name, a + 1, depth);
                false -> case length_bytes(h) == 0 or depth <= 0 or starts_with(h, "to_silica_") or contains(exports, ts_text@concat3("export ", h, "/")) of {
                    true -> false;
                    false -> only_dead_calls(text, exports, h, 0, depth - 1) and only_dead_calls(text, exports, name, a + 1, depth)
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn plain_call_notes(text: string, exports: string, i: int64) -> string {
    key: string <- "\n//@to_silica receives\t";
    a: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, key, i);
    case a < 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            s: int64 <- a + length_bytes(key);
            e: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\n", s);
            line: string <- substring(text, s, e);
            sig: string <- until(line, 0, "\t");
            name: string <- substring(line, length_bytes(sig) + 1, length_bytes(line));
            concat(case only_dead_calls(text, exports, name, 0, 6) of {
                       false -> ts_text@concat3("// to-silica: NOTE the function ", sig, " receives, so it runs only as a process (spawned, as the entry, or called in tail position by a function that runs as a process), and this unit also calls it as an ordinary function: that call fails when it is reached\n");
                       true -> ""
                   },
                   plain_call_notes(text, exports, e))
        }
    }
}

fn choice_note(needed: boolean, text: string) -> string {
    case needed of {
        true -> ts_text@concat3("// to-silica: CHOICE ", text, "\n");
        false -> ""
    }
}

fn is_one_of(v: string, a: string, b: string) -> boolean {
    length_bytes(v) == 0 or v == a or v == b
}

// The session's lowering choices (contract 7.2) that the process runtime does not follow, one line each
// (contract T7.5: a T2001 diagnostic names each).
fn choice_notes(d: string) -> string {
    concat(concat(ts_text@concat3(choice_note(not is_one_of(option(d, "a3_3"), "phase_field", "not_applicable"), ts_text@concat3("a3_3 ", option(d, "a3_3"), " is not implemented: a receive is lowered as phase_field (the waiting phase and its live variables are the actor's state)")),
                                  choice_note(not is_one_of(option(d, "a3_4"), "none", "none"), ts_text@concat3("a3_4 ", option(d, "a3_4"), " is not implemented: no yield point is written (a function that loops without receiving runs in one dispatch)")),
                                  choice_note(not is_one_of(option(d, "a4_2"), "single_pool", "single_pool"), ts_text@concat3("a4_2 ", option(d, "a4_2"), " is not implemented: the processes of a unit are the children of one supervisor with one pool of child ids (single_pool)"))),
                  ts_text@concat3(choice_note(not is_one_of(option(d, "a4_3"), "uniform_shape", "uniform_shape"), ts_text@concat3("a4_3 ", option(d, "a4_3"), " is not implemented: every process of a unit is one actor shape (uniform_shape)")),
                                  choice_note(not is_one_of(option(d, "a5_4"), "accept_sender_death", "not_applicable"), ts_text@concat3("a5_4 ", option(d, "a5_4"), " is not implemented: a send is Silica's cast, and a send to a process that has ended ends the sender (accept_sender_death)")),
                                  choice_note(length_bytes(option(d, "a3_2")) > 0, ts_text@concat3("a3_2 ", option(d, "a3_2"), " is followed for the supervisor, the spawner and the report sink only: a child's specification carries no stack policy (limitation observed), so a process has Silica's default stack reserve")))),
           "")
}

fn plain_main(sigs: string, entry: string) -> string {
    sig: string <- concat(entry, "/0");
    case length_bytes(entry) > 0 and has_sig(sigs, sig) of {
        false -> "";
        true -> main_source(entry, sig_result(sigs, sig))
    }
}

// Everything of a unit's file after its `module` line. exports, text: the export lines and the texts of its
// printed forms; sigs: what the transpile actor has written ("\x02name/arity\x03result type\x04" each); entry:
// the session's entry function when it is in this unit, else ""; d: the session's context and declared types.
// main is written when the entry function was written here with no parameters (the text then holds
// "\nfn main() -> int64 {").
fn unit_rest(silica_unit: string, d: string, exports: string, text: string, sigs: string, entry: string) -> string {
    fixed0: string <- case contains(text, "//@to_silica missing\t") of {
        true -> fix_missing(concat("\n", text), "\n//@to_silica missing\t", sigs, 0);
        false -> text
    };
    fixed: string <- case contains(fixed0, "//@to_silica nostub\t") of {
        true -> fix_missing(concat("\n", fixed0), "\n//@to_silica nostub\t", "", 0);
        false -> fixed0
    };
    case uses_processes(fixed) of {
        true -> process_unit(silica_unit, d, exports, fixed, sigs, entry);
        false -> {
            body: string <- concat(fixed, plain_main(sigs, entry));
            concat(ts_text@concat3(exports, "\n", helpers_for(body)), body)
        }
    }
}

fn notes_from(text: string, key: string, i: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    a: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, key, i);
    case a < 0 of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> {
            e: int64 <- ts_text@find(text, "\n", a + 1);
            notes_from(text, key, e, case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of {
                true -> substring(text, a + length_bytes(key), e);
                false -> ts_text@concat3(acc, "; ", substring(text, a + length_bytes(key), e))
            })
        }
    }
}

// What unit_rest found that concerns the whole unit, from the comment lines it wrote into the unit's text, or "".
// kind "NOTE": something of the unit fails when it is reached (T4002, a gap). kind "CHOICE": a lowering choice of
// the session that the unit's process runtime does not follow (T2001, contract T7.5).
fn unit_notes(text: string, kind: string) -> string {
    key: string <- ts_text@concat3("\n// to-silica: ", kind, " ");
    case contains(text, key) of {
        false -> "";
        true -> notes_from(text, key, 0, "")
    }
}

